        {
          "text": "streets of nineveh",
          "offset": 3566,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3568,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "when the assyrian empire finally fell by",
          "offset": 3570,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "around 615 bc",
          "offset": 3573,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "59:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "many of the kingdoms of the levant",
          "offset": 3575,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "59:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "including those of phoenicia",
          "offset": 3578,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "59:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "were able to rule themselves",
          "offset": 3579,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "independently for a time",
          "offset": 3581,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "59:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "until the rise of the next empire",
          "offset": 3584,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "59:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "one which inherited much of the",
          "offset": 3592,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "infrastructure left behind by assyria",
          "offset": 3594,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "59:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "that of the neo-babylonians",
          "offset": 3597,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "59:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "which in 585 bc under the king",
          "offset": 3600,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "60:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "nebuchadnezzar easily began conquering",
          "offset": 3604,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "much of the region",
          "offset": 3606,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "with the exception of tyre which held",
          "offset": 3608,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "60:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "out",
          "offset": 3611,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "60:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "for over a decade until it too was",
          "offset": 3612,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "finally forced",
          "offset": 3614,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "to submit though on relatively favorable",
          "offset": 3616,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "60:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "terms",
          "offset": 3619,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "60:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "by around 540 bc the final",
          "offset": 3623,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "60:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "vast near eastern empire of the ancient",
          "offset": 3626,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "world",
          "offset": 3629,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "60:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "that of the persian achaemenids under",
          "offset": 3630,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "cyrus the great",
          "offset": 3632,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "acquired phoenicia as one of its many",
          "offset": 3634,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "possessions",
          "offset": 3636,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3638,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "for the most part the persians allowed",
          "offset": 3641,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "60:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "the phoenicians",
          "offset": 3644,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "60:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "to run their own day-to-day affairs as",
          "offset": 3645,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "they wished",
          "offset": 3647,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "60:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "as long as they paid their taxes and",
          "offset": 3648,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "allowed the persian forces to make use",
          "offset": 3650,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "of their extensive navies",
          "offset": 3653,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "60:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "which they did on several occasions",
          "offset": 3655,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "60:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "including during their massive invasion",
          "offset": 3658,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "60:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "of greece",
          "offset": 3661,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "61:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "in 480 bc",
          "offset": 3661,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3664,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "61:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "the exception to this was during the",
          "offset": 3666,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "61:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "reign of cyrus's son",
          "offset": 3668,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "cambises ii according to herodotus",
          "offset": 3670,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "61:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "cambises wanted to launch a campaign",
          "offset": 3674,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "against the carthaginians",
          "offset": 3677,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "but the phoenicians especially the",
          "offset": 3680,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "61:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "sailors from tyre",
          "offset": 3682,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "refused due mostly to the fact",
          "offset": 3683,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "that their ancestors had been amongst",
          "offset": 3687,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "61:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "the founders of carthage",
          "offset": 3689,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "61:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "and links between the two cities",
          "offset": 3691,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "61:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "remained strong",
          "offset": 3693,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "61:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "it's also during the years of persian",
          "offset": 3700,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "61:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "rule",
          "offset": 3702,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "61:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "as well as afterward that many greek",
          "offset": 3703,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "61:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "writers",
          "offset": 3706,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "61:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "and historians took an especially keen",
          "offset": 3706,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "61:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "interest in the phoenicians",
          "offset": 3709,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "61:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "though homer mentions them in the iliad",
          "offset": 3713,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "herodotus is the first major writer to",
          "offset": 3716,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "extensively comment on them",
          "offset": 3719,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "61:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "and give substantial details about their",
          "offset": 3720,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "62:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "culture and customs",
          "offset": 3723,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "62:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "also crediting them for introducing the",
          "offset": 3726,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "alphabetic script",
          "offset": 3729,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "to the greek speaking world in his",
          "offset": 3730,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "monumental work",
          "offset": 3733,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "62:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "the histories he writes the following",
          "offset": 3734,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "so these phoenicians including the",
          "offset": 3740,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "gefraeians came with cadmos and settled",
          "offset": 3742,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "this land",
          "offset": 3744,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "62:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "and they transmitted much lore to the",
          "offset": 3745,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "helenes and in particular taught them",
          "offset": 3747,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "62:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "the alphabet",
          "offset": 3749,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "62:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "which i believe the helene's did not",
          "offset": 3750,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "have previously but which was originally",
          "offset": 3752,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "62:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "used",
          "offset": 3754,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "by all phoenicians with the passage of",
          "offset": 3754,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "62:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "time both the sound and the shape of the",
          "offset": 3758,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "62:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "letters changed",
          "offset": 3760,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "62:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "because at this time it was mostly",
          "offset": 3761,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "ionians who lived around the phoenicians",
          "offset": 3762,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "they were the ones who were first",
          "offset": 3765,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "62:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "instructed in the use of the alphabet by",
          "offset": 3766,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "62:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "offset": 3768,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "62:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "and after making a few changes to the",
          "offset": 3769,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "62:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "form of the letters they put them to",
          "offset": 3770,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "62:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "good use",
          "offset": 3772,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "62:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "but when they spoke of them they called",
          "offset": 3773,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "them phoenician letters",
          "offset": 3774,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "which was only right since these letters",
          "offset": 3776,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "had been introduced to helus",
          "offset": 3779,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "62:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "by phoenicians",
          "offset": 3781,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "63:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "in reality the phoenicians may not have",
          "offset": 3788,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "actually invented the alphabet",
          "offset": 3790,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "which scholars now believe may have been",
          "offset": 3792,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "developed by other canaanite peoples in",
          "offset": 3794,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "63:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "egypt or the levant sometime during the",
          "offset": 3796,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "63:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "middle or late bronze age",
          "offset": 3799,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "63:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "they're also being a related script from",
          "offset": 3802,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "south arabia",
          "offset": 3804,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "63:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "probably born through mercantile",
          "offset": 3805,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "connections",
          "offset": 3807,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "however it seems that the phoenicians",
          "offset": 3809,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "were among the first peoples to both",
          "offset": 3811,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "63:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "utilize",
          "offset": 3813,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "and spread the use of alphabetic writing",
          "offset": 3814,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "throughout the mediterranean",
          "offset": 3817,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "63:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "and beyond",
          "offset": 3819,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "63:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "in 343 bc the cities of tyre",
          "offset": 3824,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "and arwad revolted against the persian",
          "offset": 3827,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "63:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "king",
          "offset": 3830,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "artaxerxes iii but this rebellion was",
          "offset": 3831,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "soon crushed",
          "offset": 3834,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "other than this though phoenicia",
          "offset": 3836,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "remained relatively calm",
          "offset": 3838,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "63:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "and stable during its nearly two",
          "offset": 3840,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "centuries of persian rule",
          "offset": 3842,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "64:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "until in 332 alexander of macedon",
          "offset": 3844,
          "duration": 10,
          "formattedTime": "64:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "came to the levant",
          "offset": 3848,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "64:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "alexander's arrival and subsequent",
          "offset": 3854,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "64:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "conquest of phoenicia",
          "offset": 3856,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "64:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "marked the beginning of the gradual",
          "offset": 3858,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "64:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "hellenization",
          "offset": 3860,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the region after his death in 323",
          "offset": 3861,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "64:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "phoenicia was hotly contested amongst",
          "offset": 3866,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "64:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "his successors",
          "offset": 3868,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "64:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "but eventually the region found itself",
          "offset": 3870,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "64:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "within the confines",
          "offset": 3873,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "64:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the greek celia sid empire",
          "offset": 3874,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "64:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "ruled by one of alexander's generals",
          "offset": 3877,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "64:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "gradually greek language culture",
          "offset": 3882,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "architecture and religion began to",
          "offset": 3885,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "64:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "permeate",
          "offset": 3888,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "64:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "every aspect of phoenician life",
          "offset": 3889,
          "duration": 10,
          "formattedTime": "64:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "the age of the phoenicians was over",
          "offset": 3896,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "64:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "the hellenistic age had begun",
          "offset": 3899,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "64:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "in neighboring judea the culture of the",
          "offset": 3905,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "65:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "jews",
          "offset": 3908,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "65:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "survived albeit with a hellenistic",
          "offset": 3908,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "65:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "influence",
          "offset": 3911,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "65:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "in phoenicia however it wasn't to be the",
          "offset": 3913,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "65:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "case",
          "offset": 3916,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "65:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "like vikings in the early middle ages",
          "offset": 3920,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "65:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "the phoenicians",
          "offset": 3923,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "65:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "being victims of their own success",
          "offset": 3924,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "65:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "merging with the peoples they came into",
          "offset": 3927,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "65:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "contact with",
          "offset": 3929,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "65:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "their culture gradually disappearing",
          "offset": 3931,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "65:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "in some respects however all peoples of",
          "offset": 3937,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "65:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "the mediterranean sea",
          "offset": 3940,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "65:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "are phoenicians",
          "offset": 3942,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "65:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "despite the new world that was forming",
          "offset": 3948,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "65:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "around them",
          "offset": 3950,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "65:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "one aspect of the phoenicians that",
          "offset": 3951,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "65:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "changed little was their mastery",
          "offset": 3952,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:52"
        },
