          "formattedTime": "05:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "the birth of kingship, power, and ever",
          "offset": 327,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "05:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "larger political organizations.",
          "offset": 331,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "05:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "To the west of the moore, sheltered by",
          "offset": 338,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "05:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "the steep hills of Cumbria, enclosed by",
          "offset": 341,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "05:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "the windswept Irish Sea, sits the green,",
          "offset": 344,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "05:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "fertile valley of the River Eden.",
          "offset": 348,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "05:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 351,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "05:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "Once home to a kingdom truly worthy of",
          "offset": 353,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "05:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "that title, a last hold out of the old",
          "offset": 356,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "05:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "world. This wasn't Anglo-Saxon and it",
          "offset": 359,
          "duration": 10,
          "formattedTime": "05:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "wasn't really Roman either, but British.",
          "offset": 363,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "06:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "The massive land wall built by the",
          "offset": 374,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "06:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Emperor Hadrien in the 2n century AD",
          "offset": 377,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "06:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "across the entirety of northern Britain",
          "offset": 380,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "06:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "is perhaps the most visible remnant of",
          "offset": 382,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "06:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Roman world left here today.",
          "offset": 385,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "06:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "But a city on its western edge lingers",
          "offset": 389,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "06:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "on too.",
          "offset": 392,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "06:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "Once home to a city council able to",
          "offset": 396,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "06:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "dictate its own affairs. Today we know",
          "offset": 398,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "06:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "the place as Carlilele.",
          "offset": 402,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "06:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "And there's a good argument for this",
          "offset": 405,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "06:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "being the last city in Roman Britain.",
          "offset": 407,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "06:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "For people continued to live here long",
          "offset": 411,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "06:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "after the Western Empire collapsed.",
          "offset": 414,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "06:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "Not only that, but several fortresses",
          "offset": 419,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "06:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "along the wall show signs of continued",
          "offset": 421,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "07:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "occupation, too. At Housesteads,",
          "offset": 424,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "07:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Vinderlander, and Bird Oswald, to name a",
          "offset": 428,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "07:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "few.",
          "offset": 431,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "07:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "But did these people see themselves as",
          "offset": 435,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "07:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Romans?",
          "offset": 437,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "07:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Maybe. But just as likely is their",
          "offset": 439,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "07:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "re-mbbracing of their own pre- Roman",
          "offset": 442,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "07:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Brethonic culture.",
          "offset": 446,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "07:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Further south from Carlilele, Brethonic",
          "offset": 452,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "07:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "place names like Penri still hark back",
          "offset": 455,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "07:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "to that time.",
          "offset": 458,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "07:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Celtic holdouts turning to old customs",
          "offset": 461,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "07:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "for survival.",
          "offset": 464,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "07:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "for the kingdom in question which once",
          "offset": 468,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "07:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "ruled in these parts",
          "offset": 470,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "07:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "and perhaps stretching north into",
          "offset": 472,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "07:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Galloway to the north, the Penines to",
          "offset": 475,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "07:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "the south as a British name, too. Sung",
          "offset": 477,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "07:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "in songs for hundreds of years all the",
          "offset": 482,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "08:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "way down to today.",
          "offset": 485,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "08:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "We know it as Reggath,",
          "offset": 488,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "08:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "forged in the fires and chaos of the",
          "offset": 491,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "08:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "fifth century. Their ancestors had been",
          "offset": 494,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "08:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "here long before the Romans had come.",
          "offset": 496,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "08:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Their descendants would long outlive the",
          "offset": 500,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "08:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "empire.",
          "offset": 503,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "08:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Little remains of that ancient kingdom",
          "offset": 508,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "08:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "now. A scattering of hill forts, a",
          "offset": 511,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "08:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "handful of inscriptions and place names.",
          "offset": 514,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "08:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Britons leave scant little trace in",
          "offset": 519,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "08:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "the archaeological record.",
          "offset": 522,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "08:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "But according to many scholars, this was",
          "offset": 525,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "08:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "one of the most important of those",
          "offset": 529,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "08:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "British polities to emerge in the",
          "offset": 531,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "08:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "aftermath of Rome.",
          "offset": 534,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "08:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "Arguably the most important of the",
          "offset": 539,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "08:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Henth,",
          "offset": 542,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "09:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Old North, just one of a plethora of",
          "offset": 544,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "09:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "rival kingdoms that arose in the wake of",
          "offset": 548,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "09:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Roman withdrawal.",
          "offset": 551,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "09:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "At some like Gdin in modernday Lotheian,",
          "offset": 555,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "09:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "we see older tribal identities",
          "offset": 558,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "09:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "reemerging.",
          "offset": 561,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "09:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "At others, like old Clute and perhaps",
          "offset": 563,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "09:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Regath, they are entirely new.",
          "offset": 566,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "09:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Renegotiations of old tribal identities",
          "offset": 570,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "09:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "faced with the uncertainty of a new",
          "offset": 573,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "09:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "world.",
          "offset": 576,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "09:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "Today, the hen ogle is largely forgotten",
          "offset": 584,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "09:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "in England. For the most part, no",
          "offset": 587,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "09:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "museums or monuments can be found on the",
          "offset": 590,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "09:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "landscape.",
          "offset": 592,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "09:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet, the Old North lives on in a",
          "offset": 595,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "09:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "rich corpus of stories spanning 1,500",
          "offset": 598,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "09:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "years, passed on one generation to the",
          "offset": 602,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "10:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "next.",
          "offset": 606,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "10:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tales like that of Yurion, Reggath's",
          "offset": 608,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "10:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "most famous king. Praised in Bardic",
          "offset": 612,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "10:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "tradition as a smiter of the Anglians in",
          "offset": 615,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "10:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "many battles,",
          "offset": 618,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "10:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "champion of Britain and part inspiration",
          "offset": 620,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "10:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "for the Arthur legend.",
          "offset": 624,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "10:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "though his is just one example of a vast",
          "offset": 631,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "10:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "array of stories that miraculously",
          "offset": 635,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "10:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "survive to the present. Some of the",
          "offset": 638,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "10:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "oldest in all of Europe.",
          "offset": 640,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "10:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 644,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "10:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "For though the years 400 to 600 are some",
          "offset": 646,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "10:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the least documented in British",
          "offset": 649,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "10:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "history in Wales more information can be",
          "offset": 651,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "10:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "found than the previous or next two",
          "offset": 656,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "10:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "centuries.",
          "offset": 659,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "10:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "For them it's the age of heroes.",
          "offset": 661,
          "duration": 15,
          "formattedTime": "11:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 665,
          "duration": 11,
          "formattedTime": "11:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "When the Gallow Roman historian Gregory",
          "offset": 676,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "11:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "of To wrote his lorded history of the",
          "offset": 679,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "11:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Franks in the latter sixth century, an",
          "offset": 682,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "11:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "ambitious attempt to record the history",
          "offset": 685,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "11:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the Germanic barbarians who now held",
          "offset": 687,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "11:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "sway in what was once Gaul.",
          "offset": 690,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "11:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "He describes a class of Gallow Roman",
          "offset": 694,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "11:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "bishops and aristocrats still holding",
          "offset": 697,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "11:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "positions of high influence, lands,",
          "offset": 699,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "11:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "titles, and political power within the",
          "offset": 702,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "11:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "Frankish administration,",
          "offset": 705,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "11:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "still living in many of the Roman cities",
          "offset": 707,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "11:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "and continuing to use their",
          "offset": 710,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "11:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "institutions.",
          "offset": 712,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "11:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "When the venerable bead wrote his",
          "offset": 721,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "12:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "history in the 8th century, the first",
          "offset": 723,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "12:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "real attempt at an objective telling of",
          "offset": 726,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "12:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "events for centuries,",
          "offset": 729,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "12:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is no trace of anything of the",
          "offset": 731,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "12:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "sort.",
          "offset": 734,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "12:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just battles and bloodshed and violence",
          "offset": 735,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "12:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "between two diametrically opposed",
          "offset": 740,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "12:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "peoples.",
          "offset": 742,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "12:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 744,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "12:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "The situation in Britain seems to have",
          "offset": 747,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "12:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "been particularly warlike and resentful.",
          "offset": 750,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "12:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Bitter emnity felt by people speaking",
          "offset": 754,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "12:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "different languages and of a different",
          "offset": 757,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "12:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "custom.",
          "offset": 760,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "12:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 762,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "12:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "Eventually the Gallow Romans would",
          "offset": 765,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "12:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "influence the already Christian Franks",
          "offset": 768,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "12:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "so much they would stop using their own",
          "offset": 770,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "12:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "language. integrating into the",
          "offset": 773,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "12:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "population. For French is a romance",
          "offset": 776,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "12:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "language.",
          "offset": 779,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "12:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "In Britain, it would be different. In",
          "offset": 783,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "13:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Anglo-Saxon areas, their pagan ways",
          "offset": 786,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "13:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "of life and language would dominate.",
          "offset": 790,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "13:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "but in the west where ancestry from the",
          "offset": 797,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "13:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "old north would become a badge of honor",
          "offset": 799,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "13:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "for later Welsh dynasties",
          "offset": 802,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "13:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "forming an overarching backdrop to the",
          "offset": 804,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "13:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "struggle between Saxon and Britain. The",
          "offset": 807,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "13:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "British language, Brethonic, well on the",
          "offset": 810,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "13:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "way to becoming Welsh, would become the",
          "offset": 814,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "13:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "primary language, replacing the Latin",
          "offset": 816,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "13:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Irish that had made inroads, too.",
          "offset": 819,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "13:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "In centuries to come, Britain's and",
          "offset": 826,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "13:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "English would define themselves against",
          "offset": 829,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "13:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "each other and would continue to do so",
          "offset": 832,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "13:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "into modern times.",
          "offset": 835,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "13:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "And in the mid6th century, amidst all",
          "offset": 841,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "14:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "the bloodshed and the warfare,",
          "offset": 845,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "14:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "something else happened too.",
          "offset": 848,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "14:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Famine,",
          "offset": 851,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "14:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "drought,",
          "offset": 853,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "snow in midsummer.",
          "offset": 855,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "And in 536",
          "offset": 858,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the far off Eastern Roman Empire,",
          "offset": 860,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "14:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "still surviving half of the imperial",
          "offset": 863,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "majesty that was Rome.",
          "offset": 866,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Still linked to Britain by desperate",
          "offset": 868,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "trade seen in the archaeological record",
          "offset": 871,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "14:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "at places like Tintagel in Cornwall. The",
          "offset": 873,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "14:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "historian Precopius talks of the sun",
          "offset": 877,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "14:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "going dim for months on end.",
          "offset": 880,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "14:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "It's a strange tale in an otherwise",
          "offset": 885,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "14:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "completely rational and reliable account",
          "offset": 888,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "14:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "by this wellrespected court historian.",
          "offset": 892,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "14:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "Part of the emperor Justinian's inner",
          "offset": 895,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "circle.",
          "offset": 897,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "14:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet today, modern science",
          "offset": 901,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "15:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "corroborates the account.",
          "offset": 903,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "15:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "tree ring evidence suggesting a",
          "offset": 906,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "15:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "significant decline in vegetation all",
          "offset": 908,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "15:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "over Eurasia from around 535",
          "offset": 911,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "15:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "all the way until 555.",
          "offset": 915,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "15:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "We don't know exactly what caused it,",
          "offset": 919,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "15:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "but volcanic eruption might be the",
          "offset": 922,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "15:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "culprit. Ash entering the atmosphere,",
          "offset": 924,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "15:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "blocking the sun, causing temperatures",
          "offset": 927,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "15:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "to drop, crops to fail, and people to",
          "offset": 930,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "15:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "die.",
          "offset": 935,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "15:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "a literal dark age.",
          "offset": 937,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "15:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "And then",
          "offset": 940,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "15:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "we have the plague.",
          "offset": 942,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "15:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "In Ireland, the annals of Olter record",
          "offset": 947,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "15:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "the deaths of at least seven important",
          "offset": 950,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "15:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "rulers to disease.",
          "offset": 953,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "15:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "In Britain, it's much the same.",
          "offset": 955,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "15:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "All over Europe in the mid6th century,",
          "offset": 962,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "16:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "it's thought as much as half of the",
          "offset": 966,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "16:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "population met miserable ends to the",
          "offset": 968,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "16:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "very first outbreak of bubonic plague.",
          "offset": 971,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "16:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "At the city of Viriconium, an unusually",
          "offset": 978,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "16:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "wellpreserved post Roman settlement, a",
          "offset": 981,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "complete collapse of the population took",
          "offset": 984,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "16:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "place. The city limits shrinking from 79",
          "offset": 986,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "16:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "to 10 hectares.",
          "offset": 990,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "New wooden structures now overlaying the",
          "offset": 993,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "previous stone foundations.",
          "offset": 996,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "The people here having little connection",
          "offset": 998,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "to those once mighty colonades and still",
          "offset": 1001,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "16:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "visible imperial remnants.",
          "offset": 1003,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "16:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "The intense bleakness of this era, beset",
          "offset": 1008,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "16:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "as it was by plague, famine, and war,",
          "offset": 1011,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "16:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "may well have left such a mark on the",
          "offset": 1016,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "psyche of Britain that it was later",
          "offset": 1018,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "16:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "remembered as the concept of the",
          "offset": 1021,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "17:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "wasteland in medieval literature.",
          "offset": 1023,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "17:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1029,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "17:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is in this post-apocalyptic landscape",
          "offset": 1036,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "17:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "unimaginably terrible conditions",
          "offset": 1040,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "17:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "that the mostly unrecorded struggle",
          "offset": 1044,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "17:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "between Britain and Saxon was waged.",
          "offset": 1046,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "17:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "This is the untold tale of those fawn",
          "offset": 1051,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "17:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdoms.",
          "offset": 1055,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "17:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "War leaders without armies, kings",
          "offset": 1057,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "17:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "without kingdoms.",
          "offset": 1060,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "17:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1062,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "17:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "A tale pieced together bit by bit from",
          "offset": 1064,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "17:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "the depths of time.",
          "offset": 1067,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "17:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "One of the most incredible ever told.",
          "offset": 1070,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "17:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "This is the entire history of the Old",
          "offset": 1073,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "17:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "North.",
          "offset": 1076,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "17:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1078,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "17:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "An epic tale spanning some 300 years",
          "offset": 1081,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "18:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "from the end of Roman Britain to the",
          "offset": 1086,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "18:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "early Middle Ages.",
          "offset": 1088,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "18:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1090,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "18:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "So get yourself comfortable. There's a",
          "offset": 1095,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "18:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "lot to take in.",
          "offset": 1097,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "18:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "From Constantinople to Scotland, I",
          "offset": 1100,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "18:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "traveled all over Europe to film it.",
          "offset": 1103,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "18:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Applause]",
          "offset": 1106,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "18:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1106,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "18:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "It's well over 3 hours long, and it took",
          "offset": 1110,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "18:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "me 3 years to make.",
          "offset": 1113,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "18:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "But first, a quick word from the sponsor",
          "offset": 1119,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "18:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "of this video, a longtime supporter of",
          "offset": 1122,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "18:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "the channel, and one of my favorite",
          "offset": 1124,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "18:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "streaming services on the web. It's",
          "offset": 1126,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "18:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mellant TV. For just a small monthly",
          "offset": 1129,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "18:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "fee, you can find thousands of",
          "offset": 1132,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "18:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "documentaries on practically any subject",
          "offset": 1134,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "18:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "you can think of. History, geography,",
          "offset": 1137,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "18:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "science, culture, and much, much more.",
          "offset": 1140,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "19:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "all streamed directly to your phone,",
          "offset": 1144,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "your tablet, and your smart TV.",
          "offset": 1146,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "19:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "My current recommendation is Justinian,",
          "offset": 1149,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "last of the Romans, and we'll be seeing",
          "offset": 1152,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "19:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "much more of him later, but you can also",
          "offset": 1154,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "19:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "find loads more on Rome, ancient",
          "offset": 1158,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "history, and medieval Britain. All of",
          "offset": 1160,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "19:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "the good stuff.",
          "offset": 1163,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Now, I've teamed up with Mellin to offer",
          "offset": 1166,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "19:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "you an exclusive free trial. Head on",
          "offset": 1168,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "19:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "over to try.magelantv.com/histime",
          "offset": 1172,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "19:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "or click on my link in the description",
          "offset": 1177,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "19:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "below.",
          "offset": 1179,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Now back to antiquity.",
          "offset": 1181,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "19:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1184,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "19:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "By the mid 530s, a well-informed citizen",
          "offset": 1190,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "19:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the Eastern Mediterranean may well",
          "offset": 1194,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "have assumed that a Roman revival was on",
          "offset": 1196,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "19:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "the way.",
          "offset": 1199,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "19:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1201,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "20:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "the restoration of the entire Western",
          "offset": 1203,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "20:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Empire.",
          "offset": 1206,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "20:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "For the Eastern Empire hadn't just",
          "offset": 1210,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "20:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "survived the fifth century calamities",
          "offset": 1212,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "20:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "that beset its Western counterpart.",
          "offset": 1214,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "20:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Safe behind the massive Theodosian",
          "offset": 1217,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "20:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "walls, greatest in the world, built in",
          "offset": 1220,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "20:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "the 440s to keep out the Huns. For",
          "offset": 1223,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "20:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "decades now, it had thrived.",
          "offset": 1227,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "20:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "still firmly holding on to all of its",
          "offset": 1231,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "20:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "immensely rich eastern possessions,",
          "offset": 1233,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "20:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "including Egypt, parts of Mesopotamia,",
          "offset": 1236,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "20:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "and the Levventine shore.",
          "offset": 1239,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "20:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "As the west fell apart piece by piece,",
          "offset": 1244,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "20:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "riven by internal revolt, enthralled to",
          "offset": 1248,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "20:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "the whims of Germanic invaders.",
          "offset": 1251,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "20:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "By the later fifth century, the east",
          "offset": 1254,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "20:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "found itself expertly governed by the",
          "offset": 1257,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "20:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "firm hand of Zeno, head of a sorely",
          "offset": 1260,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "needed militaristic infusion from inside",
          "offset": 1264,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "21:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "the empire in the form of the Asorans,",
          "offset": 1266,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "21:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "fierce mountain people of Anatolia.",
          "offset": 1271,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1274,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 518, after a severe crackdown on",
          "offset": 1277,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "corruption and the pursuit of firm",
          "offset": 1281,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "21:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "defensive policies, Zeno's chosen",
          "offset": 1283,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "successor Anastasius",
          "offset": 1286,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "21:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "was able to leave behind a massive",
          "offset": 1289,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "treasury overflowing with gold,",
          "offset": 1291,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "21:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "23 million solid.",
          "offset": 1295,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "21:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "The stage was set for perhaps the most",
          "offset": 1301,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "momentous reign of any single Roman",
          "offset": 1305,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "emperor.",
          "offset": 1307,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "21:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "Within just 10 years of coming to power,",
          "offset": 1315,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "the domestic achievements of Justinian",
          "offset": 1317,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "were remarkable.",
          "offset": 1320,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "22:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "In 534, a groundbreaking new law code",
          "offset": 1323,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "22:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "was created which would permanently",
          "offset": 1326,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "22:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "alter European society.",
          "offset": 1329,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "22:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "In 537, the Aya Sophia, largest",
          "offset": 1332,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "22:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Christian building ever constructed, was",
          "offset": 1336,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "22:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "built in Constantinople,",
          "offset": 1339,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "22:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "forming the center of Eastern Roman",
          "offset": 1341,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "22:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "society for a thousand years to come.",
          "offset": 1343,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "22:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "This was an age of incredible",
          "offset": 1348,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "22:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "architectural achievement, the very",
          "offset": 1350,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "22:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "pinnacle of Roman development.",
          "offset": 1353,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "22:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "But it was Justinian's foreign policy",
          "offset": 1357,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "22:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "that was really remarkable.",
          "offset": 1359,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "22:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "To the north of the Alps, the Franks,",
          "offset": 1366,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "22:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Catholic allies of a Catholic emperor,",
          "offset": 1370,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "22:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "dominated,",
          "offset": 1372,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "22:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "exacting tribute from all of the",
          "offset": 1374,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "22:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdoms around them, enjoying good",
          "offset": 1376,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "22:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "trade links with the empire and",
          "offset": 1379,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "22:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "fostering ties even further a field in",
          "offset": 1381,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "23:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Scandinavia, Britain, and beyond.",
          "offset": 1384,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "23:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Commerce between east and west boomed.",
          "offset": 1389,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "23:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Finally, things were looking good.",
          "offset": 1393,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "23:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1397,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "23:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "And by the 530s, the Eastern Empire was",
          "offset": 1400,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "23:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "finally strong enough to intervene",
          "offset": 1403,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "23:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "directly in the Germanic West, resting",
          "offset": 1406,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "23:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "back total control of the Mediterranean",
          "offset": 1409,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Seaways,",
          "offset": 1412,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "ending the piracy of the feared Vandals,",
          "offset": 1415,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "23:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "scourge of the seas for a 100red years,",
          "offset": 1418,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "23:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "once and for all.",
          "offset": 1420,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "23:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "On the distant eastern frontier, after 5",
          "offset": 1426,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "23:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "years of brutal warfare, an ambitiously",
          "offset": 1429,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "titled eternal peace had been signed",
          "offset": 1432,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "23:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "with Sassinid Persia in 532,",
          "offset": 1435,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "23:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "allowing Justinian to focus on his real",
          "offset": 1438,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "target,",
          "offset": 1441,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "24:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Africa.",
          "offset": 1443,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "24:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1445,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "24:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Applause]",
          "offset": 1446,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "24:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "seized by the Vandals close to a century",
          "offset": 1448,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "24:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "before.",
          "offset": 1450,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "24:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "Within just two years, the Vandalic",
          "offset": 1453,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "24:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Kingdom was dead. Its last rulers killed",
          "offset": 1455,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "24:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "or sent off to exile on the Persian",
          "offset": 1459,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "24:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "frontier.",
          "offset": 1461,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "24:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "After a century of outside occupation,",
          "offset": 1465,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "24:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "the North African coast, once the bread",
          "offset": 1468,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "24:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "basket of the empire, was back in Roman",
          "offset": 1471,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "24:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "hands.",
          "offset": 1474,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "24:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1475,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "24:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "And by 536, led by one of the greatest",
          "offset": 1479,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "24:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "generals in all of history, Belisarius,",
          "offset": 1483,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "24:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "the mighty city of Rome itself was",
          "offset": 1486,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "24:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "retaken.",
          "offset": 1489,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "24:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "The forces of the Ostrogothic Kingdom",
          "offset": 1494,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "24:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "pushed back behind the fortress walls of",
          "offset": 1496,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "24:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Revena.",
          "offset": 1498,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "24:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Whether the now well-integrated citizens",
          "offset": 1505,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "25:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Rome applauded this victory remains",
          "offset": 1508,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "25:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "unclear,",
          "offset": 1511,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "25:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1512,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "25:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "but a bitterly fought reconquest of the",
          "offset": 1513,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "25:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Italian mainland ensued,",
          "offset": 1516,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "25:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "ultimately leading to the slow death of",
          "offset": 1519,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "25:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Ostrogoths as a people.",
          "offset": 1522,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "25:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1525,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "25:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "The fact that the kingdom had been",
          "offset": 1529,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "25:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "largely peaceful with Latin speakers and",
          "offset": 1531,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "25:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Romans holding positions of power and",
          "offset": 1534,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "25:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "influence throughout all echelons of",
          "offset": 1536,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "25:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "society didn't matter to Justinian.",
          "offset": 1538,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "25:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1542,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "25:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nor the fact that they'd been Christian",
          "offset": 1544,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "25:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "for decades and largely left Roman",
          "offset": 1546,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "25:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "society intact, fostering great works of",
          "offset": 1549,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "25:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "art and literacy.",
          "offset": 1553,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "25:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "As far as he was concerned, they were",
          "offset": 1555,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "25:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "barbarians.",
          "offset": 1557,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "25:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "If they resisted, all were put to the",
          "offset": 1559,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "25:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "sword.",
          "offset": 1562,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "26:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "And that's when things started to go",
          "offset": 1566,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "26:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "wrong.",
          "offset": 1569,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "26:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1570,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though often lorded as the greatest of",
          "offset": 1573,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "26:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "all emperors,",
          "offset": 1576,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "26:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "overseer of a remarkable change of",
          "offset": 1578,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "26:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "fortunes,",
          "offset": 1581,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "the change was to be short-lived.",
          "offset": 1582,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "26:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "And stranger accounts of Justinian exist",
          "offset": 1587,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "too.",
          "offset": 1589,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "26:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "At the very beginning of his reign,",
          "offset": 1593,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "26:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "Justinian had ordered the massacre of",
          "offset": 1595,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "26:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "tens of thousands of his own people",
          "offset": 1598,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "26:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "during the Nico riots.",
          "offset": 1600,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "26:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "And he never fully shook off the",
          "offset": 1602,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "26:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "reputation as an oppressor.",
          "offset": 1604,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "26:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the strange secret history written by",
          "offset": 1608,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "court historian Precopius, Justinian",
          "offset": 1611,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "roams the halls of his palace at night,",
          "offset": 1614,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "ever restless, demonic even, able to",
          "offset": 1617,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "26:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "detach his head from his body and float",
          "offset": 1621,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "around.",
          "offset": 1624,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "He was a restless figure for sure. Being",
          "offset": 1626,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "in charge of the most powerful state in",
          "offset": 1629,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "27:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "the world must do that to a person.",
          "offset": 1631,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "27:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "Then in 535,",
          "offset": 1635,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "writing from the newly conquered",
          "offset": 1638,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "metropolis of Carthage in Precopius's",
          "offset": 1640,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "public history, an especially",
          "offset": 1643,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "27:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "wellrespected source at the very heart",
          "offset": 1645,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the imperial power structure that we",
          "offset": 1647,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "27:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "hear of an especially unusual event",
          "offset": 1650,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "27:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "during this year. A most dread portant",
          "offset": 1657,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "took place. The sun gave forth its light",
          "offset": 1659,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "27:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "without brightness, like the moon during",
          "offset": 1662,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "27:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "the whole year, and it seemed",
          "offset": 1665,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "exceedingly like the sun in eclipse, for",
          "offset": 1666,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "27:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "the beams it shed were not clear, nor",
          "offset": 1669,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "27:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "such as it is accustomed to shed.",
          "offset": 1672,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "The similarly lorded contemporary writer",
          "offset": 1677,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "27:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cassiodoris,",
          "offset": 1680,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "author of a now lost multi-part epic on",
          "offset": 1681,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "28:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "the history of the Goths, speaks of a",
          "offset": 1684,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "28:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "similar event.",
          "offset": 1687,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "28:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "And it's not just in the Roman world",
          "offset": 1691,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "28:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "that we hear of this dimming of the sun.",
          "offset": 1693,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "28:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Writing much later, but using his own",
          "offset": 1697,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "28:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "independent sources, the venerable bead",
          "offset": 1700,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "28:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "talks of solar eclipses in 538 and 540,",
          "offset": 1703,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "28:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "though of course his dates are slightly",
          "offset": 1708,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "28:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "off.",
          "offset": 1710,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "28:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "So too, Michael the Syrian",
          "offset": 1714,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "28:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "Today, using modern science, this",
          "offset": 1721,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "28:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "unusual solar activity can actually be",
          "offset": 1724,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "28:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "seen in tree ring records.",
          "offset": 1726,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "28:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the 1980s, Mike Bailey, a leading",
          "offset": 1732,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "28:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "expert on dendo chronology, spotted",
          "offset": 1735,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "28:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "unusually slow tree growth in Western",
          "offset": 1737,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "28:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Europe and Scandinavia between 536 and",
          "offset": 1740,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "28:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "545.",
          "offset": 1743,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "29:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "leading to many scholars referring to",
          "offset": 1747,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "29:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "535 and 536 as the year without sun.",
          "offset": 1749,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "29:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "In Ireland, a failure of bread was",
          "offset": 1758,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "recorded in 538.",
          "offset": 1760,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "29:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "In Britain, heavy snowfall and distress",
          "offset": 1764,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "29:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "among men. its worst weather in a",
          "offset": 1767,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "29:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "century.",
          "offset": 1771,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "29:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Snow even fell in the Euphrates River",
          "offset": 1775,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "29:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "Valley.",
          "offset": 1778,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "29:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Crops failing throughout Italy and",
          "offset": 1780,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "southern Iraq.",
          "offset": 1783,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "In Arabia, there was famine followed by",
          "offset": 1786,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "29:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "flood.",
          "offset": 1789,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "29:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1790,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "And remarkably, this seems to have been",
          "offset": 1793,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "a global event.",
          "offset": 1795,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "29:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "In China, a major drought was recorded",
          "offset": 1800,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "30:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "where yellow dust rained down like snow",
          "offset": 1803,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "30:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1807,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "30:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "and actual snow fell in the following",
          "offset": 1811,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "30:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "August, ruining the crops.",
          "offset": 1814,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "30:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1818,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "In Japan, the emperor announced that",
          "offset": 1821,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "30:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "money cannot cure hunger.",
          "offset": 1824,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "30:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1827,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "30:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "On the other side of the world, the",
          "offset": 1837,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "30:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "colossal city of Teayoti Wakan, greatest",
          "offset": 1839,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "30:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Americas had ever seen, collapsed",
          "offset": 1843,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "30:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "for unknown reasons.",
          "offset": 1847,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "30:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "and similar collapses can be seen all",
          "offset": 1854,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "over the continent.",
          "offset": 1857,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ice cores from the Andes tell us that",
          "offset": 1859,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "severe idity descended on the Mochce",
          "offset": 1862,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "31:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "civilization of north coastal Peru",
          "offset": 1864,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "31:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "and drought is well documented in North",
          "offset": 1868,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "31:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "America.",
          "offset": 1871,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "31:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "All over the world, climatic record",
          "offset": 1875,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "31:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "suggests that the climate was awful in",
          "offset": 1878,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "31:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "535 for 5 years and then took decades to",
          "offset": 1881,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "31:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "recover.",
          "offset": 1886,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "31:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1889,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "31:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 554 in Ireland, things were still",
          "offset": 1892,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "31:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "notably bad. And similar reports are",
          "offset": 1896,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "31:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "found all over Eurasia.",
          "offset": 1900,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "31:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Today we know that in the mid6th century",
          "offset": 1903,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "31:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "something did happen. It can be seen in",
          "offset": 1907,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "31:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "the climatological record as well as the",
          "offset": 1910,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "31:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "contemporary sources.",
          "offset": 1913,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "31:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Given the wealth of evidence, numerous",
          "offset": 1918,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "31:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "writers have even gone so far to suggest",
          "offset": 1921,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "32:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "the sixth century to be the single most",
          "offset": 1923,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "32:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "abrupt climatic occurrence of the last",
          "offset": 1926,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "two millennia.",
          "offset": 1929,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "32:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "But what caused the problem?",
          "offset": 1932,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Well, it's unclear.",
          "offset": 1935,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "32:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "There was no scientific method back",
          "offset": 1938,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "32:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "then, and no one bore witness to the",
          "offset": 1940,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "actual cause of the event,",
          "offset": 1943,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "32:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "just the repercussions.",
          "offset": 1946,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "32:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "A giant asteroid, perhaps a comet",
          "offset": 1951,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "32:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "colliding with the Earth.",
          "offset": 1954,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Such a thing has been seen before with",
          "offset": 1957,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Tongaska event of 1908,",
          "offset": 1960,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "which flattened some 80 million Siberian",
          "offset": 1963,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "32:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "trees over an area well over 2,000 km,",
          "offset": 1966,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "altering the carbon content of the",
          "offset": 1973,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "atmosphere in the process.",
          "offset": 1975,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "32:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1979,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "32:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "The most likely scenario, however, is",
          "offset": 1986,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "33:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "one we humans know all too well.",
          "offset": 1989,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "33:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 1994,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "33:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "In 1816,",
          "offset": 1998,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "33:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "a massive volcanic eruption in Indonesia",
          "offset": 2000,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "33:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "caused so much material to be pushed",
          "offset": 2004,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "33:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "upwards into the atmosphere that the",
          "offset": 2006,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "33:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "effects were felt as far away as",
          "offset": 2008,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "33:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain.",
          "offset": 2010,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "33:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2012,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "33:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "This so-called year without summer is",
          "offset": 2015,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "33:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "just one recent example of the volcanic",
          "offset": 2019,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "33:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "power of the earth.",
          "offset": 2021,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "33:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "A similarly devastating eruption of",
          "offset": 2026,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "33:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "Heckler in Iceland in around 1,000 BC",
          "offset": 2028,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "33:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "could have caused a similarly",
          "offset": 2032,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "33:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "worldchanging climatic event.",
          "offset": 2033,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "33:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "But where was this volcano?",
          "offset": 2039,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "33:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "We can't be sure, but one candidate is",
          "offset": 2043,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "34:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Elchon in Chiapas, Mexico.",
          "offset": 2046,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "34:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Another is the ring of fire, the long",
          "offset": 2050,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "34:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "chain of volcanoes between Samoa and",
          "offset": 2054,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "34:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Somatra in the Pacific and Southeast",
          "offset": 2056,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "34:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Asia, homeland of the Polynesians making",
          "offset": 2058,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "34:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "tracks out into the wide Pacific.",
          "offset": 2062,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "34:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Whatever the cause for it, the",
          "offset": 2070,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "34:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "scientific evidence suggests a dramatic",
          "offset": 2071,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "34:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "slowing of tree growth. An apocalyptic",
          "offset": 2074,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "34:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "image",
          "offset": 2077,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "34:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "of a mysterious dry fog rolling over the",
          "offset": 2079,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "34:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "land, sending the world into darkness",
          "offset": 2083,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "34:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "for a year.",
          "offset": 2086,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "34:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Colder temperatures, crop failures,",
          "offset": 2089,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "34:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "drought.",
          "offset": 2092,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "34:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "People",
          "offset": 2094,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "34:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "might have feared whether the sun would",
          "offset": 2098,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "34:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "ever shine again.",
          "offset": 2100,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "34:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "And then just when the Romans might have",
          "offset": 2105,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "35:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "thought that things were getting back to",
          "offset": 2108,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "35:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "normal",
          "offset": 2110,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "35:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "once the abundant harvests of the",
          "offset": 2112,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "35:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "previous years had been consumed",
          "offset": 2114,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "35:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "and perhaps one of the worst strokes of",
          "offset": 2116,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "35:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "luck ever seen in history,",
          "offset": 2119,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "35:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "bubonic plague arrived in",
          "offset": 2122,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "35:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Constantinople.",
          "offset": 2125,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "35:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2129,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "35:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "An entirely new disease developed from",
          "offset": 2133,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "35:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "close human interaction with domestic",
          "offset": 2137,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "35:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "animals",
          "offset": 2139,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "35:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "which no one had any immunity to.",
          "offset": 2141,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "35:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2148,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "35:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "A ticking time bomb ever since the",
          "offset": 2150,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "35:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "domestication of animals some 10,000",
          "offset": 2152,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "35:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "years before.",
          "offset": 2155,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "35:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "What followed was by far the worst",
          "offset": 2159,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "35:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "epidemic the world had ever seen.",
          "offset": 2162,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "36:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Not even the emperor was safe.",
          "offset": 2166,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "36:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2170,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "36:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "Seeming to originate at the Egyptian",
          "offset": 2175,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "port city of Alexandria",
          "offset": 2177,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "where it had arrived from who knows",
          "offset": 2180,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "36:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "where, possibly Eurasia or Africa.",
          "offset": 2182,
          "duration": 10,
          "formattedTime": "36:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "The disease spread far and wide.",
          "offset": 2187,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alexandria was one of the greatest port",
          "offset": 2194,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "cities in the Eastern Mediterranean with",
          "offset": 2196,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "36:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "links all over the known world. By 542,",
          "offset": 2199,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "36:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "the plague arrived in the capital.",
          "offset": 2204,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "36:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2207,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "36:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "The sixth century church historian",
          "offset": 2211,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ivagrias describes what happened next in",
          "offset": 2213,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "36:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "grim detail.",
          "offset": 2216,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "36:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Great puss boobos developing on",
          "offset": 2220,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "orififices,",
          "offset": 2223,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "37:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "faces swelling, eyes bloody.",
          "offset": 2225,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "37:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2230,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "Those stricken often lost their minds",
          "offset": 2232,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "37:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "entirely before the end.",
          "offset": 2235,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2238,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "And even if one recovered, the disease",
          "offset": 2240,
          "duration": 10,
          "formattedTime": "37:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "would strike again and again and again.",
          "offset": 2243,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "37:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Another eyewitness, John of Ephesus,",
          "offset": 2250,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "37:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "wrote that homes suddenly became tombs,",
          "offset": 2253,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "37:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "masters and servants alike, dying in",
          "offset": 2257,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "37:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "droves.",
          "offset": 2261,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "37:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "With no one left to bury the dead, their",
          "offset": 2264,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "corpses mingled together in their",
          "offset": 2267,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "bedrooms.",
          "offset": 2269,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "37:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "John managed to escape the city only to",
          "offset": 2279,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "find the situation much the same in the",
          "offset": 2281,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "38:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "countryside.",
          "offset": 2284,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "38:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2285,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "38:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Corpses littering roads, festering in",
          "offset": 2288,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "38:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "the sun.",
          "offset": 2291,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "38:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cattle roamed aimlessly with no one to",
          "offset": 2297,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "38:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "tend to them. Fields abundant in grain",
          "offset": 2300,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "38:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "lay until no one left to reap or gather",
          "offset": 2303,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "38:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "the crop.",
          "offset": 2306,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "38:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Even the emperor himself was stricken,",
          "offset": 2311,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "38:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "laying low with particularly nasty booos",
          "offset": 2314,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "38:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "on his armpits.",
          "offset": 2317,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "38:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though with the help of the best medical",
          "offset": 2319,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "38:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "care in the world at the time, he",
          "offset": 2322,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "38:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "survived.",
          "offset": 2324,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "38:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ordering colossal mass graves to be",
          "offset": 2327,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "38:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "built. Plague ships overloaded with",
          "offset": 2329,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "38:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "corpses sent again and again to dump the",
          "offset": 2332,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "38:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "bodies into the Black Sea.",
          "offset": 2336,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "38:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2339,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "38:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "All in all, more than 50% of the city's",
          "offset": 2344,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "39:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "population is thought to have died.",
          "offset": 2347,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "39:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2350,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "39:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "And Constantinople had links all over",
          "offset": 2354,
          "duration": 11,
          "formattedTime": "39:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Europe in the east and now the west",
          "offset": 2358,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "39:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "where similar levels of casualties would",
          "offset": 2367,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "39:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "take place.",
          "offset": 2369,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "39:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2370,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "39:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 554, the annals of Olter record the",
          "offset": 2373,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "39:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "plague arriving in Britain.",
          "offset": 2377,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "39:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Across the world, all in all, around 100",
          "offset": 2382,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "39:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "million people are thought to have died.",
          "offset": 2386,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "39:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "And this was just the first of hundreds",
          "offset": 2391,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "39:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "of outbreaks to strike Eurasia again and",
          "offset": 2394,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "39:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "again and again for hundreds of years to",
          "offset": 2398,
          "duration": 10,
          "formattedTime": "39:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "come well into the 8th century.",
          "offset": 2402,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "There's a good argument that this is the",
          "offset": 2408,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "moment the Roman Empire collapsed for",
          "offset": 2411,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "good.",
          "offset": 2413,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "40:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "And as we shall see, things would only",
          "offset": 2415,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "40:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "get worse.",
          "offset": 2419,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "40:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 5:46, given restbite to lick their",
          "offset": 2428,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "40:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "wounds and reform for one last final",
          "offset": 2431,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "40:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "fight for their very way of life, the",
          "offset": 2434,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "40:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ostrogoths were back in full force.",
          "offset": 2437,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "40:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Led by a charismatic new king, Totilla,",
          "offset": 2441,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "40:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rome was sacked after a year-long siege.",
          "offset": 2445,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "40:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "its walls torn down, its people sent",
          "offset": 2448,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "away.",
          "offset": 2452,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2454,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "40:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "For after this third sack in 150 years,",
          "offset": 2457,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "40:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Totilla angrily threatened to now turn",
          "offset": 2461,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "41:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "the place into grazing land for his",
          "offset": 2464,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "41:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "sheep in revenge for the aggressive",
          "offset": 2466,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "41:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "attack on his people.",
          "offset": 2469,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "41:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "But Belisarius isn't remembered as one",
          "offset": 2473,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "41:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the greatest generals in history for",
          "offset": 2476,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "41:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "nothing. And a vicious back and forth",
          "offset": 2478,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "41:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "war followed for years to come with Rome",
          "offset": 2480,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "41:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "changing hands yet again.",
          "offset": 2484,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "41:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2487,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "41:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Within a few decades, yet more Germanic",
          "offset": 2491,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "41:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "warriors would arrive to smash their way",
          "offset": 2493,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "41:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "into the peninsula.",
          "offset": 2495,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "41:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "still pagan and fiercely warlike. These",
          "offset": 2500,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "41:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "were the barbarians that Justinian had",
          "offset": 2503,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "41:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "feared.",
          "offset": 2505,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "41:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet the Lombards were lured south by",
          "offset": 2510,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "41:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "vengeful Eastern Roman diplomacy.",
          "offset": 2514,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "41:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "If they couldn't have Italy, then the",
          "offset": 2517,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "41:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ostrogoths certainly couldn't either.",
          "offset": 2520,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "41:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2524,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "42:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "In Britain too, the advance of the",
          "offset": 2528,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "42:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Germanic settlers began a new heading",
          "offset": 2530,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "42:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "westwards along the tempames into the",
          "offset": 2534,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "42:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "middle borderlands.",
          "offset": 2536,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "42:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Vericonium, Sirencester and other towns",
          "offset": 2537,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "42:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "too falling into Saxon hands",
          "offset": 2541,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "42:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "and particularly in the north with the",
          "offset": 2548,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "42:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "foundation and expansion of a new",
          "offset": 2550,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "42:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdom on the eastern seabboard",
          "offset": 2552,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "42:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "carved out by the Kels of Anglian",
          "offset": 2555,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "42:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "warlords.",
          "offset": 2557,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "42:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "We know it as Bonia and we'll be seeing",
          "offset": 2559,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "42:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "much more of them later.",
          "offset": 2563,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "42:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "But most dangerous of all, far to the",
          "offset": 2575,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "42:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "east, over the vast plains to the north",
          "offset": 2578,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "42:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the Black Sea, Avar step nomads,",
          "offset": 2581,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "43:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "horsemen of the apocalypse made flesh,",
          "offset": 2585,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "continued their westward march.",
          "offset": 2589,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "43:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2591,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "43:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tens of thousands of them.",
          "offset": 2596,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "43:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Once the undisputed rulers of Inner",
          "offset": 2599,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Asia, now refugees,",
          "offset": 2601,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "driving hundreds of thousands of pack",
          "offset": 2605,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "43:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "animals before them to pastures new.",
          "offset": 2607,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "43:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "For the droughts of the 530s hadn't just",
          "offset": 2615,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "hit agricultural areas. They'd extended",
          "offset": 2618,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "far into central Asia, Mongolia, and",
          "offset": 2621,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "Siberia too.",
          "offset": 2624,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "43:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "This vast ocean of grassland, already",
          "offset": 2627,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "marginal at the best of times, in many",
          "offset": 2630,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "43:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "areas, became unlivable,",
          "offset": 2632,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "43:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "setting off a chain of events that would",
          "offset": 2638,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "43:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "lead the Avar horde all the way to the",
          "offset": 2640,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "44:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "walls of Constantinople itself.",
          "offset": 2643,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "44:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "losers in a conflict on the other side",
          "offset": 2652,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "44:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the world. Just as the Huns had done",
          "offset": 2655,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "44:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "before them, and others would do time",
          "offset": 2657,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "44:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "and time again over the centuries to",
          "offset": 2660,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "44:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "come, the Horde moved west,",
          "offset": 2662,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "44:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "skirting around the north shores of the",
          "offset": 2669,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "44:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Caspian Sea, leaving death in their",
          "offset": 2671,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "44:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "wake.",
          "offset": 2673,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "44:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "Eventually, they moved onto the fertile",
          "offset": 2677,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "44:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "grasslands north of the Caucuses and",
          "offset": 2679,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "44:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "from there the Hungarian plane, subduing",
          "offset": 2682,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "44:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "all they came across,",
          "offset": 2686,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "44:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "creating a new empire stretching from",
          "offset": 2691,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "44:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Rine to the Vular,",
          "offset": 2694,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "44:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "from the Baltic to the Balkans.",
          "offset": 2699,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "44:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2704,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "45:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "driving before them entire nations of",
          "offset": 2708,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "45:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Slavic refugees,",
          "offset": 2710,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "45:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2712,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "45:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "permanently altering the patchwork of",
          "offset": 2719,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "45:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "states that would develop in Eastern",
          "offset": 2721,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "45:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Europe",
          "offset": 2723,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "45:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2726,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "45:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "and leading to mass population movements",
          "offset": 2728,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "45:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "into the frontiers of the helpless",
          "offset": 2730,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "45:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Eastern Empire.",
          "offset": 2732,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "45:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "already massively weakened by losing",
          "offset": 2734,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "45:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "half of its tax base to the plague.",
          "offset": 2736,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "45:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "In just a few short decades, the world",
          "offset": 2740,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "45:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "had changed irrevocably.",
          "offset": 2743,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "45:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Western Empire was dead for good,",
          "offset": 2749,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "45:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "and the Eastern hung on by the skin of",
          "offset": 2752,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "45:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "its teeth.",
          "offset": 2755,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "45:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "never again able to interfere as far",
          "offset": 2758,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "45:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "west as it had done under Justinian.",
          "offset": 2761,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "46:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Harassed by constant warfare,",
          "offset": 2766,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "46:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "faced with recurrent plague epidemics,",
          "offset": 2769,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "46:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "civil strife,",
          "offset": 2774,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "46:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "dictatorships,",
          "offset": 2776,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "46:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2777,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "46:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Eastern Empire now very nearly died",
          "offset": 2779,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "46:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "entirely.",
          "offset": 2782,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "46:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2784,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "46:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "By the 570s, the Avar state was one of",
          "offset": 2787,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "46:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "the largest realms Europe had ever",
          "offset": 2790,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "46:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "known.",
          "offset": 2793,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "46:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "When they weren't raiding the empire,",
          "offset": 2796,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "46:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "the elite Avar horse lords and their",
          "offset": 2799,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "46:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Slavic subjects, all resolute pagans,",
          "offset": 2801,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "46:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "extorted it for cash,",
          "offset": 2805,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "46:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "content to exist parasitically from",
          "offset": 2810,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "46:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "massive peace payments.",
          "offset": 2813,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "46:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Year after year, the imperial coffers",
          "offset": 2815,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "46:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "ran a little smaller. The avars got a",
          "offset": 2818,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "46:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "little richer.",
          "offset": 2822,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "47:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Still visible today in immensely",
          "offset": 2826,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "47:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "elaborate burials found all over the",
          "offset": 2828,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "47:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hungarian plane.",
          "offset": 2831,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "47:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the space of just a few decades, from",
          "offset": 2834,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "47:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "the end of Justinian's reign, the",
          "offset": 2837,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "47:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "imperial tax base is thought to have",
          "offset": 2840,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "47:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "shrunk by approximately 60%.",
          "offset": 2842,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "47:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "as a result of Avar and Slavic land",
          "offset": 2846,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "47:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "grabs.",
          "offset": 2849,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "47:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "And then of course the Persians were",
          "offset": 2852,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "47:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "back.",
          "offset": 2856,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "47:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Justinians so-called eternal peace",
          "offset": 2860,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "47:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "lasting just a few decades.",
          "offset": 2863,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "47:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "As the Avars beset the west, besieging",
          "offset": 2868,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "47:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "the great city itself, the Persians took",
          "offset": 2872,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "47:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "the east,",
          "offset": 2875,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "47:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "seizing Mesopotamia, the Levant, even",
          "offset": 2879,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "47:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Christian stronghold of Egypt.",
          "offset": 2883,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "48:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2887,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "48:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "And then in the early 7th century from",
          "offset": 2889,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "48:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "the south this time an entirely new",
          "offset": 2892,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "48:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "force arrived to sweep away all in its",
          "offset": 2895,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "48:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "path. For the Muslims had arrived,",
          "offset": 2899,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "48:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "the mortal enemy of Constantinople for a",
          "offset": 2909,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "48:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "thousand years to come.",
          "offset": 2912,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "48:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "firmly now on the defensive for 400",
          "offset": 2917,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "48:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "years. The east no longer had the luxury",
          "offset": 2920,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "48:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "of direct involvement in the west.",
          "offset": 2923,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "48:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2927,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "48:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "Any post Roman holdouts there were on",
          "offset": 2929,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "48:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "their own.",
          "offset": 2932,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "48:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2938,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "48:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Meanwhile, in Britain,",
          "offset": 2945,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "49:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "long gone were the days when tens of",
          "offset": 2948,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "49:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "thousands of soldiers marched out of",
          "offset": 2951,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "49:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "city gates to war.",
          "offset": 2954,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "49:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "When our martyrs sailed past the great",
          "offset": 2959,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "49:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "sea fortresses of the western headlands,",
          "offset": 2962,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "49:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2964,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "49:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "great construction projects undertaken",
          "offset": 2967,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "49:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "on the orders of the emperor.",
          "offset": 2969,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "49:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "oceans and continents away.",
          "offset": 2973,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "49:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "All that had been a thing of the past",
          "offset": 2978,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "49:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "for more than a hundred years.",
          "offset": 2980,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "49:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 2983,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "49:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "And despite the immense leaps forward in",
          "offset": 2986,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "49:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "our archaeological understanding of this",
          "offset": 2989,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "49:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "era made in recent decades,",
          "offset": 2992,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "49:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "most of what happened still remains",
          "offset": 2994,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "49:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "shrouded in mystery.",
          "offset": 2997,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "49:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just one solitary contemporary source",
          "offset": 3002,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "50:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "survives.",
          "offset": 3006,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "50:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3008,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "50:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "penned by a Romano British monk",
          "offset": 3010,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "50:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "writing in late Roman Latin vernacular",
          "offset": 3014,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "50:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "sometime in the 6th century,",
          "offset": 3017,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "50:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "probably before the plague which swept",
          "offset": 3023,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "50:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "through Europe in the 540s",
          "offset": 3026,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "50:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "and likely not earlier than 500.",
          "offset": 3028,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "50:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though scholarly consensus usually",
          "offset": 3033,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "50:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "places the work towards the end of the",
          "offset": 3036,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "50:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "middle of the 6th century, say the early",
          "offset": 3038,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "50:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "530s.",
          "offset": 3041,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "50:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3043,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "50:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "And that source, it's difficult to",
          "offset": 3046,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "50:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "really understand. It's not a history.",
          "offset": 3049,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "50:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "There aren't any dates.",
          "offset": 3053,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "50:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rather, it's a fiery sermon. The",
          "offset": 3056,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "50:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "writings of an incredibly angry man.",
          "offset": 3059,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "50:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "disgusted by the actions of the waring",
          "offset": 3063,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "51:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "kings of the island.",
          "offset": 3065,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3068,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "And of course, the historical section of",
          "offset": 3071,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "51:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "Gildas is highly unreliable.",
          "offset": 3073,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "He wasn't a historian, nor was he",
          "offset": 3079,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "51:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "particularly concerned with accuracy.",
          "offset": 3081,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "51:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet, as fate would have it, it",
          "offset": 3085,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "51:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "remains the only source we have.",
          "offset": 3087,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "51:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "everything else being lost to time.",
          "offset": 3091,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3098,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "51:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Much of the text is made up of biblical",
          "offset": 3099,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "quotes, and it's not entirely obvious",
          "offset": 3102,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "51:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "when our writer is being truthful and",
          "offset": 3104,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "when he is simply launching scathing",
          "offset": 3107,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "51:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "attacks on people he hates.",
          "offset": 3109,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "51:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet, nonetheless, it does provide an",
          "offset": 3115,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "incredible glimpse into this otherwise",
          "offset": 3118,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "dark period.",
          "offset": 3120,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "52:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3123,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "52:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "And Gildus, he is not happy.",
          "offset": 3124,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "52:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "The work is called Deexidio at Conquest",
          "offset": 3129,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "52:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britannia",
          "offset": 3133,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "52:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "and in English, the language of Gildas'",
          "offset": 3135,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "52:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "enemies",
          "offset": 3137,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "52:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "on the ruin and conquest of Britain.",
          "offset": 3139,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "52:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Divided into three sections, part one",
          "offset": 3147,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "52:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "provides a brief overview of the events",
          "offset": 3150,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "52:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the previous 100 years or so since",
          "offset": 3152,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "52:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Romans pulled out of Britain.",
          "offset": 3155,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "52:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "In fiery language, it speaks of",
          "offset": 3161,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "52:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "devastation by pictish and Scottish",
          "offset": 3163,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "52:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "raiders, Saxons, and Anglian pirates",
          "offset": 3166,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "52:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "ravaging the shorelines of the North",
          "offset": 3170,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "52:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sea.",
          "offset": 3172,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "52:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "The barbarians push us back to the sea.",
          "offset": 3178,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "52:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "The sea pushes us back to the",
          "offset": 3181,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "53:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "barbarians.",
          "offset": 3183,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "53:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Between these two kinds of death, we are",
          "offset": 3185,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "53:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "either drowned or slaughtered.",
          "offset": 3187,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "So dire was the situation that several",
          "offset": 3194,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "appeals for aid were sent to the",
          "offset": 3196,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Imperial Roman court at Ravena. to the",
          "offset": 3199,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "53:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "emperor Onorius and later the magister",
          "offset": 3202,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "53:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "militum Etius Flavius.",
          "offset": 3205,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3207,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "These appeals are now known as the",
          "offset": 3210,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "53:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "groans of the Britons.",
          "offset": 3212,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "53:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "But the collapsing Western Empire had",
          "offset": 3216,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "53:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "its own issues and no help could be",
          "offset": 3218,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "53:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "sent.",
          "offset": 3222,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "53:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "Gildus goes on to describe further",
          "offset": 3225,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "53:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "events.",
          "offset": 3227,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "53:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "A number of the wretched survivors were",
          "offset": 3232,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "53:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "caught in the mountains and butchered",
          "offset": 3234,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "53:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "wholesale.",
          "offset": 3236,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "Others, their spirits broken by hunger,",
          "offset": 3238,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "53:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "went to surrender to the enemy. They",
          "offset": 3240,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "54:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "were forced to be slaves forever. Others",
          "offset": 3243,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "54:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "made for lands beyond the sea.",
          "offset": 3247,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "And many Britons did indeed cross the",
          "offset": 3260,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "54:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "sea, heading to Britany in Gaul, where",
          "offset": 3263,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "54:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "they established new polities,",
          "offset": 3266,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "remaining in contact with their island",
          "offset": 3268,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "54:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "brethren for centuries to come.",
          "offset": 3271,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "And according to Gildas, for a time the",
          "offset": 3276,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "ones that stayed in Britain found",
          "offset": 3279,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "themselves under the sway of a powerful",
          "offset": 3281,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "54:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "ruler, a tyrant who very much in the",
          "offset": 3284,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "54:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Roman imperial tradition, sent for",
          "offset": 3288,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "54:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "military help from the continent.",
          "offset": 3290,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "54:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "A call soon answered by Germanic",
          "offset": 3294,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "54:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "mercenaries.",
          "offset": 3297,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "54:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "The 9th century writer Nennius names",
          "offset": 3302,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "55:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "this British ruler as Lord Vortigern",
          "offset": 3305,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "55:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "bead names the mercenaries",
          "offset": 3309,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "55:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "hangist and horser",
          "offset": 3312,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "55:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "as they say is history's",
          "offset": 3316,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "55:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "incompetent defense of Britain the",
          "offset": 3321,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "55:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "revolt of the Saxons",
          "offset": 3324,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "55:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "and finally by around the year 500 a",
          "offset": 3327,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "55:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "successful Brit British resistance",
          "offset": 3330,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "55:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "organized",
          "offset": 3332,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "55:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "according to Gildas by one Ambrosius",
          "offset": 3334,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "55:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Aurelianis",
          "offset": 3337,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "55:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "descended from Romans.",
          "offset": 3340,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "55:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "According to much later sources, this is",
          "offset": 3344,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "55:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "the age of Arthur.",
          "offset": 3347,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "55:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "By Gildas's day, we're told that there",
          "offset": 3354,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "55:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "has largely been peace for a generation.",
          "offset": 3357,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "55:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "By that time, five great kings ruled the",
          "offset": 3361,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "56:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "southern lands from the river D to",
          "offset": 3364,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "56:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Land's End.",
          "offset": 3367,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "56:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Part two of Gildas' work consists of a",
          "offset": 3371,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "56:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "harsh condemnation of them all.",
          "offset": 3374,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "56:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "As this remains the only contemporary",
          "offset": 3380,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "56:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "information about these rulers, Gildus",
          "offset": 3383,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "56:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "is of particular interest to scholars of",
          "offset": 3385,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "56:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "British history.",
          "offset": 3388,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "56:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "First, we have Constantine of Damnonia,",
          "offset": 3395,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "56:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "the deceitful.",
          "offset": 3398,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "56:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Usually thought to have ruled in",
          "offset": 3400,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "56:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cornwall, where many landmarks are still",
          "offset": 3402,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "56:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "named for him.",
          "offset": 3404,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "56:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Next, we have Aurelius Canonus,",
          "offset": 3410,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "56:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "who we know next to nothing about.",
          "offset": 3413,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "56:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "Then we have Vortiporius, ruler of Divid",
          "offset": 3417,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "56:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "in southern Wales.",
          "offset": 3420,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "57:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Koglazus, probably a sub king ofwed in",
          "offset": 3424,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "57:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "northern Wales.",
          "offset": 3428,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "57:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "And finally, we have Male Gwyn, ruler of",
          "offset": 3431,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Gwen,",
          "offset": 3434,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "the so-called dragon of the island,",
          "offset": 3436,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps referring to his stronghold on",
          "offset": 3439,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "57:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglesy.",
          "offset": 3441,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "57:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3442,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "He receives the most hate of all from",
          "offset": 3445,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Gildas, almost described as a high king",
          "offset": 3447,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "over the others.",
          "offset": 3450,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "57:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "And though the later genealogies of",
          "offset": 3453,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "Gwennneth and heroic poetry place male",
          "offset": 3454,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Gwyn perhaps ruling from his stronghold",
          "offset": 3457,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "at Castle De Ganeway,",
          "offset": 3460,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "a generous patron of the church,",
          "offset": 3462,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "57:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3465,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "57:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "the descendant of Cana, an old north",
          "offset": 3468,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "57:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "prince of Manorin who came down to fight",
          "offset": 3471,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "off the Irish.",
          "offset": 3475,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nothing of the sort is stated here and",
          "offset": 3476,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "57:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "nothing at all on the other kingdoms in",
          "offset": 3480,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "58:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain. These sorts of things simply",
          "offset": 3483,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "58:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "didn't concern Gildas, only the faults",
          "offset": 3486,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "58:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the Western Britons south of",
          "offset": 3489,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "58:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hadrien's wall.",
          "offset": 3491,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "58:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Part three is a similar attack on the",
          "offset": 3496,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "58:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "clergy of the time.",
          "offset": 3499,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "58:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Apparently, people still sacrificed to",
          "offset": 3502,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "58:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "heathen gods. Not to mention the",
          "offset": 3504,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "58:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "personal depravity of their rulers.",
          "offset": 3507,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "58:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "And that's it. Only one written work",
          "offset": 3512,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "58:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "during a nearly 200year period.",
          "offset": 3515,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "58:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "Many more questions than answers.",
          "offset": 3520,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "58:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Who was Gildas and where was he from?",
          "offset": 3525,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "58:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "He was clearly an educated man. The",
          "offset": 3529,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "58:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "sheer fact of his writing makes that so.",
          "offset": 3532,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "58:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "living in an almost entirely illiterate",
          "offset": 3536,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "58:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "age.",
          "offset": 3538,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "58:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3540,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "59:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet, Gildus still uses terms like",
          "offset": 3543,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "59:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "governors, watchmen, and bishops.",
          "offset": 3546,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "59:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Titles likewise found on inscribed",
          "offset": 3552,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "59:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "memorial stones from Western Britain.",
          "offset": 3554,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Some conception of Rome surviving",
          "offset": 3559,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps.",
          "offset": 3562,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "59:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "But was he aware of how far Imperial",
          "offset": 3565,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "59:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "splendor had fallen? Or did he and his",
          "offset": 3568,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "59:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "countrymen assume everything was normal?",
          "offset": 3571,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "Well, it seems clear that Gildas was not",
          "offset": 3577,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "59:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "happy with the events of his time",
          "offset": 3580,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "59:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "and aware of a vague decline in the",
          "offset": 3583,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "59:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "fortunes of society.",
          "offset": 3586,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "59:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "extremely well read in the writings of",
          "offset": 3592,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "the classical world and possessing a",
          "offset": 3594,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "59:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "good grasp of Latin vernacular.",
          "offset": 3598,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "59:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Gildas clearly the result of a classical",
          "offset": 3600,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "60:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "education in an insular school seems",
          "offset": 3603,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "60:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "considerably better informed than later",
          "offset": 3607,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "60:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "writers such as Bead and Nius.",
          "offset": 3609,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "Quite simply, he may well have been one",
          "offset": 3616,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "60:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the few educated men left,",
          "offset": 3619,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "educated at one of the last schools,",
          "offset": 3625,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "offset": 3628,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "for he was the recipient of a",
          "offset": 3629,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "traditional Romanstyle education",
          "offset": 3632,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "60:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "somewhere in the west of Britain.",
          "offset": 3634,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "St. Patrick would have been put through",
          "offset": 3644,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "similar education, though his Latin",
          "offset": 3646,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "isn't as good. A product of his",
          "offset": 3649,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "60:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "education being cruy cut short by slave",
          "offset": 3651,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "60:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "traders on the Irish Sea.",
          "offset": 3655,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "60:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3658,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "60:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "One recipient we know much more about,",
          "offset": 3662,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "however, of about the same era was",
          "offset": 3664,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Augustinine of Hippo.",
          "offset": 3667,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "His parents were curialas,",
          "offset": 3669,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "local aristocrats.",
          "offset": 3672,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3674,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "61:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though even for them, people of means,",
          "offset": 3678,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "it was expensive to put their child",
          "offset": 3681,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "through school.",
          "offset": 3683,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "At one point, they had to pull him out",
          "offset": 3686,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "due to financial difficulties.",
          "offset": 3688,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "So, Gildus was clearly from a high",
          "offset": 3692,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "status family.",
          "offset": 3694,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "61:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "One candidate for his upbringing is",
          "offset": 3698,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sirencester in the Cotswwells where",
          "offset": 3701,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "significant evidence of post Roman",
          "offset": 3704,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "occupation has been found.",
          "offset": 3706,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "61:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though splendid, this was not",
          "offset": 3709,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "a scattering of houses and halls in the",
          "offset": 3715,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "61:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "center of the old amphitheater.",
          "offset": 3718,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "61:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "a much reduced population who simply",
          "offset": 3723,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "62:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "didn't have the numbers to defend the",
          "offset": 3726,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "62:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "perimeter of the town anymore.",
          "offset": 3728,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just a few decades earlier in the mid",
          "offset": 3737,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "62:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "5th century, intricately decorated",
          "offset": 3740,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "62:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "mosaics were being laid at Cheddar",
          "offset": 3742,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "62:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Villa. life going on as normal, much as",
          "offset": 3745,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "62:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "it was in many places on the island.",
          "offset": 3749,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "62:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "By the sixth century, it's a grim image",
          "offset": 3755,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "62:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "of what would become of that post Roman",
          "offset": 3758,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "62:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "world.",
          "offset": 3761,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "62:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3765,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "62:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Another candidate for Gildas is found on",
          "offset": 3769,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "62:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Shropshire farmland near Roxa.",
          "offset": 3772,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "62:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "The ruins of Viriconium,",
          "offset": 3775,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "the third or fourth largest city in",
          "offset": 3781,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "63:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Roman Britain.",
          "offset": 3784,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "63:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Unusually well preserved because of no",
          "offset": 3786,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "63:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "one built on top of it,",
          "offset": 3789,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "63:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "the place has a lured in archaeologists",
          "offset": 3791,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "63:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "and artists alike for centuries. From",
          "offset": 3793,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Byron to Mortimer Wheeler to AE",
          "offset": 3797,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Houseman,",
          "offset": 3799,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "63:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "interested in what it represents for the",
          "offset": 3803,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "63:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "fleetingness of existence as much as the",
          "offset": 3805,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "ancient ruins themselves.",
          "offset": 3808,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "63:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3810,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Once a colossal Roman basilica could be",
          "offset": 3816,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "63:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "seen here. huge pillars and roof,",
          "offset": 3819,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "63:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "one of the largest north of the Alps.",
          "offset": 3824,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "63:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3827,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "63:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "By the early fifth century, use of the",
          "offset": 3831,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "building eventually stopped.",
          "offset": 3833,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "63:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "Perhaps it was closed for safety",
          "offset": 3836,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "reasons.",
          "offset": 3838,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "The locals no longer having the means to",
          "offset": 3840,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "repair it.",
          "offset": 3843,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "64:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Soon enough, a number of WLE and Dorp",
          "offset": 3849,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "buildings were built within the place",
          "offset": 3852,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "being used for industrial purposes.",
          "offset": 3854,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "A workshop perhaps.",
          "offset": 3858,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "The roof was eventually taken down. The",
          "offset": 3860,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "64:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "shell used once more as a marketplace.",
          "offset": 3864,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "64:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3870,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "64:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet, there does seem to have been some",
          "offset": 3872,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "64:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "continuity here from the Roman era.",
          "offset": 3874,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "64:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though there is no evidence at Roxita of",
          "offset": 3879,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "64:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "the kind of Mediterranean pottery found",
          "offset": 3881,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "64:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "at other sites in western Britain like",
          "offset": 3883,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tintagel and Cadbury Castle.",
          "offset": 3886,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "Was it too far inland? And had society",
          "offset": 3889,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "and trade links really broken down that",
          "offset": 3892,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "much? The fear of bandits and briggins",
          "offset": 3894,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "keeping people more local? Perhaps",
          "offset": 3898,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3901,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "65:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "there are small bits of evidence to",
          "offset": 3904,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "65:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "suggest the place could have been home",
          "offset": 3906,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "to a bishop Rick.",
          "offset": 3908,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "65:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Maybe this was the domain of one of the",
          "offset": 3913,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "tyrants chided by Gildas.",
          "offset": 3915,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "65:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Certainly a figure who lived here was",
          "offset": 3921,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "65:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "strong enough to build a more",
          "offset": 3923,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "65:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "moderatelysized though nonetheless large",
          "offset": 3925,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "for the time timber hall",
          "offset": 3927,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "65:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "surrounded by a series of timber",
          "offset": 3931,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "65:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "buildings.",
          "offset": 3933,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "65:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "And Gildus wasn't strictly right in his",
          "offset": 3940,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "65:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "thinking that tyrants were a new thing.",
          "offset": 3943,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though those of his own time undoubtedly",
          "offset": 3947,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "65:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "seemed to have operated on a much",
          "offset": 3949,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "65:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "smaller scale, tyrants had been a common",
          "offset": 3951,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "feature of British society for",
          "offset": 3954,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "65:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "centuries.",
          "offset": 3957,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3960,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "65:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "Even before the emperor Constantine had",
          "offset": 3964,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "66:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself crowned Caesar at the city of",
          "offset": 3966,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "66:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "York in 306,",
          "offset": 3969,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "66:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "held a loft on the shields of his men.",
          "offset": 3971,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "66:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Third century emperors of Britannia had",
          "offset": 3977,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "66:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "all been the same.",
          "offset": 3979,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "66:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "Underneath the propaganda and pomp,",
          "offset": 3982,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "66:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "military strong men seizing political",
          "offset": 3985,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "66:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "and societal control.",
          "offset": 3988,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "66:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 3992,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "66:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "And in 406, after a colossal horde of",
          "offset": 3998,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "66:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Atlantic horsemen, Suvic long swords,",
          "offset": 4001,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "66:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Vandal refugees, entire nations on",
          "offset": 4005,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "66:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "the move crossed over the frozen Rine on",
          "offset": 4009,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "66:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "the last day of the year. the last day",
          "offset": 4012,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "66:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Romans could boast of total control",
          "offset": 4015,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "66:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the situation in Gaul.",
          "offset": 4017,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "66:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "When a certain British general crossed",
          "offset": 4020,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "66:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "over the channel, his own machinations",
          "offset": 4022,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "67:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "in mind, we get our first hints of the",
          "offset": 4024,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "67:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "post Roman system that would ultimately",
          "offset": 4028,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "67:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "develop in Britain.",
          "offset": 4030,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "67:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "Constantine III, we're told by the",
          "offset": 4036,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "67:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "historian Zosimus, adopted the name in",
          "offset": 4039,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "respect for the first Christian emperor",
          "offset": 4042,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "of 70 years before,",
          "offset": 4044,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "67:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "was the third tyrant in as many months.",
          "offset": 4047,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "67:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "The others, one apparently a civilian",
          "offset": 4051,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "from a city council,",
          "offset": 4054,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "67:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps one of the first independent",
          "offset": 4056,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "67:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "British rulers in centuries,",
          "offset": 4058,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "67:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "ended up conveniently dead,",
          "offset": 4062,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4068,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "67:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "leaving just Constantine to make his",
          "offset": 4070,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "67:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "grasp for power.",
          "offset": 4072,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "67:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Following in the footsteps of the late",
          "offset": 4077,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "4th century general Magnus Maximus,",
          "offset": 4079,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "Constantine stripped the province of",
          "offset": 4082,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "soldiers and headed to the quickening",
          "offset": 4084,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "maelstrom of Gaul,",
          "offset": 4087,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "68:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4089,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "68:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "appointing a Britain and a Frank as his",
          "offset": 4093,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "right-hand men. Historians have",
          "offset": 4096,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "hypothesized Constantine's true identity",
          "offset": 4098,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be British.",
          "offset": 4101,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "68:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4104,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "68:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "Whether he sought to save the empire or",
          "offset": 4105,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "68:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "break away entirely remains unclear,",
          "offset": 4107,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "68:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "but he seems to have steered clear of",
          "offset": 4111,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Germanic invaders.",
          "offset": 4113,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "68:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "The emperor Anorius ultimately sending a",
          "offset": 4116,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "force under a mercenary Saris the Goth",
          "offset": 4119,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "68:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "to fight him.",
          "offset": 4122,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "68:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "He'd end up dead, killed by one of his",
          "offset": 4126,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "68:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "own lieutenants.",
          "offset": 4129,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "68:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4131,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "By the time another tyrant, Riotamus",
          "offset": 4133,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "68:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "from Britany went to fight in Gaul,",
          "offset": 4136,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "taking a large force of many thousands",
          "offset": 4139,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "68:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "with him.",
          "offset": 4142,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "69:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "The army opposing him no longer",
          "offset": 4144,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "69:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "professed any loyalty to Rome.",
          "offset": 4146,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "69:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "They were the half guard of Yoro,",
          "offset": 4151,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "69:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "one of the mightiest of all Gothic war",
          "offset": 4154,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "leaders,",
          "offset": 4156,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "69:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "successor to Allaric, the sacker of",
          "offset": 4161,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rome, and the king of the Vigy Gothic",
          "offset": 4164,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "state, which now sprawled over much of",
          "offset": 4166,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "what was once the imperial provinces of",
          "offset": 4168,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "69:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hispania and Gaul.",
          "offset": 4171,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "69:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Riotamus, a candidate for the",
          "offset": 4176,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "inspiration for King Arthur, known from",
          "offset": 4179,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "69:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "contemporary letters as well as a later",
          "offset": 4182,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "historian Jordan",
          "offset": 4184,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "69:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "would be defeated by Yoric. And then",
          "offset": 4187,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "just 3 years later, the Germanic",
          "offset": 4190,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "69:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "mercenaries who resided over the rump of",
          "offset": 4192,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "69:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "the empire, now confined entirely to",
          "offset": 4194,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "69:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "Italy, decided to depose the last",
          "offset": 4197,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "emperor.",
          "offset": 4200,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "70:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4201,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "70:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Western Empire had already lingered",
          "offset": 4204,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "70:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "on for more than 60 years, dominated by",
          "offset": 4206,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "70:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Germanic generals.",
          "offset": 4209,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "70:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "But now it was dead.",
          "offset": 4211,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "70:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "After pulling the strings for many",
          "offset": 4216,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "70:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "years, the leader of the army, the",
          "offset": 4218,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "70:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Germanic general Odoaka, seized total",
          "offset": 4220,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "70:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "control instead.",
          "offset": 4223,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "70:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "Where consils and emperors had once",
          "offset": 4226,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "70:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "reigned, kingship had now been born.",
          "offset": 4228,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "70:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "But wait, a letter you may ask?",
          "offset": 4239,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "70:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Well, yes, literacy never died on the",
          "offset": 4243,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "70:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "continent.",
          "offset": 4246,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "70:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "And thankfully, there are many",
          "offset": 4248,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "70:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "continental sources aside from Gildas",
          "offset": 4250,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "70:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "with which we can use to construct a",
          "offset": 4253,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "70:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "basic narrative of events in Britain",
          "offset": 4255,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "70:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "during the years 400 to 600.",
          "offset": 4257,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "70:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Portchester Castle, Hampshire.",
          "offset": 4270,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "71:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "It may look like a medieval castle",
          "offset": 4273,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "71:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "today, but almost all of the",
          "offset": 4275,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "71:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "fortifications here are much older.",
          "offset": 4277,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "71:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Here",
          "offset": 4283,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "71:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "stands some of the greatest surviving",
          "offset": 4286,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "71:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Roman architecture in Western Europe.",
          "offset": 4288,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "71:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4293,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "71:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just one of a string of fortifications",
          "offset": 4295,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "71:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "built all around Britain towards the end",
          "offset": 4298,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "71:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the 3rd century to protect the",
          "offset": 4300,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "71:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "province in increasingly dangerous",
          "offset": 4303,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "71:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "times.",
          "offset": 4305,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "71:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4308,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "71:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "From Brancaster in the north to",
          "offset": 4309,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "71:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "Portchester in the west",
          "offset": 4311,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "71:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "and further north still signal towers",
          "offset": 4314,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "71:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "lined the northeastern shore of",
          "offset": 4317,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "71:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Northland.",
          "offset": 4319,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "71:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Great fortresses flanked Britain's",
          "offset": 4323,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "72:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "western seabboard too at Carlilele,",
          "offset": 4325,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "72:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Lancaster, Cardiff and more. Facing the",
          "offset": 4328,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "72:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "grim Irish Sea, home to increasingly",
          "offset": 4332,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "72:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "daring pirates.",
          "offset": 4336,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "72:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4340,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "72:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "And of course along the northern",
          "offset": 4341,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "72:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "frontier, Hadrien's wall, manned in part",
          "offset": 4343,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "72:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "even after the Empire fell.",
          "offset": 4347,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "72:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet even all these defenses weren't",
          "offset": 4352,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "72:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "enough.",
          "offset": 4356,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "72:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "Many raids are recorded and no doubt",
          "offset": 4358,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "72:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "many more remain unrecorded.",
          "offset": 4361,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "72:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4364,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "72:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "The most significant comes in 368 when a",
          "offset": 4367,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "72:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "so-called conspiracy of picss, Scots,",
          "offset": 4370,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "72:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "Atacotti, and Saxons are recorded by the",
          "offset": 4374,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "72:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "historian Amianis Marcelinus.",
          "offset": 4377,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "72:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "But great Roman war leaders could still",
          "offset": 4384,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "be found at this time. And after a year",
          "offset": 4387,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "of rampant violence, the revolt was",
          "offset": 4389,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "73:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "suppressed by a famed general from",
          "offset": 4391,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Spain, the father of a future emperor,",
          "offset": 4394,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "73:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Count Theodosius.",
          "offset": 4396,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "73:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet, the situation wasn't as simple",
          "offset": 4401,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "as that.",
          "offset": 4404,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "73:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "One of the foremost military positions",
          "offset": 4406,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "in Britain, the Duke of the Saxon shore",
          "offset": 4408,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "in 367,",
          "offset": 4410,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "73:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "may have been a German.",
          "offset": 4412,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "73:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "Times were changing",
          "offset": 4419,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "73:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Roman Britain by this time was",
          "offset": 4423,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "73:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "already a shadow of what it had once",
          "offset": 4425,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "been.",
          "offset": 4427,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "In recession for hundreds of years, its",
          "offset": 4430,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "73:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "towns had gradually shrunk in size.",
          "offset": 4433,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "73:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Its great buildings gradually",
          "offset": 4436,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "dismantled, replaced by gardens and",
          "offset": 4439,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "pavilions.",
          "offset": 4442,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Its population standing at around 2",
          "offset": 4444,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "million by the end of the 3rd century.",
          "offset": 4447,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "By the middle of the fifth, even long",
          "offset": 4449,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "74:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "before the plague of Justinian, it had",
          "offset": 4451,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "74:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "declined by a half.",
          "offset": 4454,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "74:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "When Constantine headed to the continent",
          "offset": 4460,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "in 407, the men he took were a far cry",
          "offset": 4462,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the well-rilled armies of previous",
          "offset": 4465,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "generations.",
          "offset": 4467,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "By now, soldiers were largely",
          "offset": 4470,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "hereditary, living with their families",
          "offset": 4472,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "74:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "in static held positions.",
          "offset": 4475,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "74:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was around this time that the very",
          "offset": 4480,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "74:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "last coins ever produced in Roman",
          "offset": 4482,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain would be minted.",
          "offset": 4485,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "A situation that rapidly hastened the",
          "offset": 4488,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "74:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "decline,",
          "offset": 4491,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "leading to a barter economy.",
          "offset": 4492,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Currency wouldn't return until the",
          "offset": 4495,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "seventh century.",
          "offset": 4498,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "74:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "And with the economy went the last",
          "offset": 4502,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "75:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "vestigages of the regular army, no",
          "offset": 4504,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "75:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "longer being paid salaries.",
          "offset": 4507,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "75:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "In places like Bird Oswald on Hadrien's",
          "offset": 4512,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "75:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "wall, once the Roman fort of Banner, the",
          "offset": 4515,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "75:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "men had no choice but to fight. Not for",
          "offset": 4518,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "75:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "pay now, but for their families, their",
          "offset": 4521,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "75:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "very way of life.",
          "offset": 4524,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "75:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "It's no wonder that Germanic mercenaries",
          "offset": 4529,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "75:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "began to be recruited by fearful Romano",
          "offset": 4532,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "75:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain. They needed the protection, not",
          "offset": 4535,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "75:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "only from outsiders, but from their own",
          "offset": 4539,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "75:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "neighbors.",
          "offset": 4541,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "75:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Having been occupied for close to 400",
          "offset": 4545,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "75:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "years, many in the lowlands southeast",
          "offset": 4548,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "75:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "had spoken Latin as a first language,",
          "offset": 4551,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "75:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "not British, and had little in common",
          "offset": 4554,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "75:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "with their more barbarous northern",
          "offset": 4557,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "75:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "neighbors.",
          "offset": 4558,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "75:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was these most romanized and pacified",
          "offset": 4560,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "75:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "areas that suffered the most.",
          "offset": 4563,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "76:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Germanic culture being perceptible in",
          "offset": 4566,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "76:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "the archaeological record as early as",
          "offset": 4569,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "76:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "430 AD.",
          "offset": 4572,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "76:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "But no doubt newcomers came in too,",
          "offset": 4576,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "76:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "following distant kinsmen serving in the",
          "offset": 4580,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "76:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "Roman army.",
          "offset": 4582,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "76:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "By around 400 AD, events on the",
          "offset": 4585,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "76:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "continent almost forced this to happen.",
          "offset": 4587,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "76:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "The losers in power struggles against",
          "offset": 4591,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "76:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "their Tangian and Frankish neighbors.",
          "offset": 4593,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "76:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "The old Saxons living along the German",
          "offset": 4596,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "76:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "shore were similarly beset by shifting,",
          "offset": 4598,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "76:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "unpredictable shorelines. and",
          "offset": 4601,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "76:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "increasingly deadly climatic conditions.",
          "offset": 4604,
          "duration": 10,
          "formattedTime": "76:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "A migrant crisis is very possible.",
          "offset": 4608,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "76:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "All of which was later neatly collated",
          "offset": 4613,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "76:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "into the tale of Hangist and Horser and",
          "offset": 4616,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "76:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "the insurgence of the mercenaries.",
          "offset": 4620,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "76:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "But as far as archaeology is concerned,",
          "offset": 4627,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "77:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "it wasn't all bad.",
          "offset": 4629,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "77:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "Some areas continued in much the same",
          "offset": 4632,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "77:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "way they had before.",
          "offset": 4635,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "77:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4638,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "77:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the 3rd century, the largely",
          "offset": 4643,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "77:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "self-governed Britannia Primer had",
          "offset": 4645,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "77:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "proved remarkably resilient,",
          "offset": 4647,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "77:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "and many might have assumed that life",
          "offset": 4649,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "77:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "would go on in the fifth century,",
          "offset": 4652,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "77:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps hoping for a revival of the",
          "offset": 4654,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "77:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "empire.",
          "offset": 4656,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "77:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "tying in neatly with the concept of late",
          "offset": 4658,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "77:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "antiquity rather than early medieval.",
          "offset": 4661,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "77:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "And life did go on in many areas.",
          "offset": 4667,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "77:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "Vericonium shows little change in the",
          "offset": 4670,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "77:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "initial post Roman period. Direct links",
          "offset": 4672,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "77:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "continuing via the western seaways even",
          "offset": 4675,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "77:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "after 476.",
          "offset": 4677,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "77:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Baths continued to be used until just",
          "offset": 4680,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "78:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "after 500.",
          "offset": 4682,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "78:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "In Wales and beyond the wall, long since",
          "offset": 4690,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "78:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "having been governed by auxiliaries,",
          "offset": 4694,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "78:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "native chiefs allied to the Roman cause.",
          "offset": 4697,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "78:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "The collapse wasn't anywhere near as",
          "offset": 4701,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "78:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "severe.",
          "offset": 4703,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "78:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "For here, north of the wall, the far",
          "offset": 4705,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "78:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "reaches of the Roman world, society",
          "offset": 4708,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "78:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "remained different.",
          "offset": 4711,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "78:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "bordered by the warlike picss at eternal",
          "offset": 4715,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "78:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "war with the empire. It had to be",
          "offset": 4718,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "78:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "within the Roman Empire. A firm division",
          "offset": 4725,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "78:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "existed between civilian and soldier.",
          "offset": 4728,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "78:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "The latter was a career path, not a way",
          "offset": 4731,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "78:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "of life.",
          "offset": 4734,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "78:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "But on the frontier, where life was",
          "offset": 4737,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "78:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "harder, no such division existed.",
          "offset": 4739,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "78:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "Everyone was a soldier.",
          "offset": 4743,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "79:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4748,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "79:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "So in the fifth century in the south,",
          "offset": 4758,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "79:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "mercenaries were necessary and they",
          "offset": 4760,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "79:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "weren't just Germans.",
          "offset": 4762,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "79:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4765,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "79:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "At Vericconium, the tombstone of a fifth",
          "offset": 4769,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "79:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "century Irish warrior has been found.",
          "offset": 4771,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "79:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Kunarix, roughly translated as hound",
          "offset": 4775,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "79:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "king.",
          "offset": 4777,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "79:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "His is just one of hundreds of",
          "offset": 4782,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "79:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "inscriptions like it. Often written in",
          "offset": 4784,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "79:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Latin as well as an early Irish script,",
          "offset": 4787,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "79:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Augum, found all over the west of",
          "offset": 4790,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "79:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain. testament to warrior",
          "offset": 4792,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "79:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "mercenaries sailing to make their",
          "offset": 4795,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "79:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "fortunes in Britain.",
          "offset": 4797,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "79:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "And over time, Irish place names along",
          "offset": 4803,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "80:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "the western coast suggest widespread",
          "offset": 4806,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "80:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "settlements, too. A similar story to the",
          "offset": 4808,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "80:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Germans in the east.",
          "offset": 4811,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "80:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Reoccupied hill forts in Gwenev like Gan",
          "offset": 4818,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "80:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Bodan on the Flynn Peninsula hint at a",
          "offset": 4822,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "80:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "growing unease of the Irish Sea.",
          "offset": 4825,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "80:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "This is the period St. Patrick was",
          "offset": 4828,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "80:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "seized as a slave by Irishmen.",
          "offset": 4831,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "80:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Several southern Welsh kingdoms like",
          "offset": 4837,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "80:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Divid and Breenog even trace their",
          "offset": 4839,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "80:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "lineages back to Irish free bootters.",
          "offset": 4841,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "80:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "In Gwennneth, however, the situation is",
          "offset": 4848,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "80:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "different. They trace their lineage to",
          "offset": 4851,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "80:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "another region where mercenaries weren't",
          "offset": 4854,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "80:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "necessary.",
          "offset": 4857,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "80:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "a war leader named Cana,",
          "offset": 4859,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "80:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "the old north.",
          "offset": 4863,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "81:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "But what of the last Roman outposts in",
          "offset": 4869,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "81:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "the north? The largest cities, Chester,",
          "offset": 4872,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "81:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Lincoln, and York, must surely have seen",
          "offset": 4876,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "81:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "some continuation, at least in the early",
          "offset": 4880,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "81:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "fifth century.",
          "offset": 4882,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "81:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "possessing their own independent city",
          "offset": 4884,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "81:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "councils. They were simply too",
          "offset": 4886,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "81:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "impressive to be abandoned entirely.",
          "offset": 4888,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "81:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "And on the western edge of Hadrien's",
          "offset": 4896,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "81:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "wall, Carlilele is a good candidate for",
          "offset": 4898,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "81:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Roman Britain's last city, surviving",
          "offset": 4901,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "81:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "well into the 7th century.",
          "offset": 4904,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "81:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "We have confused mentions of historical",
          "offset": 4912,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "81:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "events too surviving in much later Welsh",
          "offset": 4914,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "81:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "poetry.",
          "offset": 4917,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "81:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4919,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "81:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cole hen, for example, the old king Cole",
          "offset": 4922,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "from nursery rhymes has been suggested",
          "offset": 4924,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "82:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "as the last duck's Bratanniorum of York.",
          "offset": 4927,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "82:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Living in the early 400s, Cole sits",
          "offset": 4932,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "firmly at the top of a multitude of",
          "offset": 4934,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "82:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "royal pedigrees of old north kingdoms.",
          "offset": 4936,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though the evidence is flimsy, it's at",
          "offset": 4942,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "82:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "least possible that he declared himself",
          "offset": 4944,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "king of Britannia Secund sometime after",
          "offset": 4946,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "82:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "410, establishing some sort of",
          "offset": 4949,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "82:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "hereditary monarchy.",
          "offset": 4952,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "82:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 4955,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "82:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "And of course outside the cities we have",
          "offset": 4958,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "the hill forts.",
          "offset": 4962,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "Massive Iron Age fortresses sometimes",
          "offset": 4964,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "82:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "reoccupied in the post Roman period.",
          "offset": 4966,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "82:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "From Maiden Castle to Dennis Palace to",
          "offset": 4970,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "82:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cabbury Castle, fifth century site of",
          "offset": 4973,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "82:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "archaeologist Leslie Olock's search for",
          "offset": 4977,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "King Arthur.",
          "offset": 4980,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "82:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "But that's a story for another time.",
          "offset": 4982,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "83:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Gildas seems to have been writing after",
          "offset": 4991,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "83:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "a lengthy period of peace with the",
          "offset": 4994,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "83:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglo-Saxons.",
          "offset": 4995,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "83:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "The borders may have been fixed for a",
          "offset": 4998,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "83:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "while since the end of the fifth century",
          "offset": 5000,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "83:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps.",
          "offset": 5002,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "83:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5007,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "83:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Then in the later sixth century, the",
          "offset": 5009,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "83:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "wars begin again in earnest.",
          "offset": 5011,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "83:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "Interestingly, archaeologically few",
          "offset": 5017,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "83:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "items of Anglo-Saxon origin have been",
          "offset": 5019,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "83:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "found in Western Britain before around",
          "offset": 5022,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "83:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "550.",
          "offset": 5024,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "83:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "But this would soon change,",
          "offset": 5026,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "83:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "moving into Gloucester, Sirenester,",
          "offset": 5031,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "83:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "Bath, Dorset, and in the north beginning",
          "offset": 5034,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "83:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "to cross over the Penines into the",
          "offset": 5038,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "83:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "western lands.",
          "offset": 5040,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "83:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "The world they entered up there though",
          "offset": 5044,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "was a far cry from the one the Romans",
          "offset": 5046,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "84:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "had left behind",
          "offset": 5049,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "84:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "for 150 years is a long time.",
          "offset": 5054,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "84:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "And what of those lands north of the",
          "offset": 5058,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "84:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "wall, the least romanized portions of",
          "offset": 5060,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Roman Britain,",
          "offset": 5064,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "84:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5066,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "84:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "the very edge of the empire.",
          "offset": 5070,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "84:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Well, as far as Gildas was concerned,",
          "offset": 5076,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "84:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "they were semiarbarians.",
          "offset": 5079,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Early Welsh tradition even hints of a",
          "offset": 5082,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "84:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "war between the Western and the Northern",
          "offset": 5084,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "84:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britons in the sixth century.",
          "offset": 5086,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "with emnity between Malewin of Gwyneith",
          "offset": 5088,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "84:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Yurion of Regath.",
          "offset": 5091,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "84:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "And though it's clearly based on",
          "offset": 5095,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "fantastical travelers tales, he himself",
          "offset": 5097,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "84:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "never having visited Britain, we do have",
          "offset": 5100,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "85:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "one contemporary account of the North.",
          "offset": 5103,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "85:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "For this, we must turn back to the",
          "offset": 5107,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Eastern Empire and the writings of",
          "offset": 5110,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "Proopius.",
          "offset": 5112,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "In his history of the wars of Justinian,",
          "offset": 5114,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is a very brief, somewhat confused",
          "offset": 5117,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "mention of a diplomatic mission arriving",
          "offset": 5120,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "85:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "in Britain.",
          "offset": 5122,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "85:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "The emperor apparently still laid claim",
          "offset": 5125,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "to the island and we're told tried to",
          "offset": 5128,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "offer it to the Ostrogoths in return for",
          "offset": 5130,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sicily.",
          "offset": 5133,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "85:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5136,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "85:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "Looking past the hearsay and myth",
          "offset": 5140,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "contained in his writings, Precopius",
          "offset": 5143,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "85:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "describes the south as very different to",
          "offset": 5145,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "85:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "the north.",
          "offset": 5148,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "85:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "Divided by a great land wall, the",
          "offset": 5150,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "85:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "southerners lived in a civilized,",
          "offset": 5152,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "prosperous land inhabited by Britains,",
          "offset": 5154,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "85:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "angles, and fians.",
          "offset": 5157,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "85:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "To the north, however, a great dark",
          "offset": 5163,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "86:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "forest coated the land, peopleled by",
          "offset": 5166,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "86:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "wandering shades and monsters.",
          "offset": 5170,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "86:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "A savage landscape too tainted for",
          "offset": 5176,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "86:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "proper human occupation,",
          "offset": 5179,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "86:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "peopleled instead by wild beasts,",
          "offset": 5183,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "86:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "serpents, and the spirits of the dead.",
          "offset": 5186,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "86:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5193,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "86:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "1,500 years ago, the landscape of",
          "offset": 5199,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "86:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain looked very different to today.",
          "offset": 5202,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "86:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was wilder back then.",
          "offset": 5208,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "86:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "Huge forests coating much of the",
          "offset": 5213,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "86:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "wilderness areas,",
          "offset": 5216,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "86:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "stalked by wolves, wild cats, and bears.",
          "offset": 5218,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "86:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "No place for the faint of heart.",
          "offset": 5227,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "87:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "And to the north of Hadrien's Wall,",
          "offset": 5233,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "where woodland still thrives,",
          "offset": 5235,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "one of the greatest in all of Britain",
          "offset": 5239,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "87:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "still stood largely untouched.",
          "offset": 5242,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "87:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Great Caledonian forest.",
          "offset": 5245,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "87:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "When considering this overgrown mass of",
          "offset": 5253,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "oak and old growth wilderness, it's easy",
          "offset": 5256,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "to see how half a world away in the",
          "offset": 5259,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Eastern Empire, tales of evil spirits",
          "offset": 5262,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "87:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "and half men took hold.",
          "offset": 5265,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "87:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "For there is a good argument that as far",
          "offset": 5270,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "87:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "as the Christian Romans were concerned,",
          "offset": 5272,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "87:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "the people up here still did worship",
          "offset": 5274,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "87:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "devils and demons.",
          "offset": 5277,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "87:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "The old gods, many having become",
          "offset": 5280,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "synretatized with Roman ones long ago",
          "offset": 5282,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "88:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "and thus encouraged during earlier",
          "offset": 5285,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "88:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "times, still holding influence over the",
          "offset": 5287,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "88:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "forest dwellers.",
          "offset": 5291,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "88:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5293,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "88:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Up here, where Roman rule had only",
          "offset": 5295,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "88:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "extended briefly, the tribal societies",
          "offset": 5297,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "88:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "instead acting as clients outside the",
          "offset": 5300,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "88:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "very extreme limits of the empire,",
          "offset": 5303,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "88:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "ancient Celtic traditions were still",
          "offset": 5306,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "88:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "strong.",
          "offset": 5308,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "88:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Celtic pantheon still worshiped.",
          "offset": 5313,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "88:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "Of course, Christianity had made firm",
          "offset": 5317,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "88:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "inroads, too. And a scattering of",
          "offset": 5320,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "88:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "publicly Christian tribal kings ruled",
          "offset": 5322,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "88:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "over the populace.",
          "offset": 5325,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "88:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Regional rulers subject to overkings,",
          "offset": 5327,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "88:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "often fighting amongst themselves.",
          "offset": 5331,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "88:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "When Rome fell, most here carried on in",
          "offset": 5334,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "88:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "much the same lifestyle as they had for",
          "offset": 5337,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "88:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "millennia",
          "offset": 5340,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "88:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "without much concern for the outside",
          "offset": 5341,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "89:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "world.",
          "offset": 5344,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "89:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "And during that insularl looking",
          "offset": 5348,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "89:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "preiterate time when most evenings would",
          "offset": 5350,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "89:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "be spent huddled around hearthfire,",
          "offset": 5353,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "89:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "storytelling wasn't just a good pastime.",
          "offset": 5356,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "89:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was integral to the way society held",
          "offset": 5360,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "89:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "itself together.",
          "offset": 5363,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "89:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Britons loved a good story. We know",
          "offset": 5367,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "89:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "that.",
          "offset": 5371,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "89:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "A tale of a hero to inspire,",
          "offset": 5374,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "89:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "of a tyrant to warn,",
          "offset": 5378,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "89:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "a monster to scare children.",
          "offset": 5381,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "89:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "And during the long winter nights, with",
          "offset": 5386,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "89:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "darkness often coming at 3 or 4 p.m.,",
          "offset": 5389,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "89:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "these stories were even more important.",
          "offset": 5392,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "89:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "The greatest tale tellers of all",
          "offset": 5396,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "89:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "ultimately became heroes in their own",
          "offset": 5399,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "89:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "right. For this wasn't just a land",
          "offset": 5401,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "90:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "without the written word, but a land",
          "offset": 5404,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "90:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "where stories, reputation was integral",
          "offset": 5407,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "90:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "to the power of kings.",
          "offset": 5411,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "90:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "How indeed to hold together a kingdom",
          "offset": 5413,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "90:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "without them?",
          "offset": 5416,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "90:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "The best bars of all seem to have been",
          "offset": 5423,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "90:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "hugely influential figures in their own",
          "offset": 5426,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "90:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "right, being paid inordinate amounts of",
          "offset": 5428,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "90:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "riches to promote their patrons.",
          "offset": 5432,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "90:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "The wiliest regularly passing between",
          "offset": 5438,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "90:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "royal patrons during their careers,",
          "offset": 5441,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "90:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "depending on who promised to pay the",
          "offset": 5445,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "90:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "most.",
          "offset": 5447,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "90:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5448,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "90:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "A passing caravan of a bard would have",
          "offset": 5453,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "90:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "been a sight to behold. Armed retainers,",
          "offset": 5456,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "90:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "luxuries from across the known world,",
          "offset": 5460,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "91:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "horses animals.",
          "offset": 5463,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "91:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "In a time when most people had nothing,",
          "offset": 5470,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "91:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "the bardic life was something to aspire",
          "offset": 5474,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "91:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "towards and to love.",
          "offset": 5477,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "91:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "They were the celebrities of the day.",
          "offset": 5480,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "91:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "And in the mid6th century, the greatest",
          "offset": 5483,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "91:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "of them all, remembered in future",
          "offset": 5486,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "91:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "generations as the lord of all bars was",
          "offset": 5489,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "91:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "TAin.",
          "offset": 5492,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "91:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the latter sixth century, Tleasin",
          "offset": 5494,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "91:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "worked at many courts, at least three",
          "offset": 5497,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "91:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "that we know of. He was a PR specialist,",
          "offset": 5500,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "91:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "a spin doctor for whoever could pay the",
          "offset": 5504,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "91:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "most out of the 13 or so vying kings of",
          "offset": 5507,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "91:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Old North. His most famous patron of",
          "offset": 5509,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "91:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "all, however, and the poems that remain",
          "offset": 5513,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "91:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "most lorded today, was the great king of",
          "offset": 5515,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "91:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "Regath Yuran.",
          "offset": 5519,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "91:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Initially a straightforward court barred",
          "offset": 5526,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "92:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "during his own lifetime, TAin is also a",
          "offset": 5529,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "92:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "prime example of the shape-shifting",
          "offset": 5532,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "92:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "power of oral tradition.",
          "offset": 5534,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "92:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "By the time his stories were finally",
          "offset": 5540,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "92:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "written down by the 14th century, he had",
          "offset": 5542,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "92:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "become a literal shape shifter",
          "offset": 5545,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "92:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "and a druidic time traveler.",
          "offset": 5548,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "92:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "The possessor of a cult knowledge and",
          "offset": 5552,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "92:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "spiritual law,",
          "offset": 5554,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "92:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "transformed over the years to suit the",
          "offset": 5557,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "92:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "political needs and societal agendas of",
          "offset": 5559,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "92:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "rewriters from 9th century nationalists",
          "offset": 5562,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "92:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "to 14th century Arthuran romancers.",
          "offset": 5565,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "92:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "Such was his popularity and renown by",
          "offset": 5571,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "92:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "the high middle ages that he was used as",
          "offset": 5573,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "92:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "a floating figure to tie together any",
          "offset": 5576,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "92:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "and all writings.",
          "offset": 5579,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "92:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "In an 11th century saint's life, he",
          "offset": 5582,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "93:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "travels across the sea to Britany,",
          "offset": 5584,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "93:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "acting as a sage and prophesying the",
          "offset": 5586,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "93:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "birth of a saint king.",
          "offset": 5588,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "93:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5591,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "93:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the Welsh epic, the Mabinogian, he",
          "offset": 5593,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "93:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "follows a mythical king to war in",
          "offset": 5596,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "93:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ireland.",
          "offset": 5598,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "93:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5600,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "93:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ultimately, by the 13th century,",
          "offset": 5603,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "93:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "becoming a supporter of Thlean the",
          "offset": 5605,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "93:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Great,",
          "offset": 5607,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "93:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "by which time he'd morphed into the",
          "offset": 5609,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "93:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "archetype of the charismatic riddling",
          "offset": 5611,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "93:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "sorcerer.",
          "offset": 5614,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "93:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tooasin is also linked to pre-Christian",
          "offset": 5620,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "93:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "sorcerers like Gwyian and Merlin,",
          "offset": 5623,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "93:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "a similarly metamorphosizing figure",
          "offset": 5630,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "93:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "based on a sixth century bard",
          "offset": 5632,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "93:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "as much as he is to Christianity,",
          "offset": 5638,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "93:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "acting as a bridge between traditional",
          "offset": 5642,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "94:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Welsh law and the more modern",
          "offset": 5644,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "94:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "ecclesiastical learning of medieval",
          "offset": 5646,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "94:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "times.",
          "offset": 5648,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "94:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet even so, deep down there is truth in",
          "offset": 5652,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "94:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "the stories.",
          "offset": 5656,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "94:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Fundamental aspects of the tales which",
          "offset": 5658,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "94:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "remain from as much as a thousand years",
          "offset": 5661,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "94:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "before.",
          "offset": 5663,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "94:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "And his stories aren't alone. Long",
          "offset": 5668,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "94:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "before these later tales were written",
          "offset": 5672,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "94:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "down at the beginning of the 9th century",
          "offset": 5674,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "94:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "historianum",
          "offset": 5677,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "94:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "traditionally attributed to the",
          "offset": 5678,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "94:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "historian Nenius",
          "offset": 5680,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "94:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "we're given five names of famous poets",
          "offset": 5682,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "94:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "working during the later 6th century.",
          "offset": 5685,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "94:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5688,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "94:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "The writings of all of these figures and",
          "offset": 5695,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "94:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "more still survive today, poured over by",
          "offset": 5698,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "94:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "armies of scholars over the years.",
          "offset": 5701,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "95:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Using literary analysis, much older",
          "offset": 5705,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "95:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "sections can still be located within the",
          "offset": 5708,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "95:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "masses of later editions.",
          "offset": 5710,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "95:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "Today, the five ancient books of Wales",
          "offset": 5716,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "95:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "remain some of the oldest European",
          "offset": 5719,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "95:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "literature found anywhere.",
          "offset": 5721,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "95:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "and are integral to any study of the",
          "offset": 5724,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "95:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "sixth century old north.",
          "offset": 5727,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "95:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Talasin's book is one,",
          "offset": 5730,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "95:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ana's another,",
          "offset": 5733,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "95:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "but we also have the black book of",
          "offset": 5736,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "95:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Kamaran,",
          "offset": 5739,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "95:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "the red book of Hergus, and finally the",
          "offset": 5741,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "95:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mabonogian,",
          "offset": 5745,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "95:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "often known as the white book of Reth.",
          "offset": 5746,
          "duration": 12,
          "formattedTime": "95:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5750,
          "duration": 11,
          "formattedTime": "95:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "Bead, greatest historian of his age, who",
          "offset": 5758,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "95:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "knew just about everything that could be",
          "offset": 5761,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "96:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "known during the 8th century, barely",
          "offset": 5763,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "96:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "mentions regg, gdin, altcloot or elmeth.",
          "offset": 5766,
          "duration": 11,
          "formattedTime": "96:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "They only survive through bardic poetry.",
          "offset": 5772,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "96:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "But does this world exist outside the",
          "offset": 5777,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "96:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "stories?",
          "offset": 5780,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "96:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "What tale does the archaeology tell?",
          "offset": 5782,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "96:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5788,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "96:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Brian Hope Taylor always had a certain",
          "offset": 5792,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "96:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "flare for finding things.",
          "offset": 5795,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "96:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "He was a born archaeologist.",
          "offset": 5798,
          "duration": 11,
          "formattedTime": "96:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5802,
          "duration": 11,
          "formattedTime": "96:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "The story goes that in the early 1950s,",
          "offset": 5810,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "96:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "an artist at the time with no university",
          "offset": 5813,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "96:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "education, he stared at aerial",
          "offset": 5815,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "96:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "photographs of a North Umbrean plane.",
          "offset": 5818,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "96:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cuttingedge technology at the time.",
          "offset": 5821,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "97:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5824,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "97:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "He pinpointed several buildings he",
          "offset": 5826,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "97:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "wished to excavate.",
          "offset": 5829,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "97:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Within a few years upon arriving at the",
          "offset": 5832,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "97:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "place, it didn't take long for his hunch",
          "offset": 5835,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "97:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be proved right.",
          "offset": 5837,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "97:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5840,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "97:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Out in the fields below the imposing",
          "offset": 5842,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "97:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "mountain of Yevering Bell, a miraculous",
          "offset": 5844,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "97:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "needle in a haststack, Hope Taylor",
          "offset": 5847,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "97:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "precisely pinpointed a high status 6th",
          "offset": 5850,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "97:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "century Anglian settlement.",
          "offset": 5853,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "97:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "And not just any either.",
          "offset": 5856,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "97:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "As decades of further study would show,",
          "offset": 5862,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "97:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "this was the Anglian settlement,",
          "offset": 5864,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "97:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5867,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "97:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "a royal palace, very probably the Edge",
          "offset": 5871,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "97:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "Guthrin bead talks of in his history",
          "offset": 5875,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "97:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5879,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "97:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "where King Edwin, the first Christian",
          "offset": 5881,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "98:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "king of the English, reigned.",
          "offset": 5884,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "98:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "An immense cattle corral, timber halls,",
          "offset": 5887,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "98:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "and even an amphitheater-like structure",
          "offset": 5890,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "98:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "have been revealed.",
          "offset": 5892,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "98:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "And on the mountain overlooking it all,",
          "offset": 5897,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "98:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "an earlier massive Iron Age hill fort",
          "offset": 5900,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "98:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "occupied throughout Roman times. And",
          "offset": 5904,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "98:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "after",
          "offset": 5908,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "98:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yeing had already been a high status",
          "offset": 5911,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "98:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "capital for hundreds of years by the",
          "offset": 5914,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "98:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "time the Anglians arrived,",
          "offset": 5916,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "98:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "a center of power for the Britons,",
          "offset": 5921,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "98:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "well into the latter fifth and early 6th",
          "offset": 5925,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "98:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "century.",
          "offset": 5928,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "98:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "And it's not alone either. Excavations",
          "offset": 5931,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "98:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "at Bambra Castle, the other famous",
          "offset": 5934,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "98:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "capital of Benissia, suggested not just",
          "offset": 5936,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "98:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "earlier British occupation, but a",
          "offset": 5939,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "98:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "possible Roman settlement, too. A",
          "offset": 5941,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "99:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "lighthouse or a beacon tower, perhaps.",
          "offset": 5944,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "99:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5947,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "99:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Unfortunately, most of the evidence is",
          "offset": 5951,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "99:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "gone.",
          "offset": 5954,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "99:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 5955,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "99:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "At places like Edinburgh Rock, thought",
          "offset": 5959,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "99:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "to have been capital of the Gdin,",
          "offset": 5961,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "99:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "excavations are difficult.",
          "offset": 5963,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "99:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "More than a thousand years of occupation",
          "offset": 5966,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "99:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "have removed much of the past as the",
          "offset": 5968,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "99:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "place was built over again and again by",
          "offset": 5971,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "99:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "succeeding generations.",
          "offset": 5973,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "99:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "But in some places that weren't occupied",
          "offset": 5980,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "99:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "again, hill forts remain.",
          "offset": 5983,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "99:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Cheviat Hills near Yevering are one",
          "offset": 5993,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "99:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "example",
          "offset": 5995,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "99:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "shown in immense earthworks amidst",
          "offset": 5997,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "99:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "farmland.",
          "offset": 6000,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "99:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "This was a powerful place during Roman",
          "offset": 6001,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "100:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "times",
          "offset": 6004,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "100:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "and hill forts during the Roman period",
          "offset": 6012,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "100:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "and after were very common up here.",
          "offset": 6015,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "100:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hundreds of them have been found.",
          "offset": 6020,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "100:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 6026,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "100:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "The idea we get is of a militarized",
          "offset": 6028,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "100:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "zone. Unlike the lowland areas which",
          "offset": 6031,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "100:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "were romanized and pacified, raids from",
          "offset": 6033,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "100:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "picss and Scots remained common up here",
          "offset": 6036,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "100:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "and war was the norm.",
          "offset": 6039,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "100:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Indeed, in the north and west,",
          "offset": 6043,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "100:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "indigenous people lived in enclosed",
          "offset": 6046,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "100:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "settlements the same as they had before",
          "offset": 6048,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "100:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Romans came. Their lives had changed",
          "offset": 6050,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "100:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "little during Roman times.",
          "offset": 6053,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "100:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "One of the most important of all is also",
          "offset": 6060,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "100:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "found in Lotheian, heartland of the Gdin",
          "offset": 6062,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "101:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "at Trapane Lore, where not only a",
          "offset": 6067,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "101:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "substantial reinforcing of the walls",
          "offset": 6069,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "101:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "took place at the end of the fifth",
          "offset": 6071,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "101:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "century, but massive hordes of Roman",
          "offset": 6073,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "101:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "wealth were found in 1919.",
          "offset": 6075,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "101:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "generally interpreted as protection",
          "offset": 6078,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "101:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "payments made to client kings in return",
          "offset": 6080,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "101:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "for manning the northern frontier.",
          "offset": 6083,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "101:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Much had changed since the emperor",
          "offset": 6089,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "101:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Septimus Seus marched north at the",
          "offset": 6091,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "101:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "beginning of the 3rd century to shatter",
          "offset": 6093,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "101:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "the mighti and the caledoni.",
          "offset": 6095,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "101:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "By the fifth century, the Romans had to",
          "offset": 6100,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "101:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "rely on client kings.",
          "offset": 6103,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "101:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "And what of those kings?",
          "offset": 6106,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "101:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "In most continental provinces of the",
          "offset": 6112,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "101:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "Romans, like Hispania and Gaul,",
          "offset": 6114,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "101:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "centuries of elite participation in the",
          "offset": 6118,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "101:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Roman world led to a near total",
          "offset": 6120,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "101:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "breakdown of native culture and",
          "offset": 6122,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "102:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "language,",
          "offset": 6124,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "102:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "replaced by Latin in professional and",
          "offset": 6126,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "102:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "everyday life.",
          "offset": 6128,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "102:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 6132,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "102:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "In Britain, though the process was",
          "offset": 6134,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "102:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "encouraged, it was never fully",
          "offset": 6136,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "102:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "completed. In everyday life, brethonic",
          "offset": 6139,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "102:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "remained the language of choice for much",
          "offset": 6142,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "102:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the island,",
          "offset": 6144,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "102:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 6147,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "102:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "particularly in the north, an area not",
          "offset": 6149,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "102:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "widely settled by Romans from elsewhere",
          "offset": 6152,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "102:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the empire, being largely restricted",
          "offset": 6154,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "102:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "to military garrisons along the wall.",
          "offset": 6157,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "102:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 6161,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "102:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "It's from the writings of Roman",
          "offset": 6164,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "102:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "geographers that we get the names of the",
          "offset": 6166,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "102:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "British Confederacies that held sway",
          "offset": 6168,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "102:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "along the frontier.",
          "offset": 6169,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "102:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 6173,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "102:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Notably, we have the Damnoni, the",
          "offset": 6175,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "102:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nvanti, the Soo, and the Votadini.",
          "offset": 6177,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "102:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 6182,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "103:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "In archaeology, the Damnoni and the",
          "offset": 6183,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "103:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Votedini in particular have notable",
          "offset": 6186,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "103:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "continuity from the pre- Roman Iron Age",
          "offset": 6188,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "103:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "all the way through to the Roman period",
          "offset": 6190,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "103:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "and beyond.",
          "offset": 6192,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "103:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "As we've seen from the horde at Traprain",
          "offset": 6195,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "103:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Law, it paid well to work for Rome",
          "offset": 6197,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "103:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "and came with it a powerful legitimacy",
          "offset": 6202,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "103:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "over rival rulers.",
          "offset": 6204,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "103:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 6206,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "103:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "With the continental troubles of the",
          "offset": 6209,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "103:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "fifth century, however, no doubt came",
          "offset": 6211,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "103:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "the disintegration of many of these old",
          "offset": 6213,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "103:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "tribal loyalties.",
          "offset": 6215,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "103:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "Some of them at least propped up by",
          "offset": 6221,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "103:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Roman power,",
          "offset": 6223,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "103:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "though some of the older identities",
          "offset": 6227,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "103:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "remained intact, such as the Votadini.",
          "offset": 6229,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "103:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "New powers emerged, too. a renegotiation",
          "offset": 6232,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "103:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "of a more personal loyalty between king",
          "offset": 6236,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "103:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "and follower.",
          "offset": 6239,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "103:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "And over time, particularly as the sixth",
          "offset": 6242,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "104:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "century dawn, alongside British",
          "offset": 6245,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "104:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "archaeological finds are increasingly",
          "offset": 6248,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "104:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "seen pictish, Irish, and Anglo-Saxon",
          "offset": 6250,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "104:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "items.",
          "offset": 6254,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "104:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "mercenaries to pay masters of the old",
          "offset": 6256,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "104:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "north, perhaps exiled princes making",
          "offset": 6258,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "104:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "common cause.",
          "offset": 6261,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "104:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 6264,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "104:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "Both were common in later centuries, but",
          "offset": 6267,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "104:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "unfortunately definitive answers remain",
          "offset": 6270,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "104:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "unclear.",
          "offset": 6273,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "104:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "And what were those kingdoms really",
          "offset": 6275,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "104:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "like? Aroran castles. They were not.",
          "offset": 6278,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "104:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 6285,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "104:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Today, pubs all over Britain bear the",
          "offset": 6295,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "104:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "name of the green man.",
          "offset": 6298,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "104:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 6302,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "105:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mysterious fertility symbol found all",
          "offset": 6306,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "105:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "over Europe and beyond.",
          "offset": 6308,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "105:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "And there's an argument that the roots",
          "offset": 6312,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "105:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "of this horned figure are much older,",
          "offset": 6314,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "105:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "bearing a resemblance to the ancient",
          "offset": 6318,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "105:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Celtic deity Kunos.",
          "offset": 6320,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "105:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 6324,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "105:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "Part of the reason for the Romans",
          "offset": 6329,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "105:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "immense success as an empire was their",
          "offset": 6331,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "105:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "acceptance of religious worship. For 300",
          "offset": 6333,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "105:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "years in Britain, they had not only",
          "offset": 6337,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "105:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "encouraged native cults, but entrenched",
          "offset": 6339,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "105:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "them in society by merging their own",
          "offset": 6342,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "105:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "gods with them.",
          "offset": 6344,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "105:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "And by the time their rule in Britain",
          "offset": 6351,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "105:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "came to an end, these cults could still",
          "offset": 6353,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "105:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "be found all over the island.",
          "offset": 6355,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "105:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "Of",
          "offset": 6361,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "106:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "course, Christianity came too. St.",
          "offset": 6367,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "106:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ninian supposedly arriving on the",
          "offset": 6370,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "106:10"
        },
        {
