          "text": "said to have pushed the Angles all the",
          "offset": 6901,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "115:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "way back to the sea. in a great",
          "offset": 6903,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "115:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "reconquest worthy of Ambrosius",
          "offset": 6907,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "115:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Aurelianis and the great fortress of",
          "offset": 6909,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "115:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cadbury Castle a century earlier.",
          "offset": 6912,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "115:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 6916,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "115:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "For 3 days, in a great turning point in",
          "offset": 6919,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "115:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "the war, we're told forces drawn from",
          "offset": 6922,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "115:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "most of the northern British kingdoms",
          "offset": 6925,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "115:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "besieged the Anglians,",
          "offset": 6927,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "115:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "either at their fortress of Bambra or",
          "offset": 6930,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "115:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "the nearby island of Lindesvan, which",
          "offset": 6932,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "115:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "also has a prominent fortified hilltop.",
          "offset": 6935,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "115:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "The assembled kings came from far and",
          "offset": 6940,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "115:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "wide. From old Clute, Reev, Elmet, and",
          "offset": 6942,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "115:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "probably Gdin.",
          "offset": 6948,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "115:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "Their leader, of course, was Yuran,",
          "offset": 6956,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "115:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "called the pillar of Britain and King of",
          "offset": 6960,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "116:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Golden by Tusin.",
          "offset": 6963,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "116:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "And amazingly, the written record does",
          "offset": 6970,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "116:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "somewhat line up with archaeology",
          "offset": 6973,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "116:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "with Bambborra remaining one of the few",
          "offset": 6978,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "116:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "verified Anglo-Saxon settlements from",
          "offset": 6980,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "116:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "the earlier 6th century",
          "offset": 6983,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "116:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "with very few pagan burial grounds in",
          "offset": 6985,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "116:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "the area too until later.",
          "offset": 6988,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "116:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "But how had these outsiders got there in",
          "offset": 6992,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "116:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "the first place?",
          "offset": 6996,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "116:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "Well, on a keel probably as a traveling",
          "offset": 7002,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "116:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "band of sword warriors.",
          "offset": 7006,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "116:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "One near contemporary ship is the 23 m",
          "offset": 7010,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "116:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "long protol long ship found at Naidum in",
          "offset": 7013,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "116:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Germany in the 19th century.",
          "offset": 7016,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "116:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "It's an impressive site and a glimpse",
          "offset": 7019,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "116:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "into this long lost world.",
          "offset": 7022,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "117:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Anglo-Saxon chronicle written much",
          "offset": 7028,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "117:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "later but working from much older",
          "offset": 7030,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "117:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "sources gives a name for the founder of",
          "offset": 7033,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "117:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "this kingdom",
          "offset": 7035,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "117:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "the flamebringer",
          "offset": 7038,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "117:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "son of Eopa and king of Bernissia for 12",
          "offset": 7040,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "117:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "years from 547.",
          "offset": 7044,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "117:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 7047,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "117:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "But whether he came from the Anglo-Saxon",
          "offset": 7049,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "117:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "lands further to the south or directly",
          "offset": 7051,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "117:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "from the continent is anyone's guess,",
          "offset": 7054,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "117:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 7057,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "117:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "but many historians think an origin in",
          "offset": 7059,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "117:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "the other older Anglian areas is",
          "offset": 7062,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "117:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "possible.",
          "offset": 7065,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "117:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Perhaps at DRA around York, where",
          "offset": 7067,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "117:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "according to much later traditions, a",
          "offset": 7070,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "117:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "mercenary named Samuel is thought to",
          "offset": 7073,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "117:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "have seized control in the fifth",
          "offset": 7075,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "117:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "century.",
          "offset": 7077,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "117:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "These days, rather than a",
          "offset": 7081,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "118:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "straightforward land grab, the situation",
          "offset": 7082,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "118:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "is now thought to have been far more",
          "offset": 7085,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "118:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "nuanced.",
          "offset": 7088,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "118:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Germanic soldiers had been operating on",
          "offset": 7093,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "118:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "the northern frontier since the 1st",
          "offset": 7096,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "118:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "century AD,",
          "offset": 7098,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "118:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "from Bavian marines under the first",
          "offset": 7100,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "118:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "emperors to alammanic nobility under",
          "offset": 7102,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "118:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Constantine.",
          "offset": 7106,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "118:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "All alike came here in service to Roman",
          "offset": 7108,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "118:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "pay masters, thrral to Roman coin.",
          "offset": 7112,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "118:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "And by the sixth century, their remains",
          "offset": 7119,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "118:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "are hinted at in the archaeological",
          "offset": 7121,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "118:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "record by new styles of Germanic metal",
          "offset": 7123,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "118:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "work found at burial sites. And over",
          "offset": 7126,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "118:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "time, the overall culture becomes more",
          "offset": 7129,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "118:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "and more Germanic.",
          "offset": 7132,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "118:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 7136,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "118:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "It seems the Anglian mercenaries did",
          "offset": 7140,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "118:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "their job well, fending off Pictish and",
          "offset": 7142,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "119:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "other seaborn raiders. A little too",
          "offset": 7145,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "119:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "well, in fact. Eventually, perhaps via",
          "offset": 7148,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "119:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "marriage coupled with pressure from more",
          "offset": 7152,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "119:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "incoming colonists, and maybe access to",
          "offset": 7154,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "119:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "the trade system of the North Sea, after",
          "offset": 7158,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "119:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "the collapse of the Roman system, they",
          "offset": 7160,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "119:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "became the pay masters.",
          "offset": 7163,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "119:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "The locals either joined them, becoming",
          "offset": 7168,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "119:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Germanic over time, or became their",
          "offset": 7170,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "119:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "slaves.",
          "offset": 7173,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "119:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "As with many Germanic dynasties, in",
          "offset": 7178,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "119:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Benia, Eda as the founder rings out",
          "offset": 7181,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "119:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "above all others.",
          "offset": 7184,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "119:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "And though we can't be sure of the real",
          "offset": 7187,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "119:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "extent of his power, future kings of",
          "offset": 7189,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "119:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "Benia all claimed descent from him.",
          "offset": 7191,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "119:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "For Henry of Huntington writing in the",
          "offset": 7197,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "119:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "12th century, he was the leader of a",
          "offset": 7199,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "119:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "group of war bands operating north of",
          "offset": 7202,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "120:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "the wall between the Tine and the Tweed",
          "offset": 7204,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "120:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the mid6th century.",
          "offset": 7206,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "120:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "And though no helmets have been found",
          "offset": 7210,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "120:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "from this era and very little",
          "offset": 7212,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "120:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "archaeological evidence, we can see",
          "offset": 7213,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "120:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "hints of this warrior culture in the",
          "offset": 7216,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "120:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "contemporary Swedish helmets at Vendel",
          "offset": 7218,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "120:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Valsciad",
          "offset": 7220,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "120:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "and the slightly later helmet at Sutton",
          "offset": 7224,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "120:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "who",
          "offset": 7227,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "120:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "one hint at the power of these people is",
          "offset": 7231,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "120:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "the bambber sword. One of the most",
          "offset": 7233,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "120:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "magnificent pattern welded swords ever",
          "offset": 7236,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "120:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "found.",
          "offset": 7239,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "120:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though bead claims that Eda built the",
          "offset": 7246,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "120:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "castle at Bambber, there is evidence of",
          "offset": 7249,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "120:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "earlier British occupation.",
          "offset": 7251,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "120:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "And despite the importance given to Edah",
          "offset": 7255,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "120:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "by his later descendants, his rule never",
          "offset": 7258,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "120:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "extended further than a foothold on the",
          "offset": 7260,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "121:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "coast.",
          "offset": 7263,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "121:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "His immediate descendants too would only",
          "offset": 7264,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "121:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "survive the Britons by the skin of their",
          "offset": 7267,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "121:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "teeth.",
          "offset": 7269,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "121:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "But survive they did. And it's likely",
          "offset": 7271,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "121:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "that in reality Eda wasn't the only",
          "offset": 7274,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "121:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglian warlord operating in the region.",
          "offset": 7277,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "121:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "After his death, his brood of sons,",
          "offset": 7281,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "121:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "grandsons, and rivals would rise to",
          "offset": 7284,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "121:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "power one after the other, raiding far",
          "offset": 7286,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "121:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "and wide.",
          "offset": 7289,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "121:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "fierce pagan warriors bred for war.",
          "offset": 7292,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "121:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "It wouldn't be long before the eastern",
          "offset": 7297,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "121:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "British lands began to be carved out by",
          "offset": 7299,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "121:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "the newcomers.",
          "offset": 7301,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "121:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "And as far as the Britain were",
          "offset": 7304,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "121:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "concerned, enough was enough. Something",
          "offset": 7306,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "121:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "had to be done to stop them.",
          "offset": 7310,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "121:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "Traditionally, the kingdom of Regath has",
          "offset": 7316,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "121:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "been associated with the hills and",
          "offset": 7319,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "121:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "valleys of Cumbria.",
          "offset": 7321,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "122:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet, Bardic references to Yuran and",
          "offset": 7323,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "122:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "his sons range from Lachlund all the way",
          "offset": 7326,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "122:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "to Yorkshire.",
          "offset": 7329,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "122:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "His strongholds are said to have been",
          "offset": 7332,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "122:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "located all over the north,",
          "offset": 7334,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "122:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "suggesting his power may have extended",
          "offset": 7339,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "122:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "to a large hedgeimony over other rulers.",
          "offset": 7341,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "122:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet many of these places have never",
          "offset": 7345,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "122:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "been located.",
          "offset": 7347,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "122:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Not to mention the fact that they might",
          "offset": 7349,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "122:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "have been added to the Yuran story by",
          "offset": 7351,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "122:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "later generations.",
          "offset": 7353,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "122:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "Due to the unreliable nature of the",
          "offset": 7356,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "122:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "sources, the actual extent of Yurian's",
          "offset": 7358,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "122:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "domain remains ever elusive.",
          "offset": 7360,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "122:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hailed as strong champion in battle by",
          "offset": 7366,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "122:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tasin,",
          "offset": 7369,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "122:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yurian's campaigns ranged far and wide.",
          "offset": 7371,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "122:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "Fighting against the north Welsh in one",
          "offset": 7374,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "122:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "tradition, attacking Manor in another, a",
          "offset": 7376,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "122:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "place interpreted variously as Manorga",
          "offset": 7380,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "122:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "Dothin in the north or even the aisle of",
          "offset": 7382,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "123:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "man. Reg did lie on the Irish Sea after",
          "offset": 7385,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "123:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "all.",
          "offset": 7389,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "123:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Slightly more concrete evidence can be",
          "offset": 7393,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "123:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "found in the battle of Ri Olute, the",
          "offset": 7395,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "123:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "fort of the Clyde, stronghold of King",
          "offset": 7398,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "123:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Redc of Alt Cloot, his later ally at the",
          "offset": 7401,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "123:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "siege of Lindesvan,",
          "offset": 7405,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "123:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "one of the only one of the kings who",
          "offset": 7409,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "123:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "fought there whose existence is attested",
          "offset": 7410,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "123:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "elsewhere in a reliable source of",
          "offset": 7413,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "123:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "non-Welsh provenence.",
          "offset": 7415,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "123:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "The 7th century life of Columba by Adam",
          "offset": 7418,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "123:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nan of Iona.",
          "offset": 7420,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "123:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Some historians have even interpreted",
          "offset": 7427,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "123:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "these battles, often described as great",
          "offset": 7429,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "123:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "cattle raids, as in reality more serious",
          "offset": 7431,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "123:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "attempts by Regg to subdue the other",
          "offset": 7434,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "123:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "British kingdoms into overlordship.",
          "offset": 7437,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "123:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 7439,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "123:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "Unfortunately, we can't know the truth.",
          "offset": 7445,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "124:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "But by the later century, sometime",
          "offset": 7448,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "124:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "around 577, according to one reading of",
          "offset": 7451,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "124:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "the sources, the combined armies of",
          "offset": 7454,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "124:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yuran, Red of Alt Clute, and three kings",
          "offset": 7457,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "124:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "named Gowac, Gualawag perhaps of Elmet,",
          "offset": 7460,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "124:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Morant, maybe of Gdothin, assembled",
          "offset": 7464,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "124:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "for an assault of Benia.",
          "offset": 7468,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "124:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "But who really was Yurion? And can",
          "offset": 7474,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "124:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "archaeological evidence of his rule be",
          "offset": 7477,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "124:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "found?",
          "offset": 7479,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "124:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Well, his kingdom has long remained a",
          "offset": 7481,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "124:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "mystery. But there is archaeology in the",
          "offset": 7483,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "124:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "Old North.",
          "offset": 7486,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "124:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Not exactly where historians have often",
          "offset": 7489,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "124:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "looked, but in the Old North",
          "offset": 7491,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "124:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "nonetheless.",
          "offset": 7493,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "124:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Reg lacks archaeology.",
          "offset": 7496,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "124:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "These archaeological sites lack history.",
          "offset": 7499,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "124:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just maybe they are one and the same.",
          "offset": 7503,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "125:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 7512,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "125:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "50 mi west of Carlilele, rising up over",
          "offset": 7517,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "125:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Sway FTH, where the river flows down",
          "offset": 7521,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "125:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "to the sea, a hill fort stands sentinel",
          "offset": 7524,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "125:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "on the landscape.",
          "offset": 7527,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "125:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "It's a tiny site. Nothing on the vast",
          "offset": 7529,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "125:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "citadels of the south.",
          "offset": 7532,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "125:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet, as early as the 1890s, shards",
          "offset": 7535,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "125:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "of e-wear pottery were found here,",
          "offset": 7538,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "125:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "indicating extensive trade links with",
          "offset": 7541,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "125:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "the faroff European mainland.",
          "offset": 7543,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "125:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "In 1913, metal work, glass vessels, and",
          "offset": 7546,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "125:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet more pottery originating in Gaul was",
          "offset": 7551,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "125:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "found.",
          "offset": 7554,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "125:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though the place was then thought to",
          "offset": 7557,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "125:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "have been occupied in the 8th or 9th",
          "offset": 7559,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "125:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "centuries,",
          "offset": 7561,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "126:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "at the time no hilltop settlements from",
          "offset": 7563,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "126:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "the early medieval period had been",
          "offset": 7566,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "126:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "found, still thought of as an entirely",
          "offset": 7568,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "126:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "dark age.",
          "offset": 7570,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "126:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "Then in the 1950s and60s, a series of",
          "offset": 7573,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "126:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "astonishing finds at Cadbury Castle,",
          "offset": 7577,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "126:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Dennis Pace, and elsewhere changed this",
          "offset": 7580,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "126:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "perception for good.",
          "offset": 7583,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "126:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "When the motive mark was thoroughly",
          "offset": 7586,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "126:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "re-exavated in the 1970s by Lloyd Lang",
          "offset": 7588,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "126:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "and David Longley, it was definitively",
          "offset": 7591,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "126:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "proven that the place had been fortified",
          "offset": 7594,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "126:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the sixth century with trade",
          "offset": 7597,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "126:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "continuing until the mid to later 7th",
          "offset": 7600,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "126:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "century.",
          "offset": 7603,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "126:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "A connection to the nearby population",
          "offset": 7605,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "126:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "center at Witthorn was also established,",
          "offset": 7607,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "126:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "the site of an important monastic center",
          "offset": 7610,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "126:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "associated with St. Ninian.",
          "offset": 7613,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "126:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "Apparently, the two sites being supplied",
          "offset": 7616,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "126:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "and frequented by the same merchants.",
          "offset": 7618,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "126:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet, the motive of Mark wasn't",
          "offset": 7623,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "127:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "necessarily a high status settlement,",
          "offset": 7625,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "127:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps being the home of a master",
          "offset": 7629,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "127:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "craftsman and his family and followers.",
          "offset": 7631,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "127:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "It's a site reminiscent of the story of",
          "offset": 7636,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "127:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Wayland the smithy and the Welsh story",
          "offset": 7639,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "127:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Kullik and Olwin which both suggest",
          "offset": 7642,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "127:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "the activities of smiths and jewelers",
          "offset": 7645,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "127:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "were richly rewarded and highly regarded",
          "offset": 7648,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "127:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 7653,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "127:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "like bards perhaps integral to the power",
          "offset": 7654,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "127:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "of kings.",
          "offset": 7657,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "127:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "They often lived and worked somewhere",
          "offset": 7660,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "127:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "outside of regular society and moved to",
          "offset": 7662,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "127:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "where the pay would be best.",
          "offset": 7665,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "127:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "So a royal capital this was not but a",
          "offset": 7670,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "127:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "stronghold of regg.",
          "offset": 7674,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "127:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "The hunt continued for a stronghold fit",
          "offset": 7678,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "127:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "for a king.",
          "offset": 7681,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "128:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 7684,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "128:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "In 2012, another hilltop in Galloway was",
          "offset": 7688,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "128:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "excavated.",
          "offset": 7692,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "128:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Firmly situated in the old territory of",
          "offset": 7694,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "128:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Selgave, a people who'd fiercely",
          "offset": 7697,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "128:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "resisted Rome.",
          "offset": 7700,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "128:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "At 72 m tall, it's not the most",
          "offset": 7702,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "128:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "prominent summit in the area, resting on",
          "offset": 7705,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "128:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "a craggy null in Galloway's Ballland",
          "offset": 7708,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "128:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hills further to the west of the motive",
          "offset": 7710,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "128:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Mark,",
          "offset": 7712,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "128:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "but it is significantly larger than its",
          "offset": 7715,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "128:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "neighbor, more akin to the strongholds",
          "offset": 7718,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "128:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "at Edinburgh and Dumbartan Rock.",
          "offset": 7721,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "128:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Today the landscape is overgrown in",
          "offset": 7727,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "128:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "scrub and heather and until recently the",
          "offset": 7729,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "128:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "place was known for its ramparts",
          "offset": 7733,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "128:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "generally thought to be iron age in",
          "offset": 7735,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "128:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "construction along with an unusual pish",
          "offset": 7737,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "128:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "carving stone",
          "offset": 7740,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "129:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "etched on the exposed bedrock at the",
          "offset": 7744,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "129:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "entrance to the fort",
          "offset": 7746,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "129:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "depicting sea monsters and warriors.",
          "offset": 7748,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "129:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Similar carvings have also been found at",
          "offset": 7752,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "129:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Edinburgh and the Dalriartan stronghold",
          "offset": 7755,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "129:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Dunad.",
          "offset": 7757,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "129:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Neither of them Pictish strongholds.",
          "offset": 7759,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "129:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless, Trusty's Hill has often",
          "offset": 7762,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "129:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "been suggested to be an outlying Pictish",
          "offset": 7764,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "129:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "fort built by a victorious war band.",
          "offset": 7767,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "129:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Perhaps",
          "offset": 7770,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "129:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "the truth may have been very different.",
          "offset": 7772,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "129:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "The chronology revealed in 2012 lined up",
          "offset": 7775,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "129:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "perfectly with the Old North. the place",
          "offset": 7778,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "129:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "being occupied between 375 and 710.",
          "offset": 7781,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "129:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "Like most other contemporary forts,",
          "offset": 7787,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "129:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "there had been habitation here before",
          "offset": 7790,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "129:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Romans, and when they left, once",
          "offset": 7792,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "129:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "more.",
          "offset": 7795,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "129:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "There is now a good argument for",
          "offset": 7799,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "129:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "Trusty's Hill being a site of royal",
          "offset": 7801,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "130:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "inauguration,",
          "offset": 7804,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "130:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "just maybe for the kings of Regg.",
          "offset": 7806,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "130:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "It's a pretty big leap, but just maybe",
          "offset": 7810,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "130:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "the most famous of all, Yuran.",
          "offset": 7812,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "130:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "After all, an abundance of early",
          "offset": 7817,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "130:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "medieval material has been found in",
          "offset": 7819,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "130:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Galloway compared to little in Cumbria.",
          "offset": 7821,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "130:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "The place also has more fertile",
          "offset": 7826,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "130:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "agricultural land and strategic access",
          "offset": 7828,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "130:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "to all sides of the Irish Sea. A better",
          "offset": 7831,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "130:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "region to hold court from perhaps with",
          "offset": 7834,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "130:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "military outposts further a field.",
          "offset": 7837,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "130:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 7840,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "130:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Like at the motive of Mark, smelting",
          "offset": 7845,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "130:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "slag suggests workshops creating high",
          "offset": 7847,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "130:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "status metal work, though only tiny",
          "offset": 7850,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "130:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "pieces have survived.",
          "offset": 7853,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "130:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 7857,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "130:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Evidence of continental trade has also",
          "offset": 7858,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "130:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "been found. Whoever ruled this place",
          "offset": 7861,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "131:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "enjoying trade links as far away as",
          "offset": 7863,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "131:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ireland, the aisle of man, Meaveiian",
          "offset": 7865,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "131:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Gaul, and the faroff Mediterranean.",
          "offset": 7868,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "131:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 7871,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "131:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "And it isn't just pictish influence that",
          "offset": 7874,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "131:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "can be seen here, but Germanic, too,",
          "offset": 7876,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "131:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "giving tantalizing clues that Regg may",
          "offset": 7880,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "131:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "have been more Anglian before the",
          "offset": 7883,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "131:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "conquest than we realize.",
          "offset": 7885,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "131:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Free booting mercenaries operating here,",
          "offset": 7888,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "131:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps.",
          "offset": 7890,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "131:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 7892,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "131:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "And what did this kingdom look like?",
          "offset": 7894,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "131:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Well, it bears little resemblance at all",
          "offset": 7897,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "131:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "to the Roman or late antique world where",
          "offset": 7900,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "131:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Romanitas continued in some form.",
          "offset": 7902,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "131:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "This was a renegotiated power base for a",
          "offset": 7906,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "131:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Celtic people",
          "offset": 7909,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "131:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the context of recovery and a new",
          "offset": 7912,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "131:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "order rather than the continuation of",
          "offset": 7914,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "131:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "the old.",
          "offset": 7917,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "131:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "And even further west, we have yet",
          "offset": 7922,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "132:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "another site far more mysterious as it's",
          "offset": 7924,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "132:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "never been excavated,",
          "offset": 7928,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "132:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "but proposed by many as a hill fort with",
          "offset": 7931,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "132:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "early medieval habitation.",
          "offset": 7934,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "132:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Today, Dun Ragget sits overgrown, almost",
          "offset": 7942,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "132:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "entirely forgotten, save the adjacent",
          "offset": 7946,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "132:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "village, which bears an uncanny",
          "offset": 7949,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "132:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "resemblance to the kingdoms of the Old",
          "offset": 7951,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "132:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "North.",
          "offset": 7954,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "132:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "What happened here, we just don't know.",
          "offset": 7959,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "132:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Until it's excavated, it's a mystery.",
          "offset": 7962,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "132:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "Archaeologists, let's get this place",
          "offset": 7968,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "132:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "excavated.",
          "offset": 7971,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "132:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 7972,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "132:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "If you want to learn more about these",
          "offset": 7976,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "132:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "hill forts and many more all over",
          "offset": 7978,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "132:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain, I have a series on my other",
          "offset": 7980,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "133:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "channel where I go and visit them to",
          "offset": 7982,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "133:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "have a look for myself. Go check it out",
          "offset": 7984,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "133:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "here after you finish this video. And",
          "offset": 7987,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "133:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "don't forget to subscribe.",
          "offset": 7989,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "133:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "What became of this land? Well, it",
          "offset": 7994,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "133:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "doesn't look great. By the 7th century,",
          "offset": 7997,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "133:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "both the moat of Mark and Trusty's Hill",
          "offset": 8000,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "133:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "were destroyed by fire.",
          "offset": 8003,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "133:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "The ramparts torn down and demolished.",
          "offset": 8009,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "133:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Soon afterwards, the motive of Mark",
          "offset": 8016,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "133:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "would be reoccupied. And tellingly,",
          "offset": 8018,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "133:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglian runic inscriptions have been",
          "offset": 8021,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "133:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "found etched on bones.",
          "offset": 8023,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "133:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "Which brings us back to the siege of",
          "offset": 8027,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "133:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "Lindesvan.",
          "offset": 8030,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "133:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the written sources, we're told that",
          "offset": 8036,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "133:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "five kings succeeded as rulers of Benia.",
          "offset": 8038,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "133:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Four of them his sons",
          "offset": 8043,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "134:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "and another called Hassa.",
          "offset": 8045,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "134:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nius tells us that it was Hussa who",
          "offset": 8048,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "134:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "ruled at the time of the siege, though",
          "offset": 8050,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "134:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "it may even be that two rival groups now",
          "offset": 8053,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "134:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "held power. One at Bambra and the other",
          "offset": 8056,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "134:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "at Lindesvan.",
          "offset": 8059,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "134:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "And so for three days and three nights,",
          "offset": 8063,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "134:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "the British army laid siege to the",
          "offset": 8065,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "134:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "island.",
          "offset": 8068,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "134:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "But ultimately, the campaign would end",
          "offset": 8071,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "134:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "in disaster.",
          "offset": 8073,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "134:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "We're told Yurion was betrayed. murdered",
          "offset": 8075,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "134:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "by Loven, an agent of King Morcant,",
          "offset": 8078,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "134:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "jealous and wary of his power,",
          "offset": 8085,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "134:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "or attempting to overthrow the",
          "offset": 8088,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "134:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "overlordship of Regath.",
          "offset": 8090,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "134:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "This betrayal and untimely death has led",
          "offset": 8093,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "134:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "many scholars to suggest Yurion as an",
          "offset": 8096,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "134:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "integral inspiration for the eventual",
          "offset": 8099,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "134:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "King Arthur legend.",
          "offset": 8101,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "135:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the years that followed, the",
          "offset": 8108,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "135:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "situation told of by the poets is of",
          "offset": 8110,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "135:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "squabbbling and war,",
          "offset": 8112,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "135:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "allowing the Anglians time to not only",
          "offset": 8115,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "135:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "survive, but regain their strength.",
          "offset": 8118,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "135:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8121,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "135:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yurian's kinsmen, Luark, sings of the",
          "offset": 8123,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "135:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "king's sons being attacked by their",
          "offset": 8126,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "135:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "father's enemies.",
          "offset": 8128,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "135:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Morant, Gualawag, and Dunard the Stout,",
          "offset": 8131,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "135:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps reflecting the decline of Reggie",
          "offset": 8135,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "135:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the early 7th century.",
          "offset": 8138,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "135:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yurian's son Owen, also a famed figure",
          "offset": 8141,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "135:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "in his own right, may have continued the",
          "offset": 8144,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "135:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "struggle for a time, but was himself",
          "offset": 8146,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "135:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "killed.",
          "offset": 8149,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "135:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Anglians ever advancing onwards.",
          "offset": 8151,
          "duration": 13,
          "formattedTime": "135:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8154,
          "duration": 12,
          "formattedTime": "135:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though often portrayed as contemporaries",
          "offset": 8163,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "136:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "living in the same age, Ana and Tasin in",
          "offset": 8166,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "136:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "fact may not have been.",
          "offset": 8170,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "136:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tileasin sings the praises of courtly",
          "offset": 8175,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "136:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "life and all powerful battling kings of",
          "offset": 8178,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "136:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "the mid6th century.",
          "offset": 8180,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "136:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "a buoyant, exuberant age.",
          "offset": 8185,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "136:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "The good times.",
          "offset": 8189,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "136:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anarin's work, on the other hand, is",
          "offset": 8196,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "136:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "almost entirely wistful,",
          "offset": 8198,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "136:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "lamenting the loss of more recent times.",
          "offset": 8202,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "136:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "Allergies for dead kings,",
          "offset": 8209,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "136:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "the faded glory of the recent past.",
          "offset": 8212,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "136:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "Thought to have been sung into existence",
          "offset": 8220,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "137:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the early years of the 7th century.",
          "offset": 8222,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "137:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "They lament a dying world.",
          "offset": 8226,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "137:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "And Anarin's work isn't alone, of",
          "offset": 8233,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "137:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "course. An anonymous song from the red",
          "offset": 8236,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "137:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "book of Hergist is thought to date from",
          "offset": 8239,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "137:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "around this time, too.",
          "offset": 8242,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "137:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8244,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "137:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the poem, we're told of a solitary",
          "offset": 8250,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "137:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "bard wandering the wilderness.",
          "offset": 8253,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "137:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8258,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "137:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Once regailed in the halls of kings, he",
          "offset": 8259,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "137:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "now goes by the wilder ways.",
          "offset": 8262,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "137:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "Following old paths through overgrown",
          "offset": 8268,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "137:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "meadows, over hills and forest gullies.",
          "offset": 8270,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "137:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "Crows and beasts his only companions.",
          "offset": 8277,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "137:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Finally, our fugitive spies a ruined",
          "offset": 8283,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "138:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "wall in the distance.",
          "offset": 8286,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "138:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Flanked by vinyl laden masonry, the now",
          "offset": 8290,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "138:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "collapsed roof of a great hall rises up",
          "offset": 8294,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "138:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "on his approach.",
          "offset": 8297,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "138:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Overgrown with nettles, empty,",
          "offset": 8303,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "138:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "bereft of its protector, just the same",
          "offset": 8309,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "138:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "as the countryside around.",
          "offset": 8312,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "138:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "He is walking in the king's fortress.",
          "offset": 8316,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "138:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "No one lives there now. Home only to",
          "offset": 8320,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "138:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "pigeons and baying wolves.",
          "offset": 8323,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "138:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "But the morning bard has a purpose. He",
          "offset": 8327,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "138:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "has come here for a reason.",
          "offset": 8331,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "138:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "He has on his person the head of the",
          "offset": 8335,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "138:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "great king.",
          "offset": 8338,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "138:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "mouth spattered with foaming blood.",
          "offset": 8343,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "139:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Brought back to the hallowed halls of",
          "offset": 8347,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "139:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "his ancestors.",
          "offset": 8349,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "139:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sent home.",
          "offset": 8351,
          "duration": 12,
          "formattedTime": "139:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8353,
          "duration": 12,
          "formattedTime": "139:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "The passage has long intrigued scholars,",
          "offset": 8363,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "139:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "for the bringing home of the head of a",
          "offset": 8366,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "139:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "slain prince is known to have been a",
          "offset": 8368,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "139:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "traditional pagan ritual amongst the",
          "offset": 8370,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "139:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Celtic peoples.",
          "offset": 8373,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "139:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "Unfortunately, whether this is a genuine",
          "offset": 8377,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "139:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Celtic leftover or a later addition, we",
          "offset": 8380,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "139:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "can't be sure,",
          "offset": 8383,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "139:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "but the passage is thought to be old.",
          "offset": 8387,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "139:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Another mention by the poet Luark",
          "offset": 8394,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "139:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "mentions Yurian's decapitation too. And",
          "offset": 8397,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "139:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet is also called the Lord of",
          "offset": 8400,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "140:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Christrysendom in other sections.",
          "offset": 8404,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "140:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "But who's to say these heavily Christian",
          "offset": 8408,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "140:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "epithets aren't later additions?",
          "offset": 8410,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "140:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "After all, Yurion, like KingWendelo of",
          "offset": 8416,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "140:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "After, was one of the three bull",
          "offset": 8419,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "140:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "protectors of Britain.",
          "offset": 8421,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "140:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "And other references in regards to him",
          "offset": 8424,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "140:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "are made to malevolent, otherworldly",
          "offset": 8426,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "140:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "birds.",
          "offset": 8429,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "140:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Across the sea in Ireland, a land",
          "offset": 8434,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "140:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "traditionally thought to have been",
          "offset": 8437,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "140:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "mostly Christian by this point, high",
          "offset": 8439,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "140:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "kings were still occasionally pagan.",
          "offset": 8442,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "140:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "with pagan burial practices certainly",
          "offset": 8446,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "140:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "surviving until the late 7th century.",
          "offset": 8448,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "140:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "And in 569, a similar written mention of",
          "offset": 8452,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "140:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "pre-Christian traditions is found too",
          "offset": 8456,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "140:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "when King Dermit was slain by Hugh Duff",
          "offset": 8458,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "140:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Maxwain at Wrath. His body was interred",
          "offset": 8461,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "141:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "in Conry, but his head was sent",
          "offset": 8464,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "141:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "elsewhere",
          "offset": 8467,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "141:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "to Clon Viknos as he requested himself.",
          "offset": 8471,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "141:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "Indeed, the picss would hold on to their",
          "offset": 8478,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "141:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "pagan beliefs for much longer.",
          "offset": 8480,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "141:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8484,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "141:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "So why not at least some of the Britons",
          "offset": 8486,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "141:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "north of Hadrien's wall?",
          "offset": 8488,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "141:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless, by the year 600, the",
          "offset": 8494,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "141:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "British alliance had failed.",
          "offset": 8497,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "141:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yurion was dead and a new order arising.",
          "offset": 8500,
          "duration": 11,
          "formattedTime": "141:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8505,
          "duration": 10,
          "formattedTime": "141:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Until the 590s, the northern Britons had",
          "offset": 8512,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "141:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "largely escaped the calamities",
          "offset": 8515,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "141:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "experienced by their southern neighbors.",
          "offset": 8517,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "141:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Their wars were amongst themselves,",
          "offset": 8521,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "142:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "managing to hold their own against",
          "offset": 8525,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "142:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "picss, Irish, and Anglians alike.",
          "offset": 8527,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "142:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "But soon enough, this would change.",
          "offset": 8531,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "142:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8536,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "142:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just as the Britain fragmented back into",
          "offset": 8538,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "142:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "waring states again after the death of",
          "offset": 8541,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "142:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yurion, a new warlord arose to lead the",
          "offset": 8542,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "142:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "usually quarrelome angles of the eastern",
          "offset": 8546,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "142:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "coast.",
          "offset": 8549,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "142:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8551,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "142:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "With a fury to match that of Eda the",
          "offset": 8554,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "142:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Flamebringer,",
          "offset": 8557,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "142:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "this new warlord had risen to the top of",
          "offset": 8558,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "142:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "the pile.",
          "offset": 8561,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "142:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "One of those rare, seemingly unstoppable",
          "offset": 8566,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "142:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "figures of history,",
          "offset": 8568,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "142:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "arising from a dynasty which usually",
          "offset": 8571,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "142:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "killed its kings every few years.",
          "offset": 8573,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "142:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Twister, they called him.",
          "offset": 8576,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "142:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "We know him as Ethelf.",
          "offset": 8580,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "142:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "And he was destined to change everything",
          "offset": 8582,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "143:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the space of a single generation.",
          "offset": 8585,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "143:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "And with a new age comes a new foremost",
          "offset": 8589,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "143:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "poet.",
          "offset": 8592,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "143:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Whereas Talasin had praised the deeds of",
          "offset": 8594,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "143:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "the men of the north, singing of their",
          "offset": 8596,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "143:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "glorious victories in battle. Our source",
          "offset": 8598,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "143:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "for this age is an Aaron.",
          "offset": 8601,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "143:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "He writes with sadness.",
          "offset": 8605,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "143:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "for his was the twilight time",
          "offset": 8608,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "143:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Katra.",
          "offset": 8613,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "143:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8615,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "143:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Snowonia is one of the most starkly",
          "offset": 8632,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "143:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "beautiful landscapes in all of Britain.",
          "offset": 8634,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "143:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet it is a place a wash with the memory",
          "offset": 8642,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "144:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the past too.",
          "offset": 8644,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "144:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the 9inth and 10th centuries, we know",
          "offset": 8647,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "144:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "bars and wandering poets walked these",
          "offset": 8650,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "144:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "hills,",
          "offset": 8653,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "144:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "traveling from hall to hall to tell",
          "offset": 8655,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "144:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "their tales,",
          "offset": 8657,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "144:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "derived from the rich tradition of",
          "offset": 8659,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "144:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "heroic poetry and storytelling, so much",
          "offset": 8661,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "144:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "a part of Welsh culture,",
          "offset": 8664,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "144:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "retelling the tales of the very best of",
          "offset": 8668,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "144:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "them,",
          "offset": 8671,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "144:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the giants and ancient Celtic kings.",
          "offset": 8672,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "144:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "But most of all of the heroes of just a",
          "offset": 8678,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "144:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "few centuries before",
          "offset": 8681,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "144:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "men like Yurion and Arthur.",
          "offset": 8684,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "144:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "One of the most famous tales of all,",
          "offset": 8689,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "144:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "however, doesn't sing the deeds of",
          "offset": 8691,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "144:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "either of these figures.",
          "offset": 8693,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "144:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8695,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "144:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "It's a tragic elegy to celebrate a",
          "offset": 8698,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "144:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "doomed last charge of the men of the",
          "offset": 8701,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "145:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "North.",
          "offset": 8704,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "145:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "One final offensive to fight back the",
          "offset": 8706,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "145:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "invaders once and for all or die trying.",
          "offset": 8708,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "145:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Still celebrated today, we know it as",
          "offset": 8713,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "145:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Gdovin.",
          "offset": 8716,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "145:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8718,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "145:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Today, Edinburgh is one of the great",
          "offset": 8732,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "145:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "cities of Britain,",
          "offset": 8734,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "145:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "a sprawling metropolis, worldrenowned",
          "offset": 8736,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "145:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "center of culture and gateway to the",
          "offset": 8740,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "145:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "north.",
          "offset": 8742,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "145:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8743,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "145:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "1,400 years ago, it looked very",
          "offset": 8755,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "145:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "different.",
          "offset": 8758,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "145:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "For back then this was a rural landscape",
          "offset": 8760,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "145:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "ruled over by the ancient Britain of",
          "offset": 8763,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "146:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "old, never conquered by Rome.",
          "offset": 8766,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "146:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Underneath the towered walls of the",
          "offset": 8774,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "146:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "castle rock, the remains of thousands of",
          "offset": 8776,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "146:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "years of continual occupation have been",
          "offset": 8779,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "146:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "found.",
          "offset": 8781,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "146:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "And though much smaller than the nearby",
          "offset": 8783,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "146:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "stronghold at Trapane Law, this is",
          "offset": 8785,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "146:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "thought to have been at least a capital",
          "offset": 8788,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "146:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the Gdovin.",
          "offset": 8790,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "146:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8793,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "146:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "And as time went on and trapin law was",
          "offset": 8795,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "146:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "abandoned by the end of the fifth",
          "offset": 8797,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "146:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "century, the most important of all,",
          "offset": 8799,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "146:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "once a vast sprawling high kingship,",
          "offset": 8807,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "146:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "many scholars think the heartlands of",
          "offset": 8811,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "146:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "Dea and Benia, both British names, had",
          "offset": 8812,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "146:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "once been under Gdin overlordship.",
          "offset": 8816,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "146:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "By the year 600, though, all that had",
          "offset": 8820,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "147:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "come to an end.",
          "offset": 8823,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "147:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet the kings here still wielded power",
          "offset": 8827,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "147:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "over their neighbors.",
          "offset": 8830,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "147:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "For some time around that year, Anarin",
          "offset": 8832,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "147:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "sings of a great mustering to the king.",
          "offset": 8836,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "147:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alongside the household warriors of King",
          "offset": 8844,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "147:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mindog, we're told the assembled",
          "offset": 8847,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "147:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "warriors came from all the lands of the",
          "offset": 8849,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "147:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "northern British.",
          "offset": 8852,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "147:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "Gdin Altcloot",
          "offset": 8854,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "147:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Reggv Elmet",
          "offset": 8857,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "147:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "and from Wales, too. Penguin,",
          "offset": 8860,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "147:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Pois Gwennneth.",
          "offset": 8864,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "147:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "And we're given stranger names, too,",
          "offset": 8868,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "147:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "that can't be placed geographically.",
          "offset": 8871,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "147:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "Men from Green Uffin,",
          "offset": 8874,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "147:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8876,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "147:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Pictish warriors from beyond the fourth,",
          "offset": 8880,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "148:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Irishmen too.",
          "offset": 8883,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "148:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8887,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "148:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "300 of them in all, all young freed men,",
          "offset": 8888,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "148:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "aristocrats, even perhaps accompanied by",
          "offset": 8892,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "148:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "their own war bands and shieldbearers.",
          "offset": 8895,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "148:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "All had come to pledge their loyalty to",
          "offset": 8901,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "148:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "the king for one last battle against the",
          "offset": 8904,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "148:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "English.",
          "offset": 8907,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "148:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8909,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "148:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mentog the rich feasted the men for over",
          "offset": 8911,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "148:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "a year.",
          "offset": 8914,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "148:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though he wouldn't lead the attack",
          "offset": 8918,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "148:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself, he seems to have been too old",
          "offset": 8920,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "148:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "for battle and stayed in his hall. The",
          "offset": 8922,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "148:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "force was to be led by three kings.",
          "offset": 8926,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "148:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps his sons, Kinry, Kynan, and",
          "offset": 8929,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "148:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "Kinra.",
          "offset": 8933,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "148:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8935,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "148:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "An Aaron individualizes 80 of the men.",
          "offset": 8938,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "148:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Heroes to those gathered around",
          "offset": 8942,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "149:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "listening to the tale in years to come.",
          "offset": 8944,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "149:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Perhaps sometimes figures they'd",
          "offset": 8948,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "149:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "recognize from other stories. each given",
          "offset": 8950,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "149:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "an immortalizing description.",
          "offset": 8953,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "149:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Like Karadog who rushed into battle, a",
          "offset": 8958,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "149:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "wild boar, an armed bull, killer of",
          "offset": 8961,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "149:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "three kings, he fed wolves by his hand.",
          "offset": 8964,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "149:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 8969,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "149:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Owen who wore a coat of male over",
          "offset": 8971,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "149:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "his crimson undershirt and is also",
          "offset": 8974,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "149:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "described as wearing multicolored armor",
          "offset": 8976,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "149:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Blaine beautiful he burned in gold",
          "offset": 8981,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "149:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "and purple riding his well-fed horses",
          "offset": 8984,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "149:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "and an Aaron stresses that these most",
          "offset": 8991,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "149:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "renowned men of their day rode as a",
          "offset": 8993,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "149:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "cavalry army just maybe harking back to",
          "offset": 8996,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "149:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "tactics from the late Roman world.",
          "offset": 8999,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "149:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "After all, we know Anglo-Saxon helmets",
          "offset": 9004,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "150:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "reserved only for elite soldiers and",
          "offset": 9007,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "150:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "kings, ultimately derived from those",
          "offset": 9010,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "150:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "once worn by late Roman soldiers.",
          "offset": 9013,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "150:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "So why not the Britain, too?",
          "offset": 9016,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "150:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "And so when the year had passed, the men",
          "offset": 9022,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "150:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "readied themselves to head south. a last",
          "offset": 9026,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "150:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "alliance to curb the advance of the",
          "offset": 9030,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "150:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglians. They rode out to war, to",
          "offset": 9032,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "150:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "death,",
          "offset": 9036,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "150:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "to Catre.",
          "offset": 9038,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "150:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 9044,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "150:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "And the location of the battle, well, we",
          "offset": 9048,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "150:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "don't know for certain, but many",
          "offset": 9051,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "150:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "historians see the town of Katarik as a",
          "offset": 9053,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "150:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "good bet.",
          "offset": 9056,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "150:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 9057,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "150:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just to the east of Stainmore in North",
          "offset": 9061,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "151:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yorkshire, Katarik had been an important",
          "offset": 9063,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "151:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Roman stronghold on the old road to the",
          "offset": 9066,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "151:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "north.",
          "offset": 9069,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "151:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "And though no archaeological evidence",
          "offset": 9073,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "151:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "has of yet been found, the place has",
          "offset": 9075,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "151:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "often been suggested to be an important",
          "offset": 9078,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "151:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "royal stronghold for Yuran in the later",
          "offset": 9080,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "151:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "6th century.",
          "offset": 9082,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "151:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "maybe even the location of the earlier",
          "offset": 9087,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "151:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "elegy from the red book of Hergus.",
          "offset": 9089,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "151:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Archaeology does suggest that York and",
          "offset": 9095,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "151:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "the entire surrounding area up to the",
          "offset": 9098,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "151:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "central hill country had fallen under",
          "offset": 9100,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "151:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglian sway by the end of the sixth",
          "offset": 9102,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "151:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "century.",
          "offset": 9105,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "151:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "A Germanic elite ruling over a mostly",
          "offset": 9106,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "151:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "British population perhaps.",
          "offset": 9109,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "151:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "And when Katarik and the surrounding",
          "offset": 9113,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "151:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "countryside fell in the aftermath of",
          "offset": 9115,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "151:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yurian's death, which we know it did,",
          "offset": 9117,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "151:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Anglians would have gained easy",
          "offset": 9121,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "152:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "access much further a field via the",
          "offset": 9123,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "152:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Roman road.",
          "offset": 9126,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "152:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "If the northern British were to survive,",
          "offset": 9130,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "152:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "the place had to be retaken.",
          "offset": 9132,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "152:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "And so the riders charged forth.",
          "offset": 9136,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "152:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 9143,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "152:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "What happens next, sung in halls in the",
          "offset": 9149,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "152:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "north and the west for hundreds of years",
          "offset": 9152,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "152:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "to come, is a classic tale of heroism",
          "offset": 9154,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "152:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "and sacrifice.",
          "offset": 9157,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "152:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 9161,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "152:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "Said to have been opposed by a wildly",
          "offset": 9167,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "152:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "exaggerated number of a 100,000",
          "offset": 9169,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "152:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "warriors,",
          "offset": 9172,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "152:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "the 300 British war leaders, probably",
          "offset": 9173,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "152:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "supported by their own subordinates,",
          "offset": 9176,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "152:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "soon made it to the old Roman ruins.",
          "offset": 9178,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "152:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Still an impressive site after its",
          "offset": 9183,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "153:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "abandonment just over a hundred years",
          "offset": 9185,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "153:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "earlier.",
          "offset": 9187,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "153:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "But of course, the Germanic shield wall",
          "offset": 9190,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "153:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "proved too strong.",
          "offset": 9193,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "153:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "All the might of the Britons was not",
          "offset": 9195,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "153:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "enough.",
          "offset": 9198,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "153:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "An Aaron, who may have actually been",
          "offset": 9201,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "153:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "present at the battle, composing the",
          "offset": 9203,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "153:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "tale just a few years later, also claims",
          "offset": 9205,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "153:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "to have been the only survivor.",
          "offset": 9208,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "153:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "The 300 warriors, all riding to their",
          "offset": 9214,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "153:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "doom.",
          "offset": 9217,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "153:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Within a generation of the defeat,",
          "offset": 9225,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "153:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "mentioned as one of the atrocious",
          "offset": 9227,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "153:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "assassinations of the island of Britain",
          "offset": 9229,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "153:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the Welsh triads, Gaddin and Elmet",
          "offset": 9231,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "153:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "would come to an end.",
          "offset": 9236,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "153:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "Reg would soon follow.",
          "offset": 9238,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "153:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet the tale would continue to",
          "offset": 9244,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "154:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "inspire generation after generation of",
          "offset": 9247,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "154:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britons and Welshmen",
          "offset": 9249,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "154:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "from Kadwallan to Rodri the Great. Two",
          "offset": 9252,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "154:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "kings who both eventually met their ends",
          "offset": 9255,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "154:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "on the battlefield against Anglo-Saxon",
          "offset": 9258,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "154:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "foes.",
          "offset": 9260,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "154:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "But who was the Anglian war leader at",
          "offset": 9268,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "154:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Catra?",
          "offset": 9270,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "154:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Well, we don't know for sure. Geography",
          "offset": 9272,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "154:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "would suggest a dayun contingent, still",
          "offset": 9276,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "154:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "independent from the Benissians of",
          "offset": 9279,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "154:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Bambra at the time. And yet, Ethelfr, or",
          "offset": 9280,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "154:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "at least a subruler under his command,",
          "offset": 9285,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "154:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "still stands out as the most likely",
          "offset": 9288,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "154:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "figure.",
          "offset": 9290,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "154:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "After all, soon enough he would rule",
          "offset": 9293,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "154:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "both kingdoms.",
          "offset": 9296,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "154:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "It's even been suggested that the battle",
          "offset": 9300,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "155:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "took place slightly earlier under",
          "offset": 9302,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "155:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethelf's father, Ethel, or even",
          "offset": 9305,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "155:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Theodoric, Urian's archeneemy.",
          "offset": 9309,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "155:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Unfortunately, we simply don't know.",
          "offset": 9313,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "155:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Much like British leaders generally",
          "offset": 9316,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "155:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "didn't concern later English chronicers,",
          "offset": 9318,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "155:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglians didn't concern the British.",
          "offset": 9321,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "155:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "But thankfully for us, by the beginning",
          "offset": 9328,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "155:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the 7th century, this period finally",
          "offset": 9331,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "155:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "begins to emerge onto the pages of",
          "offset": 9334,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "155:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "history.",
          "offset": 9336,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "155:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "For literacy and recordkeeping were on",
          "offset": 9339,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "155:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "the rise.",
          "offset": 9342,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "155:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "Whoever the Anglian leader was at Catra,",
          "offset": 9346,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "155:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "the damage had been done.",
          "offset": 9349,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "155:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Anglians around York wouldn't be",
          "offset": 9352,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "155:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "dislodged. Not now.",
          "offset": 9354,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "155:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "And within a few decades, now in firm",
          "offset": 9358,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "155:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "control of all the lowland areas of the",
          "offset": 9360,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "156:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "West, that even begin moving from the",
          "offset": 9362,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "156:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "cattle corrals of the countryside into",
          "offset": 9365,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "156:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "urban Roman halls.",
          "offset": 9367,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "156:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 9371,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "156:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "Within just three decades, King Edwin",
          "offset": 9372,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "156:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "would be baptized at York,",
          "offset": 9375,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "156:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "though they would become no less",
          "offset": 9378,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "156:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "warlike.",
          "offset": 9381,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "156:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Britons were pushed west over the",
          "offset": 9385,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "156:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "hills into rougher, more land.",
          "offset": 9387,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "156:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Never again would they push the English",
          "offset": 9391,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "156:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "back, now in control of all the lowland",
          "offset": 9394,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "156:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "fertile areas.",
          "offset": 9397,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "156:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet from the north, yet another",
          "offset": 9402,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "156:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "power was arising.",
          "offset": 9405,
          "duration": 13,
          "formattedTime": "156:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 9407,
          "duration": 14,
          "formattedTime": "156:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the year 574,",
          "offset": 9418,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "156:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "so says the Irish monk Adaman.",
          "offset": 9421,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "157:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "A new king came to power in the Gaelic",
          "offset": 9425,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "157:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sea Kingdom of Daliata,",
          "offset": 9428,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "157:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "striding up the staked ramparts of",
          "offset": 9435,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "157:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Dunad, mightiest fortress in the",
          "offset": 9437,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "157:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Northlands,",
          "offset": 9440,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "157:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "just as his ancestors had done before",
          "offset": 9442,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "157:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "him since they crossed over the waves",
          "offset": 9444,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "157:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "from Ireland in the preceding centuries.",
          "offset": 9446,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "157:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "He would undergo the traditional rituals",
          "offset": 9449,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "157:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "of inauguration at the Kingstone.",
          "offset": 9452,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "157:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "The assembled lords of the islands",
          "offset": 9457,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "157:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "amassed around him.",
          "offset": 9460,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "157:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "For Aiden Mgabrain was a descendant of",
          "offset": 9464,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "157:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nile of the Nine Hostages, semi-leendary",
          "offset": 9467,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "157:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "progenitor of a slew of royal houses",
          "offset": 9471,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "157:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "who'd lived sometime in the fourth or",
          "offset": 9474,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "157:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "fifth centuries.",
          "offset": 9476,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "157:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "A figure who'd changed the political",
          "offset": 9479,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "157:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "system in Ireland for good,",
          "offset": 9482,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "158:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "revolutionizing the old power structures",
          "offset": 9485,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "158:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "by looking outside of the island, not",
          "offset": 9487,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "158:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "within,",
          "offset": 9490,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "158:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "ravaging seashores far and wide, gaining",
          "offset": 9494,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "158:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "great wealth and power in the process,",
          "offset": 9498,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "158:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps even taking part in the great",
          "offset": 9502,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "158:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "conspiracy of the barbarians spoken of",
          "offset": 9504,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "158:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the Roman sources. is",
          "offset": 9507,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "158:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "in those Roman sources, Irishmen were",
          "offset": 9512,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "158:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "often called cannibals.",
          "offset": 9515,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "158:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "And despite being Christian now since",
          "offset": 9518,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "158:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "the days of St. Patrick, some of those",
          "offset": 9520,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "158:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "pagan ways still clung on.",
          "offset": 9523,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "158:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "But of course, the succession was not",
          "offset": 9531,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "158:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "uncontested.",
          "offset": 9533,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "158:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "The previous king, Conal, had many sons",
          "offset": 9535,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "158:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "and relatives, all eager for power.",
          "offset": 9539,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "158:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Aiden, already nearing 40, would have to",
          "offset": 9543,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "159:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "pull every favor he could to secure the",
          "offset": 9546,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "159:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingship.",
          "offset": 9549,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "159:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "As far as Adam Nan was concerned, one",
          "offset": 9553,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "159:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "figure in particular acted as king maker",
          "offset": 9556,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "159:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "at this time.",
          "offset": 9558,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "159:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "We know him as Columbumber",
          "offset": 9560,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "159:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "and he is the center of Adam Naman's",
          "offset": 9564,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "159:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "story.",
          "offset": 9566,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "159:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Following the death of the previous king",
          "offset": 9570,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "159:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Conal Columba spent three days and",
          "offset": 9572,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "159:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "nights fasting on the tiny spit of Hima.",
          "offset": 9575,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "159:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "There he spoke to angels.",
          "offset": 9580,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "159:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "And when he returned to Dunad, he'd made",
          "offset": 9586,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "159:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "up his mind.",
          "offset": 9588,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "159:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "For by this time, after St. Patrick's",
          "offset": 9591,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "159:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "great influence on Irish society in the",
          "offset": 9593,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "159:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "fifth century, divine holy blessing went",
          "offset": 9595,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "159:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "hand in hand with kingship.",
          "offset": 9599,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "159:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "One of the first times in post Roman",
          "offset": 9604,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "160:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Europe that this had happened.",
          "offset": 9606,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "160:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Aiden wasn't just chosen by his kinsmen",
          "offset": 9608,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "160:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "and under kings, but by God himself.",
          "offset": 9611,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "160:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 9616,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "160:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "But this Christianity left a drift to",
          "offset": 9619,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "160:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "develop in the wild Atlantic for",
          "offset": 9621,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "160:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "hundreds of years was a far cry from the",
          "offset": 9623,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "160:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "orthodoxy preached in Rome.",
          "offset": 9626,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "160:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Now imbued by the kingstone, made",
          "offset": 9631,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "160:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "powerful by Christian magic, King Aiden",
          "offset": 9634,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "160:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "accompanied his kinsman Cola back to",
          "offset": 9638,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "160:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ireland to broker an alliance with the",
          "offset": 9640,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "160:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "assembled lords of the O'Neal.",
          "offset": 9643,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "160:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet more distant kinsmen descended from",
          "offset": 9648,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "160:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nile.",
          "offset": 9650,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "160:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "Then his southwestern borders secure.",
          "offset": 9653,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "160:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Almost immediately Aiden went to war.",
          "offset": 9656,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "160:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "This is the tale we get from history.",
          "offset": 9665,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "161:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Not strictly contemporary, but written",
          "offset": 9668,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "161:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the centuries immediately following",
          "offset": 9670,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "161:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "by people using sources entirely lost",
          "offset": 9673,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "161:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "today.",
          "offset": 9676,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "161:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet archaeology can be used to",
          "offset": 9678,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "161:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "corroborate much of the accounts too.",
          "offset": 9681,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "161:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "It seems that the heedes were indeed",
          "offset": 9686,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "161:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "populated from Ireland from the fourth",
          "offset": 9688,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "161:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "or even the 3rd century onwards.",
          "offset": 9690,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "161:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Like the rest of the western seabboard",
          "offset": 9694,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "161:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Britain by roaming warriors and",
          "offset": 9695,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "161:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "dynasties of kings.",
          "offset": 9698,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "161:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Here, the legendary hero Kakullan is",
          "offset": 9701,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "161:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "often linked to events, center of an",
          "offset": 9704,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "161:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "epic tale often called Ireland's Iliad.",
          "offset": 9707,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "161:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 9712,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "161:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "And centuries later, after so many",
          "offset": 9713,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "161:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "unrecorded events, by the sixth century,",
          "offset": 9716,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "161:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "a powerful confederacy of kin groups",
          "offset": 9719,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "161:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "held sway from Antrim to Argyle, Ireland",
          "offset": 9722,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "162:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "to the Hebdes.",
          "offset": 9726,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "162:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "numerous kin groups pledging allegiance",
          "offset": 9731,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "162:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "to one overking.",
          "offset": 9733,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "162:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "And by the sixth century, Dunad had",
          "offset": 9739,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "162:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "extensive trade links. More storage",
          "offset": 9742,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "162:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "vessels known as Ewear than anywhere",
          "offset": 9744,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "162:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "else in Britain have been found here,",
          "offset": 9746,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "162:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "indicating regular trade with the",
          "offset": 9750,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "162:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Bordeaux and Lir regions of France and",
          "offset": 9752,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "162:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "even the Mediterranean beyond.",
          "offset": 9755,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "162:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "loaded up with spices, wine, honey, and",
          "offset": 9760,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "162:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "salt. Interestingly, the pottery and",
          "offset": 9764,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "162:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "glass found here all comes from",
          "offset": 9767,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "162:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "overseas. They don't seem to have made",
          "offset": 9769,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "162:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "their own.",
          "offset": 9772,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "162:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was those sea roads to the south,",
          "offset": 9776,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "162:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "spanning the entire western seabboard of",
          "offset": 9778,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "162:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Europe and eventually penetrating deep",
          "offset": 9781,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "into the river systems that Columbus",
          "offset": 9783,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "spiritual descendants would use to",
          "offset": 9785,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "journey far and wide in the spreading of",
          "offset": 9788,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "their new faith",
          "offset": 9790,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "and their desire for knowledge.",
          "offset": 9792,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "For in the later sixth century, the",
          "offset": 9795,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "163:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "monks on Iona were some of the only",
          "offset": 9797,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "literate men in a mostly illiterate",
          "offset": 9800,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "163:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "world.",
          "offset": 9803,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "163:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet, hints of older traditions come",
          "offset": 9807,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "through too.",
          "offset": 9810,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "When Columba, exiled from his native",
          "offset": 9812,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "island, founded his stronghold on the",
          "offset": 9815,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "island of Iona, there are hints of a",
          "offset": 9817,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "163:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "blood sacrifice made to consecrate the",
          "offset": 9820,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "ground,",
          "offset": 9823,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "a human sacrifice.",
          "offset": 9825,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "163:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet Adam Nan also writes of 30",
          "offset": 9831,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "monasteries personally founded by",
          "offset": 9834,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "163:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "Columba who ranged far and wide in",
          "offset": 9836,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "163:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "picked land converting people as well as",
          "offset": 9838,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "163:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "transcribing hundreds of books.",
          "offset": 9842,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "164:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "And amazingly it's because of the",
          "offset": 9846,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "164:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "literacy on Iona where a now lost",
          "offset": 9847,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "164:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "chronicle seems to have been maintained",
          "offset": 9850,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "164:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "throughout this era that we have a",
          "offset": 9852,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "164:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "unique document telling us how many men",
          "offset": 9854,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "164:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Aiden could muster.",
          "offset": 9857,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "164:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 9864,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "164:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "The history of the men of Scotland is",
          "offset": 9866,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "164:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "believed to have been compiled in the",
          "offset": 9868,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "164:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "10th century, though it is based on much",
          "offset": 9870,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "164:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "earlier writings,",
          "offset": 9873,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "164:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "providing royal genealogies as well as a",
          "offset": 9875,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "164:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "census. No other document of its kind",
          "offset": 9878,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "164:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "survives for this era.",
          "offset": 9881,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "164:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the work, we are told that Aiden",
          "offset": 9884,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "164:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "could muster well over a thousand men, a",
          "offset": 9886,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "164:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "huge force for the time.",
          "offset": 9890,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "164:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 9893,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "164:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "There is even reference of a sea battle",
          "offset": 9896,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "164:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "fought by sailed Corax, some of the best",
          "offset": 9898,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "164:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "ships of the era.",
          "offset": 9901,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "165:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "In other Irish sources, we're told that",
          "offset": 9905,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "165:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Aiden fought a sea war in 580 against",
          "offset": 9907,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "165:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Orcne's Pictish defenders.",
          "offset": 9910,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "165:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "and no doubt against other groups of",
          "offset": 9913,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "165:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "picss too.",
          "offset": 9915,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "165:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "But for our story, we must look to the",
          "offset": 9920,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "165:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "south, back to the brethonic Welsh",
          "offset": 9922,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "165:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "sources.",
          "offset": 9926,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "165:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "As far as the Welsh are concerned,",
          "offset": 9930,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "165:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Aiden, the only non-Britain to feature",
          "offset": 9932,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "165:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "heavily in their tales, is known as the",
          "offset": 9935,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "165:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Treacherous and the Wy,",
          "offset": 9938,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "165:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps earning this name after the",
          "offset": 9942,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "165:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "collapse of an alliance with Red Hy,",
          "offset": 9943,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "165:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "King of Dumbartan Rock.",
          "offset": 9946,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "165:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 9950,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "165:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "Another triad records Aiden's host as",
          "offset": 9952,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "165:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "one of the three faithful war bands of",
          "offset": 9954,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "165:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "the island of Britain. as they went to",
          "offset": 9956,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "165:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "see for their lord.",
          "offset": 9959,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "165:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Maybe reflecting a lost account of an",
          "offset": 9961,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "166:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "expedition to Man or Orcne, perhaps",
          "offset": 9963,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "166:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "suggesting a significant British",
          "offset": 9967,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "166:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "contingent in Aiden's army. Indeed, many",
          "offset": 9969,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "166:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Welsh works claimed that Aiden had a",
          "offset": 9972,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "166:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "British mother,",
          "offset": 9974,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "166:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "a donastic allegiance between two",
          "offset": 9976,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "166:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdoms perhaps.",
          "offset": 9978,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "166:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 9980,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "166:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "So then by the start of the 7th century,",
          "offset": 9983,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "166:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "it's speculation, but there is a chance",
          "offset": 9987,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "166:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "that Aiden may have grieved when he",
          "offset": 9989,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "166:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "heard of the slaughter at Catrath.",
          "offset": 9991,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "166:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "His people shared the same religion as",
          "offset": 9996,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "166:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Britain and much more of a similar",
          "offset": 9998,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "166:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "way of life.",
          "offset": 10001,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "166:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "Either",
          "offset": 10005,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "166:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "this or he saw it as an opportunity to",
          "offset": 10009,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "166:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "carve out his own dominion over the",
          "offset": 10012,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "166:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "south. For not long afterwards, he",
          "offset": 10014,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "166:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "called his banners, gathering together a",
          "offset": 10017,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "166:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "huge army from his kingdoms, as well as",
          "offset": 10020,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "167:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "significant numbers of O'Neal from Tara",
          "offset": 10023,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "167:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "across the sea, led by Male Ume, the",
          "offset": 10026,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "167:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "brother of the high king of Ireland.",
          "offset": 10029,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "167:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10034,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "167:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "as well as contingents of Britain's and",
          "offset": 10036,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "167:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "maybe even exiled Anglian princes making",
          "offset": 10039,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "167:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "their own place for power. These are",
          "offset": 10042,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "167:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "hinted at by archaeology at Dunad.",
          "offset": 10044,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "167:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "And of course, the enemy that they were",
          "offset": 10048,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "167:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "fighting was the twister Ethelfr of",
          "offset": 10050,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "167:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Benia.",
          "offset": 10054,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "167:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "By the year 603, a reckoning was on the",
          "offset": 10061,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "167:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "way.",
          "offset": 10064,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "167:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "Elsewhere in the world, the tyrant focus",
          "offset": 10068,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "167:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "reigned in Baantium.",
          "offset": 10071,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "167:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "To the east, the Cisanian shars sent",
          "offset": 10073,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "167:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "forth their armies to do battle. Still",
          "offset": 10076,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "167:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "standing guard over one of the largest",
          "offset": 10079,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "167:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "border walls the world had ever seen.",
          "offset": 10081,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "168:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "The latest incarnation of classical",
          "offset": 10084,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "168:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "eastern empires to arise in Mesopotamia.",
          "offset": 10086,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "168:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ever since the Samrians many thousands",
          "offset": 10089,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "168:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "of years before,",
          "offset": 10091,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "168:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10094,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "168:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "further east still, the first great",
          "offset": 10096,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "168:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Turkish confederation, the blue sky",
          "offset": 10098,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "168:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "girks, still tangest in their belief",
          "offset": 10100,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "168:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "system, held sway over nearly the",
          "offset": 10103,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "168:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "entirety of the Eurasian step.",
          "offset": 10105,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "168:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10108,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "168:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "In Arabia to the south, polytheism still",
          "offset": 10110,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "168:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "reigned.",
          "offset": 10113,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "168:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "For this was an age before Islam was",
          "offset": 10114,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "168:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "even born.",
          "offset": 10117,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "168:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "And in remote, faroff Britain, the first",
          "offset": 10124,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "168:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "great battle in British history, just on",
          "offset": 10127,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "168:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "the edge of verifiable recorded events,",
          "offset": 10130,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "168:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "would be fought.",
          "offset": 10132,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "168:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "The two armies met, so we're told, at a",
          "offset": 10136,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "168:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "pre-arranged place somewhere in the",
          "offset": 10139,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "168:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "north of Britain called Dex Stone.",
          "offset": 10141,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "169:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10144,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "169:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "a great monolith described by Bead.",
          "offset": 10146,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "169:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Apparently, everybody knew where it was,",
          "offset": 10150,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "169:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "though the location is lost today.",
          "offset": 10153,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "169:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10158,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "169:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "The ensuing battle, by far the largest",
          "offset": 10160,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "169:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "conflict since the fall of Roman",
          "offset": 10163,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "169:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain, pitted the two foremost",
          "offset": 10165,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "169:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "superpowers of the North against one",
          "offset": 10168,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "169:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "another.",
          "offset": 10170,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "169:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "squabbling over the carcass of the old",
          "offset": 10171,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "169:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "north.",
          "offset": 10174,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "169:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "To the victor would go the lands of the",
          "offset": 10175,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "169:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britons.",
          "offset": 10178,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "169:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10180,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "169:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Aiden's name does not speak favorably to",
          "offset": 10182,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "169:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "his reputation amongst the Britons of",
          "offset": 10185,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "169:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alt Cloot, where some of our sources may",
          "offset": 10187,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "169:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "have originated with a longlost",
          "offset": 10189,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "169:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "chronicle written there.",
          "offset": 10191,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "169:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "It may be that Dexteran was fought over",
          "offset": 10194,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "169:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "control of Lotheian in the aftermath of",
          "offset": 10197,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "169:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Catrath.",
          "offset": 10199,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "169:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "There are even hints of an Irish raid on",
          "offset": 10203,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "170:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Bambra in the BIC tradition. And no",
          "offset": 10205,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "170:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "doubt many Britons saw the Irish,",
          "offset": 10207,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "170:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Christians at least, as a far preferable",
          "offset": 10210,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "170:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "choice of overlord to the Anglians.",
          "offset": 10213,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "170:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10216,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "170:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "We don't actually know whether Ethelf",
          "offset": 10222,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "170:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "was present at the battle, though it's",
          "offset": 10224,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "170:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "likely he was. His father had likely",
          "offset": 10226,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "170:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "been killed by the Britain when he was a",
          "offset": 10230,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "170:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "boy. And ever since that time, all he'd",
          "offset": 10232,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "170:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "known was war.",
          "offset": 10235,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "170:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "And by the time he came of age, he",
          "offset": 10238,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "170:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "didn't just have one axe to grind.",
          "offset": 10241,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "170:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "He had thousands of them.",
          "offset": 10244,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "170:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "Outnumbered as they were, the Anglians",
          "offset": 10247,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "170:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "were probably better armed and better",
          "offset": 10250,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "170:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "motivated.",
          "offset": 10252,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "170:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10253,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "170:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "They marched in several detachments led",
          "offset": 10256,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "170:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "by largely independent war leaders",
          "offset": 10259,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "170:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "followed by incredibly loyal followers.",
          "offset": 10264,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "171:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethelfith's brother Theodbolt led one of",
          "offset": 10269,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "171:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Anglian detachments. Supported by",
          "offset": 10272,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "171:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "elite hearth troops, professional career",
          "offset": 10275,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "171:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "soldiers whose code and very way of life",
          "offset": 10278,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "171:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "demanded they fight to the death if",
          "offset": 10281,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "171:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "their lord was killed.",
          "offset": 10283,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "171:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "No doubt many of them veterans of",
          "offset": 10286,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "171:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Catrath.",
          "offset": 10288,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "171:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "trailed by a swarm of less welle",
          "offset": 10291,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "171:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "equipped regular farmer soldiers eager",
          "offset": 10293,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "171:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "for glory.",
          "offset": 10296,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "171:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10297,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "171:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Herring, son of Huss, the warlord who'd",
          "offset": 10301,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "171:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "fought against Yuran at Lindisvan a",
          "offset": 10304,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "171:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "generation earlier, may even have fought",
          "offset": 10306,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "171:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "on the Irish side, or perhaps opted to",
          "offset": 10308,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "171:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "watch the fighting and join the winner,",
          "offset": 10312,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "171:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "as so many precariously allied noblemen",
          "offset": 10315,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "171:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "would do throughout history.",
          "offset": 10318,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "171:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10322,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "172:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "The fighting was brutal, lasting all",
          "offset": 10329,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "172:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "day. We can imagine the Anglian shield",
          "offset": 10333,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "172:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "wall shattering the British cavalry",
          "offset": 10336,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "172:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "charge again and again, though suffering",
          "offset": 10338,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "172:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "horrendous casualties in the process.",
          "offset": 10342,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "172:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "According to Adam Nan, Aiden's son",
          "offset": 10346,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "172:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Domingart was killed in the fry along",
          "offset": 10348,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "172:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "with the Irish prince Male Umay.",
          "offset": 10351,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "172:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet Theodbold died too. We can imagine",
          "offset": 10354,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "172:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "his retainers going to their doom around",
          "offset": 10358,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "172:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "him, devastated at the death of their",
          "offset": 10360,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "172:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "lord, their sole means of attaining",
          "offset": 10363,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "172:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "glory and power.",
          "offset": 10365,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "172:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "Even hundreds of years later, long after",
          "offset": 10369,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "172:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "Christianity took hold, Anglo-Saxon",
          "offset": 10372,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "172:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "soldiers still saw it as their god-given",
          "offset": 10374,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "172:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "duty to either die for their Lord or",
          "offset": 10376,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "172:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "triumph against the enemy that killed",
          "offset": 10379,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "172:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "him. Tradition dictated they would be",
          "offset": 10381,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "173:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "cast out from society if they didn't.",
          "offset": 10384,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "173:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "And this grim determination may be one",
          "offset": 10389,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "173:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the reasons for their success in the",
          "offset": 10392,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "173:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "battle.",
          "offset": 10394,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "173:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Chopping off the head of the snake",
          "offset": 10397,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "173:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "simply didn't work with this enemy.",
          "offset": 10399,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "173:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "They would fight harder and if",
          "offset": 10402,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "173:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "victorious, another would take the",
          "offset": 10404,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "173:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "Lord's place.",
          "offset": 10406,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "173:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the aftermath of the battle, not just",
          "offset": 10417,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "173:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Driartans and the Britain, but all",
          "offset": 10419,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "173:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Christians in Britain suffered a",
          "offset": 10422,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "173:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "devastating blow.",
          "offset": 10425,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "173:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Aiden had been chosen by God, which",
          "offset": 10428,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "173:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "meant God was on the side of the pagans.",
          "offset": 10431,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "173:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10436,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "173:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "It must have been a terrifying",
          "offset": 10439,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "173:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "existential crisis.",
          "offset": 10441,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "174:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Within a year or two, Ethelfr",
          "offset": 10445,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "174:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "successfully annexed Dra, unifying the",
          "offset": 10447,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "174:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "two Anglian kingdoms into one, laying",
          "offset": 10450,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "174:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "the foundation for the Kingdom of North",
          "offset": 10453,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "174:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Umbrea,",
          "offset": 10455,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "174:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "adding its young warriors to his growing",
          "offset": 10457,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "174:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "force.",
          "offset": 10459,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "174:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "For him, the battle was especially",
          "offset": 10462,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "174:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "beneficial, taking out Anglian rivals as",
          "offset": 10464,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "174:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "well as the Irish.",
          "offset": 10468,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "174:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Bead tells us that not only was almost",
          "offset": 10472,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "174:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "the entire Dalriartan force wiped out,",
          "offset": 10474,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "174:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "but never again, even right up until his",
          "offset": 10478,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "174:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "own time, well over a century later,",
          "offset": 10481,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "174:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "would the Irish ever dare to attack",
          "offset": 10483,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "174:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "English lands, thus putting an end to",
          "offset": 10486,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "174:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "almost 300 years of Irish piracy and",
          "offset": 10489,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "174:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "raiding on British shores.",
          "offset": 10492,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "174:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the space of a single day, everything",
          "offset": 10495,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "174:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "had changed.",
          "offset": 10498,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "174:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Had",
          "offset": 10500,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "175:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Alliance won, history would have",
          "offset": 10504,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "175:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "been very different. But they didn't.",
          "offset": 10507,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "175:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Old North was doomed.",
          "offset": 10510,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "175:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "The choice was now simple. Resist and be",
          "offset": 10517,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "175:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "destroyed, or pay tribute and join",
          "offset": 10520,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "175:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethelf.",
          "offset": 10523,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "175:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the years to come, Ethelf's warriors",
          "offset": 10528,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "175:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "ranged far and wide, as far as the Welsh",
          "offset": 10530,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "175:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "stories are concerned, brutalizing those",
          "offset": 10533,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "175:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "who opposed them, driving them out,",
          "offset": 10536,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "175:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "killing or taking slaves of anyone who",
          "offset": 10540,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "175:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "hadn't already fled.",
          "offset": 10543,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "175:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10548,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "175:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "For bead, although they were still pagan",
          "offset": 10549,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "175:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "at the time, God was on the Anglican",
          "offset": 10551,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "175:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "side. divine justice against the",
          "offset": 10554,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "175:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "heretical British church playing its",
          "offset": 10556,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "175:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "part in growing the borders of the first",
          "offset": 10559,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "175:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "great power of the north.",
          "offset": 10561,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "176:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10565,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "176:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "And now with the lack of anyone to",
          "offset": 10566,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "176:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "oppose it, that swift advance to the",
          "offset": 10568,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "176:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "west seen in archaeology as well as",
          "offset": 10571,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "176:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "history continued unabated.",
          "offset": 10574,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "176:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 613, in an especially bold move,",
          "offset": 10580,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "176:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethelfr advanced all the way to the",
          "offset": 10583,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "176:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "river D in what is now Cheshire,",
          "offset": 10585,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "176:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps seeking to drive a wedge between",
          "offset": 10590,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "176:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "the northern and the Western Britons.",
          "offset": 10592,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "176:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10595,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "176:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Dedicated to a Celtic war goddess in",
          "offset": 10601,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "176:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "days gone by, perhaps still venerated by",
          "offset": 10603,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "176:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "some, the D was a stronghold of British",
          "offset": 10607,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "176:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "rule.",
          "offset": 10610,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "176:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "A great walled city of the Romans stood",
          "offset": 10616,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "176:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "there still.",
          "offset": 10618,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "176:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Once home to an entire legion,",
          "offset": 10620,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "177:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "today we know the place as Chester.",
          "offset": 10624,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "177:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Perhaps",
          "offset": 10628,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "177:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "allied to the city of Viriconium to the",
          "offset": 10632,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "177:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "south",
          "offset": 10634,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "177:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "before the Anglian Mercians rose to",
          "offset": 10636,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "177:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "prominence under their own conquering",
          "offset": 10638,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "177:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "king Penda. The region is thought to",
          "offset": 10640,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "177:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "have been ruled by a prince of Pois, one",
          "offset": 10643,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "177:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the most powerful of the Welsh",
          "offset": 10646,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "177:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdoms.",
          "offset": 10648,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "177:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sometimes known as Solomon in the Welsh",
          "offset": 10655,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "177:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "triads, Celif, son of Kynan, was a",
          "offset": 10657,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "177:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "feared fighter in his day. Known as",
          "offset": 10660,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "177:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "serpent in battles",
          "offset": 10663,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "177:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "and it wasn't just the men of pois who",
          "offset": 10666,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "177:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "came to oppose the Anglian menace that",
          "offset": 10669,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "177:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "day. Bardic tradition suggests the",
          "offset": 10671,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "177:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "entire power of North Wales may have",
          "offset": 10674,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "177:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "come to their aid,",
          "offset": 10676,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "177:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "notably a contingent from Gwen.",
          "offset": 10678,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "177:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "And it wasn't just fighters either.",
          "offset": 10684,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "178:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hundreds of monks from the nearby",
          "offset": 10686,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "178:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "monastery of Bangar came too, praying",
          "offset": 10688,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "178:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "for the victory of their countrymen.",
          "offset": 10691,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "178:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "When Ethelf arrived at the battlefield,",
          "offset": 10697,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "178:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "however, he spotted these priests",
          "offset": 10700,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "178:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "working their Christian magic. He had",
          "offset": 10702,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "178:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "separated from the main force.",
          "offset": 10705,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "178:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ordering his men forwards, they were cut",
          "offset": 10710,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "178:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "down to a man.",
          "offset": 10713,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "178:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "As the main Welsh force entered the fry,",
          "offset": 10718,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "178:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "their morale already low, having",
          "offset": 10721,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "178:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "witnessed the slaughter of their holy",
          "offset": 10723,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "178:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "men, they too fell to the Anglian",
          "offset": 10725,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "178:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "swords.",
          "offset": 10728,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "178:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "Zeif's death is recorded in the Anel's",
          "offset": 10732,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "178:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cambrii.",
          "offset": 10735,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "178:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "Chester became an English city and",
          "offset": 10737,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "178:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cheshure an English stronghold,",
          "offset": 10740,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "178:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10743,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "179:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "turning what had started as essentially",
          "offset": 10746,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "179:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "a pirate band operating out of Bambra",
          "offset": 10748,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "179:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "just over a decade before into the most",
          "offset": 10751,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "179:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "powerful military force in all of",
          "offset": 10754,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "179:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain.",
          "offset": 10757,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "179:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Scores of armies had tried to stop them.",
          "offset": 10761,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "179:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "They'd all failed.",
          "offset": 10764,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "179:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "No doubt many more unrecorded battles",
          "offset": 10767,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "179:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "taking place too.",
          "offset": 10770,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "179:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10773,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "179:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "But then in 616, in one of the great",
          "offset": 10774,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "179:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "changes of fortune in British history,",
          "offset": 10778,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "179:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethelf, master of the north, triumphant",
          "offset": 10781,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "179:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "in battle, outstretched himself.",
          "offset": 10785,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "179:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10791,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "179:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "Corpses of his enemies spled on the",
          "offset": 10795,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "179:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "shields and spears of his followers. He",
          "offset": 10797,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "179:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "went south, ever searching for the",
          "offset": 10800,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "179:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "deposed prince of Dra, Edwin,",
          "offset": 10802,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "180:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "rival to his power.",
          "offset": 10806,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "180:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10809,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "180:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "There on the southern borderlands of his",
          "offset": 10815,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "180:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "realm, with only a small force around",
          "offset": 10818,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "180:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "him, he was ambushed by another king.",
          "offset": 10820,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "180:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "For Edwin had found a powerful ally.",
          "offset": 10824,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "180:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10827,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "180:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "This one with farreaching trade contacts",
          "offset": 10833,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "180:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "across Europe.",
          "offset": 10835,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "180:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "Direct influence stretching from Lindsay",
          "offset": 10838,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "180:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "to the aisle of white.",
          "offset": 10840,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "180:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Of course, it was Redwald of East",
          "offset": 10844,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "180:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglia.",
          "offset": 10846,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "180:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10848,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "180:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "Writing hundreds of years later, Henry",
          "offset": 10854,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "180:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Huntington describes what happened",
          "offset": 10857,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "180:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "next.",
          "offset": 10859,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "180:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hemmed in onto the banks of the River",
          "offset": 10865,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "181:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Idol, Ethelfith lurched forward,",
          "offset": 10867,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "181:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "charging towards Redwald's son, Raina,",
          "offset": 10871,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "181:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "cutting him down in his battle fury.",
          "offset": 10874,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "181:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Massively outnumbered with just a few",
          "offset": 10880,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "181:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "select men, Ethelfreth raged into the",
          "offset": 10882,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "181:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "East Anglian line.",
          "offset": 10885,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "181:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Reveling in the slaughter,",
          "offset": 10888,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "181:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "systematically slicing down man after",
          "offset": 10891,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "181:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "man.",
          "offset": 10894,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "181:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet Redwald's numbers were simply too",
          "offset": 10896,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "181:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "much.",
          "offset": 10898,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "181:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "He may have even sailed his army up the",
          "offset": 10901,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "181:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "coast into the Humber to cut the Benians",
          "offset": 10903,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "181:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "off.",
          "offset": 10905,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "181:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "And it was only a matter of time before",
          "offset": 10907,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "181:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethelfreth was surrounded, overwhelmed,",
          "offset": 10909,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "181:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "and slain allegedly on a pile of corpses",
          "offset": 10912,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "181:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "stacked up around him.",
          "offset": 10916,
          "duration": 10,
          "formattedTime": "181:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 10918,
          "duration": 10,
          "formattedTime": "181:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Florent of Worcester even implies that",
          "offset": 10926,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "182:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "it was Redwald himself who dealt the",
          "offset": 10928,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "182:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "killing blow,",
          "offset": 10930,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "182:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "meaning the remote possibility exists.",
          "offset": 10932,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "182:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "The sword found at Sutton who could have",
          "offset": 10935,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "182:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "taken Ethelfith's life at the idol. The",
          "offset": 10937,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "182:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "famous helmet, the protection he wore.",
          "offset": 10941,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "182:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Whether he dealt the killing blow or",
          "offset": 10950,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "182:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "not, his strategy put an end to the",
          "offset": 10952,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "182:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "Benissian expansion for a time.",
          "offset": 10954,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "182:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "The only thing that could kill this",
          "offset": 10957,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "182:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglian warlord was another.",
          "offset": 10959,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "182:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Unlike Redwald, who may have died of old",
          "offset": 10964,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "182:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "age, probably at least partly a",
          "offset": 10966,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "182:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Christian, Ethelfreth joined the ranks",
          "offset": 10969,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "182:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "of practically every other king of North",
          "offset": 10972,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "182:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "Umbrea in a 100 years, cut down in the",
          "offset": 10974,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "182:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "prime of his life, resolutely a pagan,",
          "offset": 10978,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "182:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "he went on to feast in the halls of his",
          "offset": 10982,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "183:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "ancestors.",
          "offset": 10984,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "183:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Unfortunately, no candidate for Ethelf's",
          "offset": 10990,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "183:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "grave has ever been found,",
          "offset": 10993,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "183:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "and very little evidence of swords or",
          "offset": 10996,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "183:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "helmets for this period in North Umbrea.",
          "offset": 10999,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "183:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "There is a grave at Ying that could have",
          "offset": 11002,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "183:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "originally contained a helmet like that",
          "offset": 11004,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "183:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "at Sutton who perhaps worn by Ethelfr,",
          "offset": 11006,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "183:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "though it long ago rotted away like",
          "offset": 11010,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "183:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "almost every other item from this age.",
          "offset": 11014,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "183:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "Only 16 years into the 7th century and",
          "offset": 11022,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "183:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "the British were effectively out. There",
          "offset": 11025,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "183:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "was a new order.",
          "offset": 11028,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "183:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Anglo-Saxons definitively in the",
          "offset": 11031,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "183:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "driver's seat.",
          "offset": 11034,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "183:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "There was a new king in North Umbrea,",
          "offset": 11038,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "183:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "too. This one hailing from the southern",
          "offset": 11040,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "183:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdom Edwin.",
          "offset": 11042,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "184:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "initially under the overlordship of",
          "offset": 11044,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "184:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Redwald of East Anglia.",
          "offset": 11046,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "184:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though soon enough he would pass away,",
          "offset": 11049,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "184:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "allowing Edwin to go it alone.",
          "offset": 11052,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "184:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 11055,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "184:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "In 617, the obscure kingdom of Elmet in",
          "offset": 11060,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "184:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Penines, which survives only in a",
          "offset": 11064,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "184:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "handful of place names, was invaded.",
          "offset": 11067,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "184:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Its king, who may have poisoned Edwin's",
          "offset": 11071,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "184:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "brother under Ethelfr's orders, was",
          "offset": 11075,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "184:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "driven out.",
          "offset": 11077,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "184:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "What happened to its population? We",
          "offset": 11083,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "184:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "don't know.",
          "offset": 11085,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "184:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though Edwin later became a Christian",
          "offset": 11088,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "184:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "and as such is praised by Bead as a",
          "offset": 11091,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "184:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "great and just ruler,",
          "offset": 11093,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "184:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "in reality, Edwin may have been just as",
          "offset": 11096,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "184:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "warlike as his predecessor.",
          "offset": 11098,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "184:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless, the Old North had a",
          "offset": 11104,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "185:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "significant influence on the Anglians.",
          "offset": 11106,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "185:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Some Welsh sources even suggest Edwin",
          "offset": 11109,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "185:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "had been raised or spent time at the",
          "offset": 11112,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "185:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "court of Gwennneth in North Wales",
          "offset": 11114,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "185:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "alongside his future enemy, Cadwallan.",
          "offset": 11117,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "185:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "They also suggest he was baptized by a",
          "offset": 11123,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "185:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "son or grandson of Yurion,",
          "offset": 11126,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "185:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "suggesting a level of prestige and",
          "offset": 11129,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "185:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "influence still for the descendants of",
          "offset": 11131,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "185:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "the great king of Regath.",
          "offset": 11133,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "185:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though we're also told he was baptized",
          "offset": 11136,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "185:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "by Palinus from Rome as Redwald may have",
          "offset": 11138,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "185:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "been.",
          "offset": 11142,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "185:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "It may be he was baptized by both faiths",
          "offset": 11144,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "185:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "having slightly differing creeds.",
          "offset": 11147,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "185:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "By the 620s, Christianity was certainly",
          "offset": 11152,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "185:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "seeping into the north.",
          "offset": 11156,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "185:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though it didn't make the Anglians any",
          "offset": 11161,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "186:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "less warlike,",
          "offset": 11164,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "186:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "declining in influence over the years to",
          "offset": 11173,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "186:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "the point of obscurity.",
          "offset": 11175,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "186:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "It would nevertheless be several decades",
          "offset": 11178,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "186:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "yet until the strongholds of Reggath and",
          "offset": 11180,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "186:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "Gdin would fall.",
          "offset": 11182,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "186:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Unfortunately, we have scanted little",
          "offset": 11188,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "186:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "knowledge of this. Bead writing in the",
          "offset": 11191,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "186:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "8th century has almost nothing to say on",
          "offset": 11194,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "186:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "the matter. His is a tale of",
          "offset": 11196,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "186:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Christianity. It simply wouldn't do to",
          "offset": 11199,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "186:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "dwell on the destruction of Christian",
          "offset": 11202,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "186:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdoms.",
          "offset": 11203,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "186:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "but disappear they would.",
          "offset": 11206,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "186:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 11210,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "186:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "One particularly important event is",
          "offset": 11213,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "186:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "spoken of in the Irish annals in 638",
          "offset": 11215,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "186:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "during the time of Edwin's successor",
          "offset": 11220,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "186:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "Oswald.",
          "offset": 11222,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "187:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "A son of Ethelfr who rose to power after",
          "offset": 11224,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "187:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "the death of Edwin at the hands of",
          "offset": 11227,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "187:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cadwallan of Gwennneth and Penda of",
          "offset": 11228,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "187:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mercia. an unlikely alliance between",
          "offset": 11231,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "187:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "British Christian and Anglian pagan.",
          "offset": 11234,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "187:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Oswald had been raised in Daliata in the",
          "offset": 11240,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "187:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "wake of his father's downfall,",
          "offset": 11243,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "187:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "and it was to Irish Christianity that he",
          "offset": 11246,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "187:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "looked for spiritual guidance.",
          "offset": 11249,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "187:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet, he was no less warlike than his",
          "offset": 11252,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "187:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "predecessors.",
          "offset": 11255,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "187:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though his Irish right-hand man, Aiden,",
          "offset": 11256,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "187:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "continued to spread the faith amongst",
          "offset": 11259,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "187:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Anglians.",
          "offset": 11261,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "187:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "In 638, we're told in the Irish sources",
          "offset": 11266,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "187:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "that Oswald and his brother Oswi",
          "offset": 11270,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "187:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "captured the fortress of Den Eden,",
          "offset": 11272,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "187:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "modern-day Edinburgh.",
          "offset": 11276,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "187:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "The kingdom of God was no more. By 642,",
          "offset": 11280,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "188:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "all of Lotheian came under their direct",
          "offset": 11285,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "188:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "control,",
          "offset": 11287,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "188:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "beginning the long overlordship of what",
          "offset": 11290,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "188:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "would become large swavthes of the",
          "offset": 11292,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "188:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Scottish lowlands by the Anglians of",
          "offset": 11294,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "188:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "North Umbrea,",
          "offset": 11296,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "188:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 11300,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "188:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "dividing the kingdom between North",
          "offset": 11301,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "188:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "Umbrea, the Britons of Altcloot, and the",
          "offset": 11303,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "188:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Scots of Daliata.",
          "offset": 11306,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "188:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "In that year, however, it was Oswald's",
          "offset": 11309,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "188:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "time to die.",
          "offset": 11311,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "188:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "like almost every other king of this",
          "offset": 11314,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "188:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "era, meeting his end on the battlefield.",
          "offset": 11317,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "188:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "this time against Pender of Mercia,",
          "offset": 11321,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "188:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "fighting again with Welsh support,",
          "offset": 11323,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "188:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "leaving a fragmented North Umbrea to his",
          "offset": 11330,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "188:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "brother and right-hand man, Oswthv's",
          "offset": 11332,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "188:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "end came later still. Yet it may have",
          "offset": 11340,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "189:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "been of a different kind.",
          "offset": 11344,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "189:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "For Osw's first wife and mother of one",
          "offset": 11347,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "189:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "of his heirs, Ulfrith was a British",
          "offset": 11350,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "189:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "princess.",
          "offset": 11352,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "189:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "We're told by the Histori Brettonum, a",
          "offset": 11358,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "189:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "great granddaughter of Yurion.",
          "offset": 11361,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "189:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "Thus for a brief time though the kingdom",
          "offset": 11365,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "189:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "itself was annexed by around 650 a",
          "offset": 11368,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "189:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "descendant of its greatest king sat on",
          "offset": 11371,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "189:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "the now Christian throne of North",
          "offset": 11374,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "189:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "Umbrea.",
          "offset": 11376,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "189:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 11378,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "189:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "A political act which fused the two",
          "offset": 11380,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "189:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdoms together.",
          "offset": 11382,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "189:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "An unthinkable arrangement during the",
          "offset": 11386,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "189:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "previous century.",
          "offset": 11388,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "189:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "Times were changing",
          "offset": 11390,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "189:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "and it's very likely that Britain's",
          "offset": 11393,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "189:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "exercised influence within the kingdom",
          "offset": 11396,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "189:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "only becoming gradually more Anglian as",
          "offset": 11400,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "189:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "time went on.",
          "offset": 11402,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "190:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "They may even have had an influence on",
          "offset": 11407,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "190:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "the burgeoning literacy of the kingdom",
          "offset": 11408,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "190:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "eventually growing into the likes of",
          "offset": 11411,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "190:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "bead.",
          "offset": 11413,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "190:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "By the 7th century, as we've seen,",
          "offset": 11417,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "190:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "significant evidence for North Umbrean",
          "offset": 11419,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "190:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "influence in Galloway and Cumbria can be",
          "offset": 11421,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "190:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "found.",
          "offset": 11424,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "190:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "Great crosses erected to signify the",
          "offset": 11428,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "190:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "power of the new elite and just maybe an",
          "offset": 11430,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "190:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "attempt to make the transition easier.",
          "offset": 11433,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "190:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 685, Cumbria and Galloway were",
          "offset": 11438,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "190:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "securely in Anglian hands.",
          "offset": 11441,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "190:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "North Umbrea with Edgefr, son of Oswi,",
          "offset": 11444,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "190:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "the most powerful king in Britain, even",
          "offset": 11448,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "190:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "launching raids across the sea to ravage",
          "offset": 11450,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "190:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "the heartlands of Ireland,",
          "offset": 11453,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "190:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "seizing man and launching campaigns far",
          "offset": 11458,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "190:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "to the north, taking vast swaves of",
          "offset": 11461,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "191:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "picked land.",
          "offset": 11464,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "191:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet against all the odds, one old north",
          "offset": 11466,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "191:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdom survived.",
          "offset": 11469,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "191:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "Seated on its impenetrable fortress on",
          "offset": 11472,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "191:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Clyde near modern-day Glasgow. Alt",
          "offset": 11475,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "191:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Clout, the kingdom of the rock.",
          "offset": 11478,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "191:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 11493,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "191:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sometime in the fifth century, a boy was",
          "offset": 11496,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "191:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "kidnapped by slavers on the Irish Sea.",
          "offset": 11499,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "191:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "His father had been a durian, we're",
          "offset": 11504,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "191:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "told, a title of the late Roman world.",
          "offset": 11506,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "191:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "along with his father's servants and",
          "offset": 11518,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "191:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "everyone else who'd been seized in his",
          "offset": 11521,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "192:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "community. He entered a life of harsh",
          "offset": 11523,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "192:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "servitude on the other side of the sea.",
          "offset": 11526,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "192:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "A life with little hope of escape.",
          "offset": 11530,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "192:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 11533,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "192:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though given a Christian education in",
          "offset": 11539,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "192:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "much the same way as Gildas and other",
          "offset": 11541,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "192:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "wealthy Romano British families, it was",
          "offset": 11543,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "192:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "in pagan Ireland, tending sheep on high",
          "offset": 11546,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "192:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "hillsides, that the young man really",
          "offset": 11550,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "192:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "came close to God.",
          "offset": 11553,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "192:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 11554,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "192:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "And after he hatched his daring escape a",
          "offset": 11560,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "192:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "few years later, rejoining the learned",
          "offset": 11562,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "192:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "literate world, clinging on in Britain",
          "offset": 11565,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "192:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "by the skin of its teeth,",
          "offset": 11567,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "192:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "it was back to Ireland that he'd return",
          "offset": 11570,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "192:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "voluntarily this time,",
          "offset": 11576,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "192:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "bringing his faith with him to convert",
          "offset": 11581,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "193:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "his former captives.",
          "offset": 11584,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "193:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Thus begins one of the greatest of all",
          "offset": 11592,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "193:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "stories of the sub Roman period, that of",
          "offset": 11595,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "193:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "St. Patrick.",
          "offset": 11599,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "193:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 11601,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "193:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "Patrick's story is unique because we",
          "offset": 11608,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "193:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "know it not just from the saints lives",
          "offset": 11610,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "193:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "written about him later, but also from",
          "offset": 11613,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "193:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "his own words recorded in middling",
          "offset": 11616,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "193:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Latin.",
          "offset": 11619,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "193:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Not quite the impressive pros of Gildas,",
          "offset": 11621,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "193:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "but to be fair to Patrick, his education",
          "offset": 11624,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "193:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "had been cut painfully short.",
          "offset": 11627,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "193:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "One of these accounts, the confession,",
          "offset": 11634,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "193:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "reads as a short autobiography of his",
          "offset": 11636,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "193:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "own tale.",
          "offset": 11639,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "193:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 11640,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "194:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "The other is a letter to a certain king,",
          "offset": 11642,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "194:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "a ruler of the North who'd been slaving",
          "offset": 11646,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "194:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "on the Irish Sea,",
          "offset": 11649,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "194:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "capturing newly converted Christians for",
          "offset": 11651,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "194:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "sale to pagan buyers.",
          "offset": 11654,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "194:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "This ruler was probably at least",
          "offset": 11659,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "194:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "nominally a Christian. Otherwise,",
          "offset": 11661,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "194:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Patrick's threat of excommunication",
          "offset": 11663,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "194:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "would have been entirely an empty one.",
          "offset": 11666,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "194:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though this ruler did associate with",
          "offset": 11671,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "194:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "heathen picss.",
          "offset": 11674,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "194:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "His name King Keroticus.",
          "offset": 11677,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "194:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Often associated with Cerotic Galletic,",
          "offset": 11684,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "194:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "a king of Dumbartan Rock.",
          "offset": 11688,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "194:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "Described as a seafaring kingdom capable",
          "offset": 11694,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "194:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "of launching raids all along the Irish",
          "offset": 11697,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "194:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "coasts as well as influencing events in",
          "offset": 11699,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "194:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "picked lands to the north.",
          "offset": 11702,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "195:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "If Keroticus did rule from Dumbartan",
          "offset": 11705,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "195:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rock, as many scholars suggest,",
          "offset": 11707,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "195:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Patrick's letter shines a light on an",
          "offset": 11710,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "195:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "otherwise entirely dark period.",
          "offset": 11712,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "195:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 11718,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "195:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the 1970s, excavations at the rock",
          "offset": 11725,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "195:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "uncovered high status items from the",
          "offset": 11728,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "195:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Iron Age, Roman period, and onwards,",
          "offset": 11730,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "195:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "with continuity well into the 9th",
          "offset": 11733,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "195:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "century.",
          "offset": 11736,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "195:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "The grip of Rome never extended this far",
          "offset": 11740,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "195:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "north, not permanently anyway. And it",
          "offset": 11743,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "195:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "was from the Celtic Damnoni that the",
          "offset": 11746,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "195:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdom had its roots.",
          "offset": 11748,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "195:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though the place soon disappears again",
          "offset": 11754,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "195:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "in history until the very end of the",
          "offset": 11756,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "195:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "sixth century when one of the most",
          "offset": 11758,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "195:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "famous kings of the age appears.",
          "offset": 11761,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "196:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Red Hy known as the generous in the",
          "offset": 11769,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "196:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Welsh sources seems to have ruled from",
          "offset": 11772,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "196:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "around 580 to 614.",
          "offset": 11774,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "196:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "A remarkably long period.",
          "offset": 11778,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "196:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "a contemporary of Columba and a one-time",
          "offset": 11784,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "196:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "ally of Yuran, who unlike most other",
          "offset": 11786,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "196:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "figures of this time, ruled for an",
          "offset": 11789,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "196:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "extensive period,",
          "offset": 11791,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "196:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps even surviving to die of old",
          "offset": 11794,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "196:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "age.",
          "offset": 11796,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "196:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "As we have already seen, he may have",
          "offset": 11802,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "196:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "fought at After Red as well as Dexistan,",
          "offset": 11804,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "196:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "sending a cavalry detachment under Aiden",
          "offset": 11808,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "196:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "McKabrain at the latter.",
          "offset": 11811,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "196:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "His existence is frequently corroborated",
          "offset": 11815,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "196:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "by a slew of other sources, Irish,",
          "offset": 11818,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "196:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Welsh, and Scottish, an unusual amount",
          "offset": 11821,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "197:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "of historicity.",
          "offset": 11824,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "197:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "And yet his kingdom is a wash with",
          "offset": 11830,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "197:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "legends and myths. Tales of Arthur and",
          "offset": 11833,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "197:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Merlin.",
          "offset": 11837,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "197:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "For this was the very last of the Old",
          "offset": 11839,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "197:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "North, where many of these tales may",
          "offset": 11841,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "197:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "have originated, surviving another 400",
          "offset": 11844,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "197:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "years or so after the demise of its",
          "offset": 11848,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "197:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "neighbors.",
          "offset": 11850,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "197:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "weathering innumerable successive waves",
          "offset": 11853,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "197:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "of invasion over its long history by",
          "offset": 11855,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "197:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rome, Irishmen, PS and angles",
          "offset": 11858,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "197:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "until finally in the 9th century came",
          "offset": 11863,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "197:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "one they could not withstand.",
          "offset": 11866,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "197:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet they weren't entirely on the",
          "offset": 11874,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "197:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "defensive either. Not by a long shot. In",
          "offset": 11876,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "197:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "642, just as the Anglians pushed ever",
          "offset": 11880,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "197:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "onwards, the annals of Olter report that",
          "offset": 11882,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "198:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Britons of Alt Cloot, led by Eugian,",
          "offset": 11885,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "198:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "son of Belly, went to do battle at a",
          "offset": 11888,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "198:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "place called Strath Karen.",
          "offset": 11891,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "198:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "Their enemy this time wasn't the",
          "offset": 11896,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "198:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Germanics, but the Irishman of Delriata,",
          "offset": 11898,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "198:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "led by Dom,",
          "offset": 11902,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "198:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "grandson of Aiden.",
          "offset": 11904,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "198:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "Dom was killed and the Britons took the",
          "offset": 11907,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "198:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "upper hand.",
          "offset": 11909,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "198:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "From then onwards throughout the 8th",
          "offset": 11912,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "198:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "century, Altcloot may have exercised",
          "offset": 11914,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "198:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "overlordship over a number of smaller",
          "offset": 11917,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "198:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdoms,",
          "offset": 11920,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "198:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "fighting wars for supremacy,",
          "offset": 11921,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "198:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "particularly over border areas of picked",
          "offset": 11923,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "198:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "land.",
          "offset": 11925,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "198:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "The pictish king Brud is even called son",
          "offset": 11927,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "198:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the king of alt clute in a line of",
          "offset": 11930,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "198:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "poetry attributed to Adaman.",
          "offset": 11933,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "198:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 11937,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "198:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "The pictish king list names brood's",
          "offset": 11941,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "199:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "father as belly often seen as belly",
          "offset": 11944,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "199:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "aathan",
          "offset": 11947,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "199:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "an especially well-connected ruler in",
          "offset": 11949,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "199:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "the north with donastic ties to picked",
          "offset": 11951,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "199:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "land.",
          "offset": 11954,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "199:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 11955,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "199:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "One of his sons, Bride III, was destined",
          "offset": 11959,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "199:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "to be one of the most powerful and",
          "offset": 11963,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "199:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "influential kings the picss ever had.",
          "offset": 11965,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "199:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is to picked land that we must turn",
          "offset": 11969,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "199:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "to next.",
          "offset": 11971,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "199:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 685, Edgefr of North Umbrea stood",
          "offset": 11983,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "199:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "unopposed in the north.",
          "offset": 11986,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "199:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Overlord of many kingdoms, triumphant in",
          "offset": 11990,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "199:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "wars across land and sea. His armies",
          "offset": 11993,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "199:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "pushed ever onwards deep into the north",
          "offset": 11997,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "199:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "until finally they were met by a",
          "offset": 12002,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "200:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "formidable opponent.",
          "offset": 12004,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "200:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "It wouldn't be the Irish who would throw",
          "offset": 12007,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "200:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "them back or the Britons, though both",
          "offset": 12009,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "200:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "most likely had some small part to play",
          "offset": 12012,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "200:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the battle.",
          "offset": 12014,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "200:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was the Picss under their king Brid",
          "offset": 12020,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "200:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself a cousin of Edge.",
          "offset": 12023,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "200:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "There at a place named Dun Nectane",
          "offset": 12028,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "200:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "somewhere in modern-day Scotland.",
          "offset": 12030,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "200:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "English power over the north was finally",
          "offset": 12033,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "200:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "broken. Edgefr killed",
          "offset": 12036,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "200:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "over the next 150 years or so. His",
          "offset": 12044,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "200:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "successors, forced to deal with renewed",
          "offset": 12046,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "200:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "mercy and aggression from the south, as",
          "offset": 12049,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "200:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "well as pictish raids from the north,",
          "offset": 12052,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "200:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "became increasingly hamstrung by a",
          "offset": 12054,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "200:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "uniquely murderous culture of kinstrife",
          "offset": 12056,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "200:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "known as the long winter.",
          "offset": 12059,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "200:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 12063,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "201:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "The kingdom of the rock had weathered",
          "offset": 12068,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "201:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "the storm. It would survive even as the",
          "offset": 12070,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "201:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "picss themselves disappeared into",
          "offset": 12074,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "201:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "memory.",
          "offset": 12076,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "201:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 12081,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "201:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "There are few mentions of alt glute over",
          "offset": 12084,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "201:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "the rest of the 7th century. Few",
          "offset": 12086,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "201:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "historical sources surviving",
          "offset": 12089,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "201:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "though some mentions of battles in Irish",
          "offset": 12094,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "201:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "sources contain British fighters.",
          "offset": 12097,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "201:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Perhaps",
          "offset": 12100,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "201:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 12103,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "201:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "mercenaries",
          "offset": 12104,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "201:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "or exiles scattered by the Anglo-Saxon",
          "offset": 12107,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "201:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "conquest.",
          "offset": 12110,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "201:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though there is a small chance of them",
          "offset": 12114,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "201:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "being campaigns directed by the rulers",
          "offset": 12116,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "201:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Alt Cloot, roaming far and wide as",
          "offset": 12118,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "201:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "pirate lords once more.",
          "offset": 12122,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "202:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "After all, all of its neighbors, North",
          "offset": 12127,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "202:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Umbrea, Pland, and Dal Riata are known",
          "offset": 12129,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "202:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "to have sent armies to Ireland at times.",
          "offset": 12133,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "202:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "In 711, the annals of Olter record a",
          "offset": 12140,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "202:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "battle between Altcloot and Daliata at a",
          "offset": 12143,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "202:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "place named Log Eklet and another in 717",
          "offset": 12147,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "202:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "at a rock called Min.",
          "offset": 12151,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "202:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "And by 7:44 the pictish king Angus got",
          "offset": 12155,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "202:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "involved too, launching three",
          "offset": 12159,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "202:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "unsuccessful campaigns against Dumbartan",
          "offset": 12162,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "202:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rock.",
          "offset": 12164,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "202:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 750, Angus was back in old glute",
          "offset": 12166,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "202:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "territory. This time fighting alongside",
          "offset": 12170,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "202:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "Edbert of North Umbrea.",
          "offset": 12173,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "202:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though again he would face defeat at the",
          "offset": 12181,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "203:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "hands of Tedar of Alt Glute. Whereas",
          "offset": 12183,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "203:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Talagan, brother of Angus, was killed.",
          "offset": 12186,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "203:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tedar died in 752 though and it was",
          "offset": 12191,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "203:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "likely his son Dumnagul who faced a",
          "offset": 12194,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "203:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "renewed attack by Angus and Eidbert in",
          "offset": 12197,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "203:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "756",
          "offset": 12200,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "203:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "agreeing to submit to the invading army",
          "offset": 12205,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "203:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "only after a siege of Dumbartan Rock.",
          "offset": 12208,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "203:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "However, soon enough Edbert's army was",
          "offset": 12211,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "203:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "all but wiped out on its way back south.",
          "offset": 12214,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "203:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 12217,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "203:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 780, though the circumstances remain",
          "offset": 12222,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "203:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "obscure, Dumbartan Rock was apparently",
          "offset": 12225,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "203:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "burned.",
          "offset": 12228,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "203:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "And by 8:49, the men of Alt Clout,",
          "offset": 12231,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "203:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps under King Arthgal, burned the",
          "offset": 12234,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "203:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "Pictish ecclesiastical center at Don",
          "offset": 12237,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "203:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Blaine.",
          "offset": 12239,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "203:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 12241,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "204:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 870, however, an entirely new threat",
          "offset": 12244,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "204:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "had arrived.",
          "offset": 12247,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "204:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "After a 4-month siege, Dumbartan Rock",
          "offset": 12252,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "204:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "was destroyed by a massive Viking army,",
          "offset": 12255,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "204:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps under the sea king Ivar the",
          "offset": 12259,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "204:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "Boneless,",
          "offset": 12261,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "204:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "sailing back to their lair of Dublin",
          "offset": 12263,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "204:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "with a huge prey of Englishmen, picss,",
          "offset": 12265,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "204:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Britons.",
          "offset": 12268,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "204:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "The ruins smoldering on the horizon.",
          "offset": 12271,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "204:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 12279,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "204:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though Dumbartan Rock was gone, its",
          "offset": 12282,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "204:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "people survived,",
          "offset": 12285,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "204:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "[Music]",
          "offset": 12289,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "204:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "moving further up the estie, rebranding",
          "offset": 12292,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "204:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "themselves as Strath Clyde and surviving",
          "offset": 12295,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "204:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "for yet more centuries to come.",
          "offset": 12297,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "204:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "And as North Umbrea similarly fell to",
          "offset": 12303,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "205:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Vikings in the south, the men of Strath",
          "offset": 12305,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "205:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Clyde would move back south to reclaim",
          "offset": 12308,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "205:08"
        },
