          "text": "the immensely far-flung voyages and",
          "offset": 841,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "14:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "settlements of the early medieval",
          "offset": 843,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Scandinavians,",
          "offset": 845,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "14:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "as well as this one called the green",
          "offset": 848,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "14:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] land on the animals and",
          "offset": 850,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "landscape of that furthest most",
          "offset": 852,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "permanent settlement.",
          "offset": 854,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "14:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "And there's so much more to choose from,",
          "offset": 857,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "too. And now you can watch both of these",
          "offset": 859,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "14:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "titles completely for free by signing up",
          "offset": 862,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "for a month-long free trial using my",
          "offset": 865,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "link in the description below. Go and",
          "offset": 867,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "14:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "get yourself some free knowledge.",
          "offset": 870,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Now back to Viking Britain.",
          "offset": 875,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 884,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "14:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 890,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "14:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "Before the arrival of the great army in",
          "offset": 895,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "14:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "865,",
          "offset": 897,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "14:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Scandinavian war bands in Britain had",
          "offset": 899,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "14:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "almost always operated autonomously from",
          "offset": 901,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "15:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] one another and generally lacked",
          "offset": 904,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "15:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "unity.",
          "offset": 906,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "15:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 910,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "15:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "Unlike these earlier groups, however,",
          "offset": 913,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "15:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "this one had several leaders, and they",
          "offset": 915,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "15:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "had all come together to work side by",
          "offset": 918,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "15:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "side with the mutual goal of outright",
          "offset": 920,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "15:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "conquest.",
          "offset": 924,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "15:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "Initially, the army seems to have been",
          "offset": 929,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "15:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "led by three war leaders, Ivar, Halaman,",
          "offset": 931,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "15:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Oba.",
          "offset": 936,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "15:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "According to the Norse sagas, these were",
          "offset": 941,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "15:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "the sons of the legendary Viking Ragnar",
          "offset": 944,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "15:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "Lothrock.",
          "offset": 947,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "15:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Each a sea king potentially commanding",
          "offset": 951,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "15:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "thousands of warriors and numerous long",
          "offset": 954,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "15:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "ships.",
          "offset": 957,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "15:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "If the Saras are to be believed, they",
          "offset": 962,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "had come to England to avenge the death",
          "offset": 964,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "of their father, killed by the North",
          "offset": 966,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "16:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Umbrean king Aaylor.",
          "offset": 969,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "16:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 973,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "16:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is just as likely, however, that the",
          "offset": 976,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "16:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "invasion was the natural [music]",
          "offset": 978,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "16:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "culmination of decades of raids into the",
          "offset": 980,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "16:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglo-Saxon kingdoms.",
          "offset": 983,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "16:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "the natural progression by ambitious",
          "offset": 987,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "worshippers of the Norse gods who saw",
          "offset": 989,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "16:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "the means to carve kingdoms out for",
          "offset": 992,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "themselves.",
          "offset": 995,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "16:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "After landing in East Anglia, they",
          "offset": 1005,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "forced the local king Edmund to give",
          "offset": 1008,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "them horses and supplies before they",
          "offset": 1010,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "marched north to capture the city of",
          "offset": 1013,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "16:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "York, capital of North Umbrea, which at",
          "offset": 1015,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "16:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "the time was suffering from civil war",
          "offset": 1019,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "16:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "between two rival claimments,",
          "offset": 1021,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "17:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "one of whom, Aah, is later said to have",
          "offset": 1024,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "17:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "been the king who killed Ragnarok.",
          "offset": 1027,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "17:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "After this battle, North Umbrea would",
          "offset": 1033,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "17:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "become a bastion of Scandinavian culture",
          "offset": 1035,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "17:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "for two centuries to come.",
          "offset": 1037,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "17:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Next, after ravaging North Umbrea, the",
          "offset": 1044,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "17:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "army again went on the move, likely",
          "offset": 1046,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "17:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "gathering more and more warriors to",
          "offset": 1050,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "17:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "their banners from all over the",
          "offset": 1052,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "17:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "Scandinavian world as word spread of",
          "offset": 1054,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "17:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "their victories.",
          "offset": 1057,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "17:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "This time they marched south into Mercia",
          "offset": 1062,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "17:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "where they captured the town of",
          "offset": 1065,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "17:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nottingham",
          "offset": 1066,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "17:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "and faced off against an army led by the",
          "offset": 1069,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "17:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mercian king Burgrid.",
          "offset": 1072,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "17:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mercia called for aid and Wessex",
          "offset": 1078,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "17:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "answered.",
          "offset": 1083,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "18:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet no actual fighting took place as",
          "offset": 1086,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "18:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ivar and his men remained inside the",
          "offset": 1089,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "18:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "walls of Nottingham.",
          "offset": 1092,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "18:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Eventually, it's likely that Burgrid",
          "offset": 1095,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "18:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "paid them to leave and the Mercian",
          "offset": 1097,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "18:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] and West Saxon armies, mostly",
          "offset": 1100,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "18:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "made up of farmers, dispanded to plow",
          "offset": 1102,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "18:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "the fields.",
          "offset": 1105,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "18:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Happy to take mercy and coin for now,",
          "offset": 1112,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "18:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Vikings moved back to York for the",
          "offset": 1115,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "18:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "winter. considerably richer.",
          "offset": 1117,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "18:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 1122,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "18:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "The sons of Lbrock kept their word to",
          "offset": 1125,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "18:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Burgit, heading back to East Anglia in",
          "offset": 1127,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "18:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "the new year, where they conquered the",
          "offset": 1130,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "18:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdom,",
          "offset": 1133,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "18:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "turning its King Edmund into a martyr",
          "offset": 1138,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "18:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "and stamping out the kingdom entirely.",
          "offset": 1141,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "East Anglia would suffer the same fate",
          "offset": 1148,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "as North Umbrea, becoming a safe haven",
          "offset": 1150,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "19:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "for Danes for two centuries to come.",
          "offset": 1154,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "In 870, [music] the army split",
          "offset": 1161,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "19:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "with some remaining in their new lands",
          "offset": 1165,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "in North Umbrea and East Anglia and",
          "offset": 1167,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "19:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "others like Ivar going elsewhere in",
          "offset": 1170,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "19:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain to conquer other lands.",
          "offset": 1173,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "19:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "In his case, the Brethonic Kingdom of",
          "offset": 1176,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "19:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Old Clute in southern Scotland.",
          "offset": 1179,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is Halftan who takes center stage at",
          "offset": 1185,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "this point as he led part of the army",
          "offset": 1187,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "south,",
          "offset": 1190,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "bypassing Mercia entirely to raid deep",
          "offset": 1192,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "19:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "into Wessix.",
          "offset": 1195,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "19:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "After an interval of three years, during",
          "offset": 1200,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "19:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "which time his scouts and spies had",
          "offset": 1202,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "20:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "probably made their own inroads into",
          "offset": 1204,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "20:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Wessex,",
          "offset": 1206,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "20:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfdan along with another warlord, Baxg",
          "offset": 1208,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "20:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "made straight for the town of Reading,",
          "offset": 1212,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "20:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "where they fortified themselves to wait",
          "offset": 1214,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "20:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "for the inevitable West Saxon",
          "offset": 1216,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "20:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "counterattack.",
          "offset": 1218,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "20:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Meanwhile, Ethel Redd and Alfred",
          "offset": 1224,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "20:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "gathered up their levies and made for",
          "offset": 1226,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "20:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Reading where they met with Ethelwolf,",
          "offset": 1229,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "20:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Elderman of Barkshire.",
          "offset": 1232,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "20:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "Together, they attacked Halftdan's men",
          "offset": 1235,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "20:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "at Reading on the 4th of January, but",
          "offset": 1237,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "20:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "suffered an inconclusive defeat.",
          "offset": 1240,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "20:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "The West Saxons regrouped [music] over",
          "offset": 1247,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "20:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "the next few days and again took to the",
          "offset": 1249,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "20:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "field on the ETH at a place called",
          "offset": 1252,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "20:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ashdown",
          "offset": 1254,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "20:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "somewhere [music] on the Barkshire",
          "offset": 1255,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "20:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "Downs.",
          "offset": 1257,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "20:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was there, in the mist and the gloom",
          "offset": 1267,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "21:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "of a midwinter's morning that the most",
          "offset": 1270,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "21:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "decisive battle yet of the war was",
          "offset": 1273,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "21:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "fought.",
          "offset": 1275,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "21:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Etheld divided his army into two,",
          "offset": 1277,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "21:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "positioning the halves on either side of",
          "offset": 1280,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "21:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "a ridgeway with himself in command of",
          "offset": 1282,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "one side and his younger brother Alfred",
          "offset": 1285,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "the other.",
          "offset": 1288,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "21:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "As the Danes approached, they also split",
          "offset": 1292,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "21:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "their army with Halfdan commanding one",
          "offset": 1295,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Baxg the other.",
          "offset": 1297,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "21:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred and his contingent watched on",
          "offset": 1301,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "21:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "from behind their shield wall as the",
          "offset": 1303,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "21:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "Danes drew nearer.",
          "offset": 1305,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "21:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethel, meanwhile, had apparently [music]",
          "offset": 1308,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "21:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "decided that he must pray before the",
          "offset": 1310,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "21:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "battle, refusing to advance until his",
          "offset": 1312,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "21:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "prayer service was complete.",
          "offset": 1315,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "21:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "Seeing that the Danish movement would",
          "offset": 1321,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "22:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "cost him the advantage of the higher",
          "offset": 1323,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "22:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "ground, Alfred took it upon himself to",
          "offset": 1325,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "22:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "charge up the hill without the support",
          "offset": 1328,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "22:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the second contingent, heading",
          "offset": 1330,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "22:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "straight into the heart of the Danish",
          "offset": 1332,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "22:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "lines.",
          "offset": 1334,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "22:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Apparently not realizing that Alfred's",
          "offset": 1340,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "22:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "men only represented half of the West",
          "offset": 1342,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "22:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "Saxon army, the second force of Danes",
          "offset": 1344,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "22:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "also maneuvered into the combat,",
          "offset": 1347,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "22:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "which amounted to little more than a",
          "offset": 1350,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "22:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "brutal hand-to-hand slog of shield wall",
          "offset": 1353,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "22:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "on shield wall.",
          "offset": 1356,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "22:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "After heavy fighting and significant",
          "offset": 1360,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "22:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "losses on either side, Ethel Redd's",
          "offset": 1363,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "22:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "force, whose approach had possibly been",
          "offset": 1366,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "22:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "obscured in mist, finally engaged,",
          "offset": 1368,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "22:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "surprising the Danes and turning the",
          "offset": 1371,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "22:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "battle in the favor of the West Saxons.",
          "offset": 1374,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "22:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 1381,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "23:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Baxg was killed in the fighting and",
          "offset": 1383,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Halftan called his remaining men to fall",
          "offset": 1385,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "23:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "back leaving the West Saxons victorious.",
          "offset": 1388,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "23:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "After six long years of defeat, an",
          "offset": 1393,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "23:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglo-Saxon force had finally emerged",
          "offset": 1396,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "victorious against the great heathen",
          "offset": 1399,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "army.",
          "offset": 1401,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 1404,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "23:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ashdown was by no means a decisive",
          "offset": 1411,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "victory and it was certainly a costly",
          "offset": 1413,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "one.",
          "offset": 1416,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "23:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though the hard fighting may have made",
          "offset": 1418,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Halftan more cautious about his future",
          "offset": 1420,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "plans for Wessix.",
          "offset": 1423,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "23:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "To the fortune of Halddan and his",
          "offset": 1426,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "23:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "remaining warriors who had fallen back",
          "offset": 1427,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "to Reading. However, a batch of fresh",
          "offset": 1429,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "23:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "reinforcements newly arrived from",
          "offset": 1432,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "23:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "overseas glided up the tempames to join",
          "offset": 1435,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "23:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "them.",
          "offset": 1438,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "23:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "This great summer army led by a sea king",
          "offset": 1443,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "24:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "named Guthram would become integral over",
          "offset": 1446,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "24:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "the next seven long years of war.",
          "offset": 1449,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "24:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 1459,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "24:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Etheld and [music] Alfred, now known as",
          "offset": 1463,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "24:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "the boar of Ashdown, continued to fight",
          "offset": 1466,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "24:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Danes over the coming months,",
          "offset": 1469,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "24:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "fighting several more unsuccessful",
          "offset": 1471,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "24:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "engagements against them,",
          "offset": 1473,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "24:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "most notably at Bazing in late January",
          "offset": 1481,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "24:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "and at Martin in March.",
          "offset": 1484,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "24:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "By April, however, Etheld was dead,",
          "offset": 1486,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "24:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "possibly as a result of wounds suffered",
          "offset": 1491,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "24:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "in battle, and Alfred, the boar of",
          "offset": 1493,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "24:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ashdown, replaced him as king.",
          "offset": 1497,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "24:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfdan [music] had had enough of Wessix",
          "offset": 1502,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "25:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "by this point, and he accepted a large",
          "offset": 1504,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "25:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "sum of money in payment from Alfred",
          "offset": 1506,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "25:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] to leave,",
          "offset": 1508,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "25:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "just like he and his brothers had done",
          "offset": 1510,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "25:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "with Burrid back at Nottingham in 868.",
          "offset": 1512,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "25:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 1518,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "25:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Halftan would head north to become king",
          "offset": 1521,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "25:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] in North Umbrea whereas Guthram",
          "offset": 1524,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "25:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "went east to take control of the Vikings",
          "offset": 1527,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "25:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "of East Anglia.",
          "offset": 1529,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "25:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred [music] had saved his kingdom for",
          "offset": 1533,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "25:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "now, but he and all of his subjects knew",
          "offset": 1536,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "25:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Vikings [music]",
          "offset": 1540,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "25:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "would return.",
          "offset": 1541,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "25:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 1545,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "25:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 1550,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "25:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "The invasion of the great heathen army",
          "offset": 1556,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "25:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "in 865 swept through Britain like",
          "offset": 1558,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "25:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "wildfire.",
          "offset": 1561,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "26:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "After six long years of violent",
          "offset": 1565,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "struggle, by 871, the political map of",
          "offset": 1568,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "26:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain had been completely redrawn.",
          "offset": 1571,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Anglo-Saxon kingdoms of East Anglia",
          "offset": 1575,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "and North Umbrea had been swept away,",
          "offset": 1577,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "their ruling dynasties extinguished, and",
          "offset": 1580,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "26:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "their lands taken by the newcomers.",
          "offset": 1583,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "26:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the Midlands, Mercia teetered [music]",
          "offset": 1589,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "on the brink of total collapse.",
          "offset": 1592,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "its eastern portion flooded by marauding",
          "offset": 1596,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] bands of Scandinavians.",
          "offset": 1598,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "26:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the north, the various rulers of",
          "offset": 1610,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "26:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "picked land fought [music] tooth and",
          "offset": 1612,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "nail to retain their own independence.",
          "offset": 1614,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "26:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "And even the Welsh kingdoms had their",
          "offset": 1619,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "26:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "fair share of invasions to deal with.",
          "offset": 1621,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "27:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet the great army wasn't finished yet.",
          "offset": 1625,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "27:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just one kingdom remained relatively",
          "offset": 1630,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "27:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "intact.",
          "offset": 1632,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "27:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Wessix, under its new king, Alfred,",
          "offset": 1636,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "27:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "who had managed to pay a group of",
          "offset": 1644,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "27:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "invading Vikings under Halan to leave",
          "offset": 1646,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "27:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "his kingdom earlier in the year.",
          "offset": 1648,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "In a similar arrangement that Burrid of",
          "offset": 1656,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mercia and Edmund of East Anglia had",
          "offset": 1658,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "27:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "previously made, Alfred knew that sooner",
          "offset": 1660,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "27:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "or later they would be back.",
          "offset": 1664,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Great Heathen Army wasn't an army in",
          "offset": 1673,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "the conventional sense.",
          "offset": 1676,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was a coalition of war bands from all",
          "offset": 1678,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "27:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "over the Scandinavian world that had",
          "offset": 1680,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "28:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "come together to achieve a common goal,",
          "offset": 1683,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "28:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "the outright conquest of Britain.",
          "offset": 1686,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "28:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "When the opportunity presented itself,",
          "offset": 1692,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "28:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "the army tended to split off into parts,",
          "offset": 1695,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "28:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "even more so after vast swavs of land",
          "offset": 1698,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "28:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "began to be conquered and successes won.",
          "offset": 1701,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "28:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "After his withdrawal from Wessix in 871,",
          "offset": 1705,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "28:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Halftdan headed north to North Umbrea",
          "offset": 1709,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "28:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "with around half of the army.",
          "offset": 1712,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "28:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "Around a thousand or so veterans who",
          "offset": 1714,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "28:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "he'd been fighting with since his",
          "offset": 1717,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "28:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "arrival in Britain.",
          "offset": 1718,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "28:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "When he arrived in the north began to",
          "offset": 1723,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "28:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "carve up [music] the land between his",
          "offset": 1725,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "28:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "men and set about plowing the fields.",
          "offset": 1727,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "28:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "This wasn't conquest anymore. It was",
          "offset": 1731,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "28:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "colonization.",
          "offset": 1734,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "28:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ivar, meanwhile, who hadn't been present",
          "offset": 1740,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "during the Wessex campaign, had been",
          "offset": 1743,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "29:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "busy destroying yet another ancient",
          "offset": 1746,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "29:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdom. This time alongside [music]",
          "offset": 1748,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "his ally Olaf the White, a Norse sea",
          "offset": 1751,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "king of Dublin operating in the Irish",
          "offset": 1754,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sea.",
          "offset": 1757,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "29:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Together they attacked Dumbartan Rock,",
          "offset": 1763,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "the capital of the Brethonic Kingdom of",
          "offset": 1766,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "29:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alt Cloot in around 870,",
          "offset": 1769,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "besieging it for 4 months before the",
          "offset": 1772,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "29:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "defenders finally gave in. [cheering]",
          "offset": 1775,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "29:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "There would be no quarter given.",
          "offset": 1779,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Citadel was raised to the ground,",
          "offset": 1782,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "its defenders slain,",
          "offset": 1785,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "29:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "the survivors taken to be sold at the",
          "offset": 1788,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "slave markets of Dublin and York.",
          "offset": 1790,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "29:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ivar made off with so much plunder that",
          "offset": 1796,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "he may have actually retired.",
          "offset": 1798,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "29:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Luckily for Wessix, he wouldn't reappear",
          "offset": 1802,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "again on English shores.",
          "offset": 1804,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though his and Olaf's descendants in",
          "offset": 1807,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Dublin would continue to play a huge",
          "offset": 1809,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "role in Britain and Ireland for",
          "offset": 1812,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "30:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "centuries to come.",
          "offset": 1814,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "30:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Meanwhile, in East Anglia, the second",
          "offset": 1820,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "30:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "half [music] of the army that had",
          "offset": 1823,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "30:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "attacked Wessex was now under the",
          "offset": 1824,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "command of a newcomer. A sea [music]",
          "offset": 1826,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "king recently arrived into Britain with",
          "offset": 1829,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "30:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "conquest very much still on his mind.",
          "offset": 1831,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "30:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "Guthram and [music] his great summer",
          "offset": 1836,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "army had provided a breath of fresh air",
          "offset": 1838,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "into the now exhausted veterans of the",
          "offset": 1840,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "original expedition.",
          "offset": 1843,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "30:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 1845,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "30:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "And now along with [music] Halftan's",
          "offset": 1848,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "30:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "warriors up in North Umbrea, they set",
          "offset": 1850,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "30:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "their eyes upon carving up the severely",
          "offset": 1853,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "30:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "weakened Mercier.",
          "offset": 1856,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "30:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "King Bergrid, Alfred's [music]",
          "offset": 1862,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "31:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "brother-in-law, was forced into exile in",
          "offset": 1864,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "31:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "874 and a puppet ruler, Joel Wolf, put",
          "offset": 1867,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "31:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "in place whilst the Vikings divided up",
          "offset": 1870,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "31:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "the land amongst themselves.",
          "offset": 1873,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "31:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Wessix now stood alone on the very brink",
          "offset": 1878,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "31:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "of destruction.",
          "offset": 1882,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "31:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "The last Anglo-Saxon kingdom not to",
          "offset": 1884,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "31:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "fall.",
          "offset": 1887,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "31:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 875, it seems that the Vikings had",
          "offset": 1892,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "31:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "decided [music] that Alfred had had",
          "offset": 1895,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "31:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "enough of a restbite.",
          "offset": 1897,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "31:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Fleets of [music] five or six vessels",
          "offset": 1900,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "31:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "began to test West Saxon defenses.",
          "offset": 1902,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "31:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "maybe even as a diversionary tactic to",
          "offset": 1905,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "31:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "keep Alfred looking to all of his",
          "offset": 1908,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "31:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "borders for any potential sign of",
          "offset": 1909,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "31:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "invasion.",
          "offset": 1912,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "31:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "Like all of the Anglo-Saxon kingdoms,",
          "offset": 1915,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "31:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 1917,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "31:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "he could call on an army of levies to",
          "offset": 1917,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "31:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "aid him in times of war.",
          "offset": 1919,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "31:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet, [music] these men were primarily",
          "offset": 1922,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "32:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "farmers who fought with equipment and",
          "offset": 1924,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "32:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "armor they owned themselves,",
          "offset": 1926,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "which usually wasn't very much.",
          "offset": 1929,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Fur wasn't a professional standing",
          "offset": 1932,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "army like that of the Scandinavians.",
          "offset": 1934,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "32:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "After the campaigning season was over,",
          "offset": 1938,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "32:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "traditionally [music] they would return",
          "offset": 1940,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "32:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "to their lands as they had done for",
          "offset": 1941,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "32:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "generations.",
          "offset": 1943,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "32:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred's personal retinue of",
          "offset": 1946,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "32:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "professional warriors probably only",
          "offset": 1948,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "consisted of a few hundred men.",
          "offset": 1951,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Guthram, on the other hand, likely had",
          "offset": 1954,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "thousands of warriors. The vast majority",
          "offset": 1957,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "of them hardened from a lifetime of war.",
          "offset": 1960,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "They could live off the land, and as",
          "offset": 1964,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "32:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "long as they could keep supply lines",
          "offset": 1966,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "32:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "open with East Anglia and Mercia, they",
          "offset": 1968,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "could ravage Wessix almost at will,",
          "offset": 1970,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "whilst breaking down the West Saxon will",
          "offset": 1973,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "32:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "to fight,",
          "offset": 1976,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "32:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "which they did from 875 onwards.",
          "offset": 1977,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "32:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "In 876, Guthram thundered across Wessex",
          "offset": 1984,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "33:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "with a large host of mounted warriors.",
          "offset": 1988,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "33:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "He defeated a small force of West Saxons",
          "offset": 1991,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "33:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "led by Alfred on the south coast and",
          "offset": 1994,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "33:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "seized the important regional town of",
          "offset": 1996,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "33:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Wearram.",
          "offset": 1999,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "33:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred sued for peace again and Guthram",
          "offset": 2002,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "33:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "accepted. Both sides probably buying for",
          "offset": 2005,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "33:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "time.",
          "offset": 2008,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "33:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "The next spring, he was on the move",
          "offset": 2010,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "33:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "again. This time heading even further",
          "offset": 2012,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "33:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "west to Exat,",
          "offset": 2015,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "33:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "a town situated near the old border",
          "offset": 2018,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "33:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "between the West Saxons and the Britain",
          "offset": 2021,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "33:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Cornwall,",
          "offset": 2023,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "33:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "a subject people to Wessex, who had been",
          "offset": 2025,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "33:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "known to ally themselves with Vikings in",
          "offset": 2027,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "33:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "order to fight against their overlords.",
          "offset": 2030,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "33:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "Exat also provided a number of options",
          "offset": 2034,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "33:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "for Guthram should he need to [music]",
          "offset": 2037,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "33:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "retreat.",
          "offset": 2039,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "33:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet there was also another reason why",
          "offset": 2042,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "34:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Guthram had chosen to take his men",
          "offset": 2044,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "34:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "there.",
          "offset": 2046,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "34:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Whilst [music] Alfred marched west to",
          "offset": 2050,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "34:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "meet Guthram's army, a vast fleet of 120",
          "offset": 2052,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "34:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "longboats made its way down the north",
          "offset": 2056,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "34:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "coast of Devon with as many as 4,000 men",
          "offset": 2058,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "34:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "aboard.",
          "offset": 2062,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "34:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "The sea king Lothroxen had returned to",
          "offset": 2064,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "34:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "join up with Guthram and ravage Wessix",
          "offset": 2068,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "34:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "for the final definitive time.",
          "offset": 2071,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "34:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "Unlike the other sons of Lothrock, Aba",
          "offset": 2080,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "34:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "is described as ducks,",
          "offset": 2083,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "34:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "perhaps meaning king of the Frieian.",
          "offset": 2086,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "34:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "So he probably had Vikings who had been",
          "offset": 2090,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "34:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "born in [music] Frieia with him. Just",
          "offset": 2092,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "34:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "like Ivar's army probably numbered",
          "offset": 2095,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "34:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "Vikings who had been born in Ireland",
          "offset": 2098,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "34:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "amongst its ranks.",
          "offset": 2100,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "34:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "It's thought that force originated in",
          "offset": 2103,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "35:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ireland and may have overwintered on the",
          "offset": 2106,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "35:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "south coast of Wales.",
          "offset": 2109,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "35:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "The situation looked grim for Alfred",
          "offset": 2114,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "35:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "who must surely have contemplated the",
          "offset": 2117,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "35:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "grizzly fates already handed out to",
          "offset": 2119,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "35:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "Edmund of East Anglia and Aaylor of",
          "offset": 2122,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "35:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "North Umbrea.",
          "offset": 2124,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "35:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "In one of the most fortuitous moments of",
          "offset": 2132,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "35:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "chance ever to befall England, however,",
          "offset": 2134,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "35:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Aba's fleet was destroyed by a freak",
          "offset": 2138,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "35:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "storm of Swanage on the south coast of",
          "offset": 2140,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "35:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Dorset,",
          "offset": 2143,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "35:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "leaving the survivors to limp back to",
          "offset": 2145,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "35:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "their base in southern Wales.",
          "offset": 2147,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "35:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "Guthrram, meanwhile, upon hearing the",
          "offset": 2153,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "35:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "news, abandoned his plan and rode north",
          "offset": 2155,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "35:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "to Gloucester in the south of Mercia.",
          "offset": 2158,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "35:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "However much Alfred may have seen the",
          "offset": 2164,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "36:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "storm as a divine judgment against the",
          "offset": 2166,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "36:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "heathens,",
          "offset": 2168,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "36:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "he was still beset on all sides by",
          "offset": 2170,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "armies of pyatical [music] raiders,",
          "offset": 2172,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "intent on personally sacrificing him to",
          "offset": 2174,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "36:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Odin and usurping his kingdom.",
          "offset": 2177,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "On the 6th of January 878,",
          "offset": 2184,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the midst of the Christmas festival",
          "offset": 2188,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "36:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "that was an important part of",
          "offset": 2189,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "36:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglo-Saxon culture,",
          "offset": 2191,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "Guthram threw all of his cards on the",
          "offset": 2193,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "36:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "table, suddenly appearing at Alfred's",
          "offset": 2196,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "royal estate at Chippenham with a",
          "offset": 2199,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "36:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "mounted force of his best outriders.",
          "offset": 2201,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "This surprise attack, possibly launched",
          "offset": 2207,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "36:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "in conjunction with treacherous West",
          "offset": 2209,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "36:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "Saxon Elderman, very nearly ended Alfred",
          "offset": 2211,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "36:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "there and then.",
          "offset": 2215,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "36:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "He barely escaped with his life with",
          "offset": 2219,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "36:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "just a handful of followers, whilst",
          "offset": 2222,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Guthram sent his warriors in swift",
          "offset": 2224,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "pursuit.",
          "offset": 2227,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "37:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 2232,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "37:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred fled west deep into the",
          "offset": 2238,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "37:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "marshlands of the Somerset levels.",
          "offset": 2240,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "At the time, a vast area of undrained,",
          "offset": 2245,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "boggy wetlands.",
          "offset": 2248,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "He knew the area well, [music] having",
          "offset": 2250,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "37:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "spent much of his youth there, hunting",
          "offset": 2253,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "37:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "on the royal estates with his brothers",
          "offset": 2255,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "37:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "and his father.",
          "offset": 2257,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "37:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "Guthram [music] had no such knowledge of",
          "offset": 2262,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "the intricate riverways and secret paths",
          "offset": 2265,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "37:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "that crisscrossed the [music] fence.",
          "offset": 2268,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "37:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was there [music] on the island of",
          "offset": 2274,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "Athlny with just a few hundred followers",
          "offset": 2275,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "37:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "that Alfred, [music] now mostly",
          "offset": 2278,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "37:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "dispossessed of his kingdom, made his",
          "offset": 2280,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "38:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "final stand.",
          "offset": 2283,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "38:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "It is at this moment had Alfred [music]",
          "offset": 2288,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "38:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "failed or given up and ran like Burgard",
          "offset": 2291,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "38:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Mercia, England would have become",
          "offset": 2293,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "38:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Danland.",
          "offset": 2297,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "38:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Guthram stood on the very brink of",
          "offset": 2305,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "38:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "becoming king [music] in not just East",
          "offset": 2308,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "38:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglia and parts of Mercia but Wessex",
          "offset": 2310,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "38:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "too. the richest and most powerful",
          "offset": 2313,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "38:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] of the Anglo-Saxon kingdoms. For",
          "offset": 2316,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "38:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "the next several months, it was Alfred",
          "offset": 2319,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "38:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "who was forced to launch piratical",
          "offset": 2322,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "38:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] raids into his own kingdom, now",
          "offset": 2324,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "38:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "overrun by Guthram's warriors.",
          "offset": 2328,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "38:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "Uber, meanwhile, had probably spent the",
          "offset": 2334,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "38:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "winter in a pirate base off the coast of",
          "offset": 2336,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "38:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Divid.",
          "offset": 2339,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "38:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "After hearing of Guthram's success,",
          "offset": 2340,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "39:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "however, he returned to [music] Wessex",
          "offset": 2342,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "39:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "to take part in the carving up of the",
          "offset": 2344,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "39:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdom. This time with only 23 ships,",
          "offset": 2347,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "39:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "they made landfall [music] somewhere in",
          "offset": 2354,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "39:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "northern Devon near a fortress called",
          "offset": 2357,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "39:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Arks Sinwit. It was a location which may",
          "offset": 2359,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "39:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "have been intended to corner Alfred in a",
          "offset": 2362,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "39:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Pinsir movement after his withdrawal to",
          "offset": 2365,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "39:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "the wetlands of Somerset.",
          "offset": 2367,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "39:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rather than the easy campaign he had",
          "offset": 2371,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "39:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "hoped for, however, Aba was met there by",
          "offset": 2372,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "39:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "the elderman of Somerset, Oda, who had",
          "offset": 2375,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "39:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "levied his fured men to drive out the",
          "offset": 2378,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "39:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "invaders.",
          "offset": 2381,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "39:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was there at the battle of Sinwit in",
          "offset": 2385,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "39:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "878, a stride the Irish Sea that Aba,",
          "offset": 2388,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "39:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "the last living son of Lothrock, was",
          "offset": 2392,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "39:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "struck down in battle.",
          "offset": 2395,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "39:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "Guthram was left overextended by the",
          "offset": 2402,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "40:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "destruction of Aba's force at Sinwit.",
          "offset": 2404,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "40:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "And this appears to have allowed Alfred",
          "offset": 2408,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "and his elderman to break up Guthram's",
          "offset": 2410,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "exposed supply lines and lines of",
          "offset": 2413,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "communication.",
          "offset": 2415,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "40:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred then called as many of the feared",
          "offset": 2419,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "men of Somerset, Wiltshire, [music] and",
          "offset": 2422,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "40:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "Hampshire as he could.",
          "offset": 2424,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "40:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "the only counties left to have any",
          "offset": 2428,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] sort of semblance of West Saxon",
          "offset": 2431,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "government.",
          "offset": 2433,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "For three long days between the 4th and",
          "offset": 2436,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "the 7th of May, they waited at a local",
          "offset": 2438,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "40:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "rallying point called Eggbert Stone for",
          "offset": 2441,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "their warriors [music] to arrive from",
          "offset": 2444,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "all corners of the realm.",
          "offset": 2445,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "40:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 2450,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "40:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "Finally, once a [music] sufficient force",
          "offset": 2454,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "had been raised, probably numbering in",
          "offset": 2457,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "40:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "the thousands with only a few hundred",
          "offset": 2459,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "40:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "professional household soldiers, they",
          "offset": 2462,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "41:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "marched to Edington,",
          "offset": 2465,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "41:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "where Alfred engaged Guthram's warriors",
          "offset": 2472,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "41:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "in one final definitive battle that",
          "offset": 2475,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "41:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "would decide the fate of Wessix once and",
          "offset": 2478,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "41:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "for all.",
          "offset": 2480,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "41:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "A ferocious battle ensued as the two",
          "offset": 2487,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "41:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "shield walls crashed against one",
          "offset": 2490,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "41:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "another.",
          "offset": 2491,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "41:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "All day the two sides fought until",
          "offset": 2497,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "41:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "finally the smaller Danish force broke",
          "offset": 2500,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "41:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "and fell back to their fortress at",
          "offset": 2503,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "41:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "Chippenham.",
          "offset": 2505,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "41:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "The West [music] Saxons had no mercy for",
          "offset": 2509,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "41:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Danes that day,",
          "offset": 2511,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "41:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "killing everyone who didn't make it",
          "offset": 2516,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "41:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "inside the fortress and besieging",
          "offset": 2518,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "41:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Guthram for 2 weeks before he sued for",
          "offset": 2520,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "42:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "peace.",
          "offset": 2523,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "42:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "In addition to offering the customary",
          "offset": 2528,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "42:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "hostages and promising to leave Wessex",
          "offset": 2530,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "42:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "for good, the Vikings promised that",
          "offset": 2533,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "42:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Guthram would be baptized as a",
          "offset": 2535,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "42:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Christian.",
          "offset": 2538,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "42:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Unlike previous treaties that the Danes",
          "offset": 2544,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "42:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "had promised to keep and later reneged",
          "offset": 2546,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "42:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "on, these men were pushed up against a",
          "offset": 2548,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "42:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "wall and Alfred was convinced that they",
          "offset": 2551,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "42:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "would keep their word.",
          "offset": 2553,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "42:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "At the Treaty of Wedmore in 879, Guthram",
          "offset": 2558,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "42:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "was baptized, taking the Christian name",
          "offset": 2562,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "42:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "Athlan with Alfred as his godfather.",
          "offset": 2565,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "42:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "After a few more minor engagements where",
          "offset": 2572,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "42:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "minor Danish warlords defied Guthram's",
          "offset": 2575,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "42:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "orders to raid the Wessex borderlands,",
          "offset": 2577,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "42:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Danes finally pulled out of Wessix",
          "offset": 2580,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "43:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "entirely,",
          "offset": 2584,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "43:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "retreating back to [music] East Anglia,",
          "offset": 2585,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "where Guthram became king.",
          "offset": 2587,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "43:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "In 886, Mercia was divided between",
          "offset": 2593,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Guthram and Alfred",
          "offset": 2597,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "43:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "with the Anglo-Saxons [music] retaining",
          "offset": 2599,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "43:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "control of the western portion of the",
          "offset": 2601,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "43:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "county and the Danes settling the east.",
          "offset": 2603,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "43:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was an extraordinary turnaround for",
          "offset": 2608,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "43:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred and the West [music] Saxons.",
          "offset": 2610,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "43:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Not only had he saved his kingdom, but",
          "offset": 2612,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "43:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "he now found himself in a [music]",
          "offset": 2615,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "43:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "relatively strong position. Tensions",
          "offset": 2617,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "43:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "would flare up every now and again, but",
          "offset": 2620,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "43:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "by and large, Guthram would keep the",
          "offset": 2622,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "peace, giving Alfred the breathing room",
          "offset": 2625,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "he needed to fortify his country against",
          "offset": 2628,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "further invasions from overseas,",
          "offset": 2631,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "of which there would be many more over",
          "offset": 2634,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "43:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "the coming is.",
          "offset": 2637,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "43:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred's surprise victory over the",
          "offset": 2648,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "44:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Vikings in 878",
          "offset": 2650,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "44:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "both ensured the survival of his kingdom",
          "offset": 2653,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "44:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "and allowed the West Saxons the",
          "offset": 2656,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "44:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "breathing room needed to regroup and",
          "offset": 2658,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "44:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "prepare for the inevitable next attack",
          "offset": 2661,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "44:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "to come.",
          "offset": 2663,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "44:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though Guthram retired to East Anglia",
          "offset": 2667,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "44:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "after the battle to rule there as king",
          "offset": 2670,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "44:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "under the Christian name Athlan,",
          "offset": 2673,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "44:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "Wessix still faced [music] potential",
          "offset": 2677,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "44:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "attack from elsewhere.",
          "offset": 2679,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "44:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just as Guthram had successfully carved",
          "offset": 2684,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "44:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself out a kingdom well over a decade",
          "offset": 2686,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "44:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "after the initial arrival of the great",
          "offset": 2689,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "44:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "heathen army,",
          "offset": 2691,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "44:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "another could just as easily come and do",
          "offset": 2693,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "44:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "the same.",
          "offset": 2696,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "44:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was now time for a new strategy.",
          "offset": 2698,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "44:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred spent the 880s converting the",
          "offset": 2705,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "45:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "various market towns of his kingdom into",
          "offset": 2708,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "45:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "burrs, which would act as fortified safe",
          "offset": 2711,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "45:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "havens and meeting points for local",
          "offset": 2714,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "45:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "militias to fight against the sudden",
          "offset": 2716,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "45:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "appearance of Vikings.",
          "offset": 2719,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "45:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though Alfred was technically at peace",
          "offset": 2723,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "45:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "with Guthram for the rest of the old sea",
          "offset": 2725,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "45:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "king's life, there was no guarantee that",
          "offset": 2728,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "45:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "he wouldn't try his luck again.",
          "offset": 2730,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "45:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "or at least harbor those who would.",
          "offset": 2733,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "45:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred also forged a lasting alliance",
          "offset": 2739,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "45:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "with the portion of Mercia still under",
          "offset": 2742,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "45:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglo-Saxon control",
          "offset": 2744,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "45:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "now under the rule of a warlord of",
          "offset": 2748,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "45:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "unknown origins named Ethel",
          "offset": 2750,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "45:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "after the death of King Chiel in around",
          "offset": 2753,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "45:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "879.",
          "offset": 2755,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "45:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "The alliance was [music] sealed by the",
          "offset": 2759,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "45:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "marriage of Alfred's eldest daughter,",
          "offset": 2761,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "46:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethelfled, to Ethel in the early 880s,",
          "offset": 2764,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "46:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "who began to rule under the title Lord",
          "offset": 2768,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "46:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the Mercians,",
          "offset": 2770,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "46:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "apparently under some [music] degree of",
          "offset": 2774,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "46:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "West Saxon overlordship.",
          "offset": 2776,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "46:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred also achieved a similar",
          "offset": 2780,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "46:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "arrangement with the southern Welsh",
          "offset": 2783,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "46:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdoms during this time whose rulers",
          "offset": 2784,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "46:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "were hemmed in by the expansionist sons",
          "offset": 2787,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "46:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Rodri the Great in Gwen and Pois.",
          "offset": 2790,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "46:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "The most powerful of these northern",
          "offset": 2795,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "46:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Welsh kings, Anarad App Rodri may have",
          "offset": 2797,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "46:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "allied himself with the Vikings of",
          "offset": 2801,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "46:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yorvik against Wessix before eventually",
          "offset": 2803,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "46:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "he too accepted West Saxon overlordship.",
          "offset": 2806,
          "duration": 10,
          "formattedTime": "46:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "thus securing Alfred's western border.",
          "offset": 2811,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "46:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ultimately, Guthram kept the peace with",
          "offset": 2820,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "46:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "Wessex until his death in 890.",
          "offset": 2822,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "47:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though just 2 years later, the Burr",
          "offset": 2828,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "47:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "system would face its first real test",
          "offset": 2832,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "47:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "when two massive fleets of raiders",
          "offset": 2835,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "47:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "comprising of over 300 longboats under a",
          "offset": 2837,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "47:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "sea king named Haston arrived on the",
          "offset": 2840,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "47:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Kentish shore to try their luck against",
          "offset": 2843,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "47:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "the West Saxons.",
          "offset": 2846,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "47:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet times had changed over the last",
          "offset": 2851,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "47:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "decade. And after some initial",
          "offset": 2854,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "47:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "victories, Wessix held out.",
          "offset": 2856,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "47:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 896, Hast's men either left Britain",
          "offset": 2864,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "47:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "entirely or dispersed into East Anglia.",
          "offset": 2868,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "47:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Burr system had worked.",
          "offset": 2872,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "47:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 2878,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "47:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Upon his death in 899,",
          "offset": 2881,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "48:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred the [music] Great left his",
          "offset": 2885,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "48:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdom to his eldest son and heir,",
          "offset": 2887,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "48:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Edward.",
          "offset": 2889,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "48:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet the succession was not a smooth one.",
          "offset": 2893,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "48:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "There was another who sought the throne,",
          "offset": 2897,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "48:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred's nephew, Ethelwald.",
          "offset": 2900,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "48:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "After an initial engagement between the",
          "offset": 2905,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "48:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "two cousins, Ethelwald fled north to the",
          "offset": 2907,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "48:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "North Umbrean Danlaw where he was",
          "offset": 2910,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "48:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "enthusiastically accepted by the local",
          "offset": 2913,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "48:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "rulers.",
          "offset": 2915,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "48:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "Apparently happy to accept him as king",
          "offset": 2917,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "48:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "in Yorvik.",
          "offset": 2920,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "48:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though this may very well have been a",
          "offset": 2922,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "48:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "ruse to use Ethelwald to finally conquer",
          "offset": 2923,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "48:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "the last Anglo-Saxon kingdom once and",
          "offset": 2927,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "48:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "for all.",
          "offset": 2930,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "48:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "During this relatively early phase in",
          "offset": 2934,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "48:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "the history of the Danlaw, official",
          "offset": 2936,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "48:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "titles seemed to have carried little",
          "offset": 2939,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "48:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "real weight.",
          "offset": 2941,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "49:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Lands generally being held by a ruling",
          "offset": 2946,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "49:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "class of aristocrats rather than a",
          "offset": 2948,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "49:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "single king.",
          "offset": 2951,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "49:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nevertheless, Ethelwald spent his time",
          "offset": 2957,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "49:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "in North Umbrea. gathering an army",
          "offset": 2960,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "49:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "together. And by 9001 or 9002, he sailed",
          "offset": 2962,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "49:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "south to Essex,",
          "offset": 2967,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "49:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "where he was apparently [music] also",
          "offset": 2973,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "49:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "accepted as king by the local",
          "offset": 2975,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "49:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "Scandinavian elite who now ruled there.",
          "offset": 2977,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "49:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "From this base of power, he was able to",
          "offset": 2981,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "49:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "gain influence over the Vikings of East",
          "offset": 2983,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "49:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglia, specifically their new king,",
          "offset": 2985,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "49:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Eric, who joined him on a deep raid into",
          "offset": 2988,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "49:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mercia.",
          "offset": 2992,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "49:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "By December 9002, Edward had also raised",
          "offset": 2996,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "49:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "an army likely comprised of West Saxons,",
          "offset": 3000,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "49:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mercians, and Kentishmen,",
          "offset": 3003,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "50:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "and his forces finally succeeded [music]",
          "offset": 3006,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "50:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "in catching Ethelwald in a vicious",
          "offset": 3008,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "50:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "battle in the marshy lowlands near the",
          "offset": 3010,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "50:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] river Hull.",
          "offset": 3013,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "50:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "By day end, it was apparently the",
          "offset": 3017,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "50:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] Danes who emerged victorious.",
          "offset": 3020,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "50:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet the men of Kent exacted a heavy toll",
          "offset": 3023,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "50:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "for their victory.",
          "offset": 3026,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "50:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Not only was the East Anglian king Eric",
          "offset": 3030,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "50:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "killed, but Ethelwald too along with the",
          "offset": 3032,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "50:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "Kentish leader Sighhelm.",
          "offset": 3036,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "50:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "The real winner being Edward.",
          "offset": 3041,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "50:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "With Ethelwald out of the way, Edward",
          "offset": 3044,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "50:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "could now finally focus on consolidating",
          "offset": 3047,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "50:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "his rule at home, which he would do for",
          "offset": 3049,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "50:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "close to a decade to come",
          "offset": 3053,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "50:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the western portion of Mercia.",
          "offset": 3060,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Meanwhile, Ethel [music] and Ethel fled",
          "offset": 3062,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "51:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "had been busy too, following the example",
          "offset": 3065,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "51:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "set by Alfred in fortifying their",
          "offset": 3068,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "51:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "frontier with the Danlaw by building",
          "offset": 3070,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "51:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "burrs wherever they could.",
          "offset": 3073,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "51:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "As part of Ethel's marriage arrangement",
          "offset": 3077,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "51:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "with Ethelfled,",
          "offset": 3079,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "51:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred had given the Mercians control of",
          "offset": 3081,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "the city of London,",
          "offset": 3083,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "a hefty source of income.",
          "offset": 3086,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Together, the two rulers oversaw a",
          "offset": 3088,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "51:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "revival of mercy and power,",
          "offset": 3091,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "51:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "though in a reduced territorial area.",
          "offset": 3095,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "51:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "And Ethel fled, in particular, became",
          "offset": 3099,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "51:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "extremely popular amongst her adopted",
          "offset": 3101,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "people, for all intents and purposes,",
          "offset": 3103,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "51:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "seeming to become a Mercian.",
          "offset": 3106,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "51:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet soon enough, the Mercians would yet",
          "offset": 3110,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "51:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "again be forced to go on the defensive.",
          "offset": 3113,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "51:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just as Edward had been fighting his",
          "offset": 3119,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "51:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "cousin in 9002, a mass exodus of Vikings",
          "offset": 3120,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "52:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "from Ireland had led to the settlement",
          "offset": 3124,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "52:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "of a large group of exiles in the lands",
          "offset": 3127,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "52:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "just to the north of the mercen held",
          "offset": 3130,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "52:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "town of Chester.",
          "offset": 3132,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "52:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "An old Roman fortress, its walls still",
          "offset": 3134,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "52:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "visible today, formidable in Edward's",
          "offset": 3138,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "52:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "day.",
          "offset": 3141,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "52:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though the Mercians may have intended",
          "offset": 3145,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "52:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "these Irish [music] Vikings to act as a",
          "offset": 3147,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "52:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "buffer against the everpresent power of",
          "offset": 3150,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "52:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Danlaw,",
          "offset": 3152,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "52:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "by 9007 the Irish Vikings had apparently",
          "offset": 3154,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "52:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "aligned themselves with the Danlaw to",
          "offset": 3157,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "52:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "besiege Chester.",
          "offset": 3160,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "52:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "When the Mercian army went [music] north",
          "offset": 3168,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "52:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "that year to deal with this new threat,",
          "offset": 3170,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "52:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "tellingly it wasn't Ethel Red who went,",
          "offset": 3173,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "52:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "but the Lady Ethel fled with full",
          "offset": 3177,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "52:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "authority to act on his behalf due to",
          "offset": 3180,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "his [music] apparent incapacitation due",
          "offset": 3183,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "to illness.",
          "offset": 3185,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "53:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "What happened next is unclear with the",
          "offset": 3191,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "West Saxonymade Anglo-Saxon [music]",
          "offset": 3194,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Chronicle possibly not wishing to report",
          "offset": 3196,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "on a victory achieved solely by the",
          "offset": 3198,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mercians.",
          "offset": 3201,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "53:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nonetheless, the Vikings were defeated",
          "offset": 3204,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "at Chester. And in the aftermath, it was",
          "offset": 3206,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "53:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethelfled, not Ethel Red, who was firmly",
          "offset": 3209,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "53:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "in the driver's seat.",
          "offset": 3212,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Mercians were going on the",
          "offset": 3215,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "offensive.",
          "offset": 3217,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "53:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "In 909, the Anglo-Saxon Chronicle",
          "offset": 3224,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "records a joint [music] Mercian West",
          "offset": 3227,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Saxon offensive deep into Viking",
          "offset": 3229,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "territory to retrieve the relics of the",
          "offset": 3232,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "53:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "famed North Umbrean King Oswald.",
          "offset": 3234,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "53:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "The strike force also took the",
          "offset": 3240,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "53:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "opportunity [music] to pillage the",
          "offset": 3242,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "54:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "relatively inaccessible lands of Lindsay",
          "offset": 3243,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "for 5 weeks until they retreated before",
          "offset": 3245,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "54:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yorvik could react.",
          "offset": 3249,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "54:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though no leader is recorded for this",
          "offset": 3258,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "54:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "expedition, it remains possible that",
          "offset": 3260,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "Edward's eldest [music] son, Athlan,",
          "offset": 3262,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "54:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "took part.",
          "offset": 3265,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "54:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though he was the eldest child, Athlan",
          "offset": 3269,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "probably wasn't Edward's successor at",
          "offset": 3272,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "this time. Instead, being fostered by",
          "offset": 3275,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "54:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "his aunt Ethelfled [music]",
          "offset": 3278,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "in Mercia.",
          "offset": 3279,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "54:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "From around this point onwards, he",
          "offset": 3283,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "54:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "likely took part in most of the major",
          "offset": 3285,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mercian offensives whilst he trained for",
          "offset": 3287,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "a life in the military.",
          "offset": 3290,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "But we will learn much more of him",
          "offset": 3293,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "54:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "later.",
          "offset": 3295,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "54:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 3301,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "55:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "In 910, the North Umbreans retaliated,",
          "offset": 3304,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "55:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "launching a massive raid deep into",
          "offset": 3308,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "55:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mercia.",
          "offset": 3311,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "55:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "They ravaged the countryside, loading up",
          "offset": 3313,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "55:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "on plunder before beginning the journey",
          "offset": 3315,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "55:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "back north.",
          "offset": 3318,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "55:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was then near Tetan Hall at a place",
          "offset": 3320,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "55:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "named Woden'sfield",
          "offset": 3324,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "55:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "that a combined West Saxon Mercian army",
          "offset": 3326,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "55:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "caught the Vikings by surprise.",
          "offset": 3330,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "55:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 3333,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "55:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the ensuing bloodbath, the entire",
          "offset": 3338,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "55:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "leadership of the Viking force was",
          "offset": 3341,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "55:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "killed,",
          "offset": 3343,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "55:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "crippling Yorvik for years to come and",
          "offset": 3344,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "55:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "scoring a decisive victory.",
          "offset": 3348,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "55:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tetanhal was a turning point in many",
          "offset": 3353,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "55:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "ways.",
          "offset": 3356,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "55:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was around this time that Ethel",
          "offset": 3358,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "55:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "finally passed away.",
          "offset": 3360,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "55:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "And quite astonishingly, despite being a",
          "offset": 3362,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "56:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "woman in [music] a militaristic",
          "offset": 3365,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "56:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "maledominated society, Ethelfled was",
          "offset": 3366,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "56:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "chosen as his successor,",
          "offset": 3370,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "56:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "ruling under the title Lady of the",
          "offset": 3372,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "56:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mercians.",
          "offset": 3375,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "56:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 3377,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "56:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though being in no position to argue",
          "offset": 3379,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "56:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "with her younger brother, in a signal of",
          "offset": 3381,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "56:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "what was to come close to a decade",
          "offset": 3384,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "56:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "later, she was also forced to relinquish",
          "offset": 3386,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "56:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "control of London to Wessex.",
          "offset": 3388,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "56:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethelfled would continue [music] to",
          "offset": 3394,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "56:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "rule. Though as she had no male heir, it",
          "offset": 3396,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "56:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "was the beginning of the end for",
          "offset": 3400,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "56:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "independent Mercia.",
          "offset": 3402,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "56:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 3405,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "56:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "For the next 8 years, Ethelfled [music]",
          "offset": 3408,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "56:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "tirelessly dedicated her time to",
          "offset": 3411,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "56:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "building burrs, not only along the",
          "offset": 3413,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "56:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "frontier with the five burers to the",
          "offset": 3415,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "56:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "east, but also against the Welsh",
          "offset": 3417,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "56:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdoms to the west, [music]",
          "offset": 3420,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "56:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "where the sons of Rodri, who had allied",
          "offset": 3423,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "57:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "with her father, [music] had now grown",
          "offset": 3425,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "57:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "old,",
          "offset": 3427,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "57:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "threatening more uncertainty in the",
          "offset": 3429,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "future.",
          "offset": 3431,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "57:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "A state of perpetual warfare existed",
          "offset": 3434,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "with the five burers of eastern Mercuria",
          "offset": 3437,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "57:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] during this time",
          "offset": 3439,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "57:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "with occasional raids recorded from the",
          "offset": 3443,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "towns of Leicester and Bedford into",
          "offset": 3445,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "57:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "western Mercuria.",
          "offset": 3447,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "57:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Edward meanwhile was finally ready to go",
          "offset": 3451,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "on the offensive against the Vikings on",
          "offset": 3454,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "57:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "his own borders.",
          "offset": 3456,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "57:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "Between 911 and 913, he moved his forces",
          "offset": 3458,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "57:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "by land and by sea into Essex,",
          "offset": 3462,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "57:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "fortifying the town of Molden and",
          "offset": 3465,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "57:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "attempting to bring the area under full",
          "offset": 3468,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "57:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "West Saxon control.",
          "offset": 3470,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "57:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "For the first time since the coming of",
          "offset": 3476,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "57:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Northmen, Wessex was growing larger.",
          "offset": 3478,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "57:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "And he now also had a base from which he",
          "offset": 3484,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "58:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "could attack his main prize,",
          "offset": 3487,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "58:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "East Anglia.",
          "offset": 3490,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "58:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet in 914, any potential attacks",
          "offset": 3495,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "58:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethelfled or Edward might have wanted to",
          "offset": 3498,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "58:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "make suddenly came crashing to a",
          "offset": 3500,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "58:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "standstill.",
          "offset": 3503,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "58:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "Across the channel in Britany, a massive",
          "offset": 3507,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "58:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Viking fleet had just conquered the",
          "offset": 3510,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "58:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "entire region, extinguishing its ruling",
          "offset": 3513,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "58:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "family. And now, under the leadership of",
          "offset": 3516,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "58:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "two warlords named Rald and Otier, they",
          "offset": 3520,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "58:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "rode the momentum of that victory all",
          "offset": 3523,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "58:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "the way over the channel to Britain to",
          "offset": 3526,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "58:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "try their luck again.",
          "offset": 3529,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "58:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sailing up through the Bristol Channel,",
          "offset": 3534,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "58:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "they headed into the river 7 in an",
          "offset": 3536,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "58:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "attempt to take the Mercians by",
          "offset": 3538,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "58:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "surprise.",
          "offset": 3540,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet once again, Ethel fled was ready for",
          "offset": 3542,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "59:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "them, pushing the Vikings out of Mercia",
          "offset": 3545,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "59:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "and into Wales, and killing Rolled in",
          "offset": 3549,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "the process.",
          "offset": 3552,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "The children of Alfred were now [music]",
          "offset": 3554,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "expert Viking fighters. They were even",
          "offset": 3556,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "59:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "more ruthless than he had ever been.",
          "offset": 3560,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "59:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "Knowing that any hint of weakness would",
          "offset": 3563,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "59:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "bring disaster,",
          "offset": 3566,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "59:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Edward pursued Otterier and his",
          "offset": 3571,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "59:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "remaining vessels all the way to the",
          "offset": 3573,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "island of Flatome near Cardiff, where he",
          "offset": 3576,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "59:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "blockaded them for weeks.",
          "offset": 3579,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "59:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Finally, Otterier gave up on England",
          "offset": 3584,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "altogether, heading across the sea to",
          "offset": 3586,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ireland.",
          "offset": 3589,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "The stage was now set for the final",
          "offset": 3591,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "59:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "confrontation of the war.",
          "offset": 3593,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "59:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 914, [music]",
          "offset": 3598,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "59:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Edward 2 was making inroads into the",
          "offset": 3599,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "59:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "five burers,",
          "offset": 3602,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "forcing the submission of some, but not",
          "offset": 3604,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "all, of the Vikings of Bedford and",
          "offset": 3606,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Northampton.",
          "offset": 3609,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "60:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 916, he was back at Molden where he",
          "offset": 3612,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "continued to make preparations for",
          "offset": 3615,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "battle.",
          "offset": 3617,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethelfled, meanwhile, was forced to",
          "offset": 3620,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "60:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "campaign into Wales [music] in 916,",
          "offset": 3622,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "60:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "where the sons of Rodri, who had allied",
          "offset": 3626,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "themselves to Alfred, had now finally",
          "offset": 3628,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "60:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "passed away,",
          "offset": 3631,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "leaving their successors, who were",
          "offset": 3634,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "unknown quantities, as potential [music]",
          "offset": 3636,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "threats.",
          "offset": 3638,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "60:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 917, both [music] Edward and",
          "offset": 3643,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethelfled were ready for their final",
          "offset": 3646,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "60:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "assaults upon the Danlaw.",
          "offset": 3648,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "60:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "A large force of Danes from the southern",
          "offset": 3659,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "60:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "portion of the five burers allied",
          "offset": 3662,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "61:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] themselves with the East",
          "offset": 3664,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "61:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglians",
          "offset": 3666,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "who finally decided to make a move.",
          "offset": 3667,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "They attempted to mirror the success of",
          "offset": 3672,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Saxons by building their own burr at",
          "offset": 3674,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Tempsford in Bedfordshire.",
          "offset": 3677,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Within weeks, however, Edward's forces",
          "offset": 3680,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "stormed the burr, killing the East",
          "offset": 3682,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglian king and sweeping onwards to",
          "offset": 3685,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "take the whole of East Anglia and",
          "offset": 3688,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "southeastern Mercuria.",
          "offset": 3690,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just if this hammer blow against the",
          "offset": 3693,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "Danes hadn't been enough, Ethel fled was",
          "offset": 3695,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "61:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "also on the move. In mid 917, she",
          "offset": 3698,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "marched her now elite army across the",
          "offset": 3702,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "border directly heading towards the",
          "offset": 3704,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "burough of Derby",
          "offset": 3707,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "where they laid siege to the town.",
          "offset": 3709,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "After a fierce battle where several of",
          "offset": 3713,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "61:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "her leading fains were killed in the",
          "offset": 3715,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "61:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "fighting, the town fell",
          "offset": 3717,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "61:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 3723,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "62:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "and with it large swavthes of eastern",
          "offset": 3726,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "62:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mercia.",
          "offset": 3729,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 918, [music]",
          "offset": 3731,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "62:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Leester was the next to submit, closely",
          "offset": 3733,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "62:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "followed by the three other burs of",
          "offset": 3736,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "62:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Stamford [music]",
          "offset": 3739,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "62:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Nottingham, and Lincoln.",
          "offset": 3740,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "Under Ethel fled, Mercia had [music]",
          "offset": 3745,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "62:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "finally completed its reconquest and now",
          "offset": 3747,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "62:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "found itself with nearly the same",
          "offset": 3751,
