        },
        {
          "text": "power in Dublin,",
          "offset": 3774,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "62:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "which now threatens [music] to bring",
          "offset": 3779,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "62:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "North Umbrea under its control.",
          "offset": 3780,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ultimately, the deal never materialized.",
          "offset": 3787,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "63:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ethelfled [music]",
          "offset": 3790,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "63:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "passed away that same year, succeeded by",
          "offset": 3791,
          "duration": 10,
          "formattedTime": "63:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "her only child, a daughter named Elfwin.",
          "offset": 3795,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "63:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 918, all of England south of the",
          "offset": 3807,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Humber was subject to Anglo-Saxon",
          "offset": 3810,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "control.",
          "offset": 3813,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "63:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "All that now remained for Edward to do",
          "offset": 3817,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "was to march north to Tamworth to seize",
          "offset": 3820,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Elfwin, place her in a monastery for",
          "offset": 3824,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "life, and finally incorporate Mercia",
          "offset": 3826,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "63:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "into his ever growing kingdom.",
          "offset": 3830,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "For the relatively unknown Elfwin living",
          "offset": 3833,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "in a heavily maledominated society,",
          "offset": 3836,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "63:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "this was a relatively easy [music]",
          "offset": 3840,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "63:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "process.",
          "offset": 3842,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "64:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Like Alfred before him, Edward then",
          "offset": 3849,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "64:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "seems to have achieved the feelalty of",
          "offset": 3851,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "64:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "the five Welsh kingdoms,",
          "offset": 3854,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "thus uniting most of the lands south of",
          "offset": 3857,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "64:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Humber for the first time in",
          "offset": 3860,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "64:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "history.",
          "offset": 3862,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "All that remained now was the kingdom of",
          "offset": 3864,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "64:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "North Umbrea.",
          "offset": 3868,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "64:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though just as Edward was annexing",
          "offset": 3872,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "64:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mercia into his ever growing realm, the",
          "offset": 3874,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "64:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "Dublin Norse, members of the soontobe",
          "offset": 3877,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "64:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "feared EVA dynasty of Ireland annexed",
          "offset": 3880,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "64:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yorvik in a lightning attack.",
          "offset": 3884,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "64:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "England had been made, but just as",
          "offset": 3889,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "64:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] easily could be broken again.",
          "offset": 3893,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "64:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "The idea of a united angle land or",
          "offset": 3905,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "England comprised of all the territories",
          "offset": 3909,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the old Anglo-Saxon kingdoms was",
          "offset": 3912,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "first conceived of and forged by Alfred",
          "offset": 3915,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "65:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Wessix [music] in the fires of Viking",
          "offset": 3917,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "invasion.",
          "offset": 3920,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "65:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was made into a reality, however, by",
          "offset": 3924,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "the reconquests of his children Edward",
          "offset": 3927,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Ethelfled.",
          "offset": 3930,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "65:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet, it was his grandson Athlan who took",
          "offset": 3934,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "65:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "the idea even further in extending his",
          "offset": 3938,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "65:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "overlordship for a time over all of the",
          "offset": 3942,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "other kingdoms of Britain,",
          "offset": 3945,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "65:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "forging the very first English Empire.",
          "offset": 3948,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 3957,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "65:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet just like his father before him,",
          "offset": 3960,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "65:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "Athlan's succession had been a disputed",
          "offset": 3963,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "66:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "one.",
          "offset": 3966,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "66:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Seen by many [music] as illegitimate,",
          "offset": 3971,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "66:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "he came to the throne amidst dynastic",
          "offset": 3974,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "66:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "turmoil that looked set to destroy the",
          "offset": 3977,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "66:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdom before it even got started.",
          "offset": 3980,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "66:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet, [music] he ended his reign, having",
          "offset": 3984,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "66:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "triumphed over every other kingdom of",
          "offset": 3986,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "66:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain, defeating one of the largest",
          "offset": 3989,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "66:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Viking invasion fleets ever assembled.",
          "offset": 3992,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "66:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "as truly the first and one of [music]",
          "offset": 3999,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "66:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "the greatest English kings in history.",
          "offset": 4002,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "66:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "Athlan [music] had been born in 894",
          "offset": 4014,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "66:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "during the reign of his grandfather",
          "offset": 4017,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "66:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Alfred [music]",
          "offset": 4019,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "66:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "who was said to have taken a liking to",
          "offset": 4021,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "the boy apparently giving him his",
          "offset": 4023,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "blessing to succeed after his son",
          "offset": 4026,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Edward.",
          "offset": 4028,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "67:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though ultimately the West Saxon",
          "offset": 4031,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "67:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "political elite would have other ideas.",
          "offset": 4033,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "Athalan's mother, referred to in the",
          "offset": 4039,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "67:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "sources as a mere concubine, died soon",
          "offset": 4041,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "67:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "after his birth, and Edward married",
          "offset": 4044,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "again.",
          "offset": 4047,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "in total having more than 14 other",
          "offset": 4049,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "67:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "children by another two wives and",
          "offset": 4052,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "67:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "pushing Athlan far back in the line of",
          "offset": 4055,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "67:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "succession.",
          "offset": 4058,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "67:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 918, Athlan was a trained warrior in",
          "offset": 4063,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "67:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "his mid20s,",
          "offset": 4067,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "having fought a long series of campaigns",
          "offset": 4069,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "at his Art Ethelfled's [music] side to",
          "offset": 4071,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "reclaim the five burers of the Danlaw",
          "offset": 4074,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "67:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "for Mercia.",
          "offset": 4076,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "67:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Upon Ethel Fled's death that summer,",
          "offset": 4081,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "however, and without a male heir to",
          "offset": 4083,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "68:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "succeed her, Edward rode north to claim",
          "offset": 4086,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "68:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "direct control over Mercuria for the",
          "offset": 4089,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "68:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "first time,",
          "offset": 4091,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "thus extending West Saxon control over",
          "offset": 4093,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "all of the lands where English was",
          "offset": 4096,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "68:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "spoken south of the river Humber.",
          "offset": 4098,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "Over the [music] next six years, Edward",
          "offset": 4105,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "worked hard to consolidate his new",
          "offset": 4108,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "68:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "realm,",
          "offset": 4110,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "68:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "at times claiming overlordship over the",
          "offset": 4112,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "five Welsh kingdoms and the Vikings",
          "offset": 4114,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "68:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] of North Umbrea with varying",
          "offset": 4117,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "68:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "degrees of legitimacy.",
          "offset": 4119,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "68:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just before his death in 924, however,",
          "offset": 4124,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "68:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "everything began to go wrong.",
          "offset": 4128,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "68:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "The Mercians seem to have risen up in",
          "offset": 4131,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "68:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "rebellion against West [music] Saxon",
          "offset": 4134,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "68:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "control.",
          "offset": 4136,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "68:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "While to the north, King Citri of Yorvik",
          "offset": 4138,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "68:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "seems to have taken the opportunity to",
          "offset": 4142,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "extend his influence southwards into the",
          "offset": 4144,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "69:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "five burers.",
          "offset": 4147,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "69:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just weeks later, Edward died.",
          "offset": 4151,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "69:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Closely followed by his son and heir,",
          "offset": 4156,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Elfwir.",
          "offset": 4158,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "69:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "Rather than [music] submit to the West",
          "offset": 4163,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Saxons, the Mercian nobility instead",
          "offset": 4164,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "69:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "opted to choose the already veteran war",
          "offset": 4168,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "69:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "leader Athlan [music] as their king.",
          "offset": 4171,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "69:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "already 30 years old and a tried and",
          "offset": 4174,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "69:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "tested ruler.",
          "offset": 4177,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "69:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "For close to a year, conflict raged",
          "offset": 4182,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "69:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "amongst the West Saxon political elite",
          "offset": 4185,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "and that of Mercia,",
          "offset": 4188,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "69:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "threatening to tear the Anglo-Saxon",
          "offset": 4190,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "69:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "realm back into its two constituent",
          "offset": 4192,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "parts.",
          "offset": 4194,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "69:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "Citri, meanwhile, [music] used the",
          "offset": 4197,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "69:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "opportunity to further expand his",
          "offset": 4199,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "69:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "influence southwards.",
          "offset": 4202,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "70:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "Finally, by the summer of 925,",
          "offset": 4209,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "70:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "the West Saxons also agreed to accept",
          "offset": 4212,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "70:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Athalan as their king,",
          "offset": 4215,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "70:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "apparently providing he agree not",
          "offset": 4219,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "70:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] to marry nor have any heirs.",
          "offset": 4221,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "70:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "Athlan in essence was to be a caretaker",
          "offset": 4225,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "70:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "king for his West Saxon half brothers.",
          "offset": 4228,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "70:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ever the able politician, when Athlan",
          "offset": 4237,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "70:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "was finally crowned in September, the",
          "offset": 4240,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "70:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "ceremony took place not [music] in the",
          "offset": 4243,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "70:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "West Saxon capital of Winchester,",
          "offset": 4245,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "70:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "nor the Mercian capital of Tamworth,",
          "offset": 4248,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "70:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "but at Kingston upon Tames on the",
          "offset": 4251,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "70:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "borderlands between the two kingdoms.",
          "offset": 4255,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "70:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "In the first royal coronation in English",
          "offset": 4261,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "71:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "history, he was [music] crowned as king",
          "offset": 4263,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "71:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the Anglo-Saxons.",
          "offset": 4266,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "71:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "Just months later, Citri of Yorvvic,",
          "offset": 4272,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "71:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "very aware of Athlan's reputation, also",
          "offset": 4275,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "71:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "submitted at Tamworth,",
          "offset": 4278,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "71:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "accepting the king's sister in marriage",
          "offset": 4282,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "71:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "and agreeing to baptism.",
          "offset": 4284,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "71:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "This was the first of many consiliatory",
          "offset": 4291,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "71:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "efforts against the Danes of Eastern",
          "offset": 4293,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "71:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "England,",
          "offset": 4295,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "71:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "increasing numbers of whom would be",
          "offset": 4297,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "71:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "recruited into Athlan's ever growing",
          "offset": 4299,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "71:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "army over the coming years.",
          "offset": 4302,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "71:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "Upon Citri's death in the next year,",
          "offset": 4308,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "71:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "however, his kinsman Guthri's claim to",
          "offset": 4311,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "71:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "the throne were revoked by Athlan.",
          "offset": 4314,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "71:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "marched north to annex the kingdom,",
          "offset": 4317,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "71:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "forcing Guthri and his family back",
          "offset": 4321,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "72:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "across the Irish Sea to Dublin.",
          "offset": 4323,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "72:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "For the first time in history, a",
          "offset": 4330,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "72:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "southern ruler sat [music] on the North",
          "offset": 4332,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "72:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Umbrean throne.",
          "offset": 4334,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "72:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet, Athlan didn't stop there. traveling",
          "offset": 4339,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "72:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "further north to Bambborra to receive",
          "offset": 4342,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "72:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "the submission of the English Bernissian",
          "offset": 4345,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "72:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "lords whose rule had survived there",
          "offset": 4347,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "72:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "largely intact throughout the long years",
          "offset": 4350,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "72:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Viking occupation.",
          "offset": 4352,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "72:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "His next stop was Cumbria",
          "offset": 4359,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "72:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "where faced with the overwhelming",
          "offset": 4363,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "72:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "strength [music] of the English army,",
          "offset": 4365,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "72:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Scottish king Constantine II and the",
          "offset": 4367,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "72:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "brethonic king of Strathclide Owen both",
          "offset": 4370,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "72:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "acknowledged him as their overlord.",
          "offset": 4374,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "72:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "The five Welsh kings also gave him their",
          "offset": 4378,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "72:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "submission, making Athlan a true king of",
          "offset": 4381,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "73:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "kings",
          "offset": 4385,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "73:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "and the most powerful ruler in Britain",
          "offset": 4387,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "73:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "since the Romans.",
          "offset": 4390,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "73:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "For the next six years, Athlan",
          "offset": 4398,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "consolidated his [music] realm,",
          "offset": 4401,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "instigating legal reforms, promoting",
          "offset": 4404,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "education and religious matters, and",
          "offset": 4406,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "73:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "lavishing gifts upon his new subjects to",
          "offset": 4409,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "73:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "ensure their continued loyalty.",
          "offset": 4412,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "73:31"
        },
        {
          "text": "By 933, however, things started to go",
          "offset": 4421,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "73:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "wrong. His brother and successor Edwin",
          "offset": 4425,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "73:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "died in mysterious circumstances whilst",
          "offset": 4429,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "73:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "apparently fleeing to the continent.",
          "offset": 4432,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "73:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "Some say he [music] was murdered.",
          "offset": 4434,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "73:54"
        },
        {
          "text": "And then Constantine threw off the",
          "offset": 4438,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "73:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "shackles of English overlordship,",
          "offset": 4441,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "declaring his independence from the",
          "offset": 4444,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "south once more.",
          "offset": 4446,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 4449,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "Athalan's response was overwhelming.",
          "offset": 4451,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "heading north by land and sea with the",
          "offset": 4455,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "combined armies of Mercuria, Wessex, and",
          "offset": 4457,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Danlaw along with several Welsh",
          "offset": 4461,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "rulers in order to make an example of",
          "offset": 4463,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "the rebellious king.",
          "offset": 4466,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "74:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was a truly multithnic force, notably",
          "offset": 4469,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "74:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "including 13 Danish along with their",
          "offset": 4473,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "retinues.",
          "offset": 4476,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "74:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "[screaming]",
          "offset": 4479,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "74:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "Once they reached Constantine's lands,",
          "offset": 4480,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Athlan's army ravaged as far north as",
          "offset": 4483,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "74:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cathnes",
          "offset": 4486,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "74:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "in a shock and awe campaign,",
          "offset": 4487,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "forcing Constantine to submit and",
          "offset": 4490,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "afterwards to accompany the English king",
          "offset": 4493,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "74:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "back south to [music] Wessex to do",
          "offset": 4495,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "74:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "homage at his court.",
          "offset": 4498,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "74:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Athlan continued his attempts to ensure",
          "offset": 4504,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "75:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "loyalty by lavishing gifts upon the",
          "offset": 4507,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "75:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "leadership of his recently acquired",
          "offset": 4509,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "75:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "lands.",
          "offset": 4512,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "75:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Despite his [music] best efforts,",
          "offset": 4516,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "75:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "however, descent continued to grow",
          "offset": 4517,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "75:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "not only in Scotland but in Wales,",
          "offset": 4522,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "75:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "Cornwall, Cumbria and North Umbrea.",
          "offset": 4525,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "75:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "A clear line had been drawn between the",
          "offset": 4530,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "75:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "English",
          "offset": 4533,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "75:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "and everyone else,",
          "offset": 4535,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "75:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "and a reckoning was on the way.",
          "offset": 4538,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "75:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "There was another power on the rise,",
          "offset": 4544,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "75:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "too, and it came on long boats from",
          "offset": 4546,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "75:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "across the sea.",
          "offset": 4550,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "75:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "King Citri of York just so happened to",
          "offset": 4558,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "75:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "have been a member of the other all",
          "offset": 4561,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "76:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "powerful dynasty in Britain during this",
          "offset": 4563,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "76:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "time. The sons of Ivar from Dublin.",
          "offset": 4566,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "76:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Norse Irish sea kings allegedly claiming",
          "offset": 4573,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "76:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "descent from the feared warlord Ivar the",
          "offset": 4576,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "76:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "Boneless who had ravaged Britain during",
          "offset": 4579,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "76:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "the 860s and 870s.",
          "offset": 4582,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "76:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "When Athlan rejected the Norse from",
          "offset": 4588,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "76:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "North Umbrea in 927 following Citri's",
          "offset": 4590,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "76:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "death, they swore to return.",
          "offset": 4593,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "76:33"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though it wouldn't be Guthri who would",
          "offset": 4598,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "76:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "be back, but his son Olaf,",
          "offset": 4601,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "76:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "successfully outmaneuvering the other",
          "offset": 4609,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "76:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "claimants to the throne of Dublin upon",
          "offset": 4611,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "76:51"
        },
        {
          "text": "his father's death in 934,",
          "offset": 4614,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "76:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "Olaf Guthritson, a ruthless and",
          "offset": 4616,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "76:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "energetic young Viking king, immediately",
          "offset": 4619,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "76:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "put in motion his plan to reclaim the",
          "offset": 4623,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "77:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "family territories in Britain.",
          "offset": 4625,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "77:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "The first item on the agenda was to",
          "offset": 4630,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "77:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "bring the other long forts of Ireland",
          "offset": 4632,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "77:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "under his heel. In particular, the most",
          "offset": 4634,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "77:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "powerful of the bunch, Limmerick.",
          "offset": 4638,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "77:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "In early 937,",
          "offset": 4644,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "77:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "after consolidating his rule in Dublin,",
          "offset": 4646,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "77:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Olaf led his warriors in a lightning",
          "offset": 4650,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "77:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "raid upon Limmerch and its king, also",
          "offset": 4652,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "77:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "named Olaf.",
          "offset": 4656,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "77:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "After a fierce battle, the king of",
          "offset": 4660,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "77:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "Limmerick was either forced into",
          "offset": 4662,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "77:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "submission or imprisoned.",
          "offset": 4664,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "77:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "But most importantly, the Limmerick men",
          "offset": 4668,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "77:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "were brought on side.",
          "offset": 4671,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "77:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "In one fell swoop, Olaf Guthritson had",
          "offset": 4677,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "77:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "succeeded in uniting all of the Norsemen",
          "offset": 4680,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "77:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "and Danes in Ireland into a single",
          "offset": 4682,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "78:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "mighty navy. The largest yet seen in the",
          "offset": 4686,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "78:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "British Isles.",
          "offset": 4689,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "78:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "It was an unprecedented feat, as many as",
          "offset": 4692,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "78:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "615 ships. According to one source,",
          "offset": 4695,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "78:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Olaf had himself grandly declared as",
          "offset": 4702,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "78:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "king of all the Norsemen and Danes in",
          "offset": 4706,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "78:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ireland.",
          "offset": 4708,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "78:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yet, he didn't stop there.",
          "offset": 4710,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "78:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "The sons of Ivar had not forgotten their",
          "offset": 4716,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "78:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "defeat at the hands of the English.",
          "offset": 4719,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "78:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "And just like Athlan, Olaf Guthritzen",
          "offset": 4724,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "78:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "was good at making allies.",
          "offset": 4728,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "78:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "Across the sea in Scotland, Constantine",
          "offset": 4736,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "78:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "II, who had fought tooth and nail for",
          "offset": 4739,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "78:59"
        },
        {
          "text": "his independence for decades against",
          "offset": 4742,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "79:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "waves of Viking invaders, was seething",
          "offset": 4745,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "79:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "after being forced to submit to Athlan's",
          "offset": 4749,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "79:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "overlordship.",
          "offset": 4752,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "79:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "as was the king of the independent",
          "offset": 4756,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "79:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdom of Strathclyde, Owen, the",
          "offset": 4758,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "79:18"
        },
        {
          "text": "successor state to the ancient kingdom",
          "offset": 4762,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "79:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "of altcloot.",
          "offset": 4764,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "79:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though it remains unclear who first",
          "offset": 4768,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "79:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "broached the alliance, by mid 937, the",
          "offset": 4771,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "79:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "two kings decided to make common cause",
          "offset": 4774,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "79:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "with the sons of Ivar against England.",
          "offset": 4778,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "79:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "secretly plotting an invasion of North",
          "offset": 4785,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "79:45"
        },
        {
          "text": "Umbrea.",
          "offset": 4788,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "79:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "According to some sources, the alliance",
          "offset": 4793,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "79:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "was even sealed by the marriage of Olaf",
          "offset": 4796,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "79:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "to a daughter of Constantine.",
          "offset": 4798,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "79:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Late in the summer of 937,",
          "offset": 4809,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "80:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "just after the usual campaigning season",
          "offset": 4812,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "80:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "had ended,",
          "offset": 4814,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "80:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Olaf loaded up his entire navy,",
          "offset": 4816,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "80:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "bolstered by all of the other long forts",
          "offset": 4821,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "80:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] of Ireland and men from all over",
          "offset": 4823,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "80:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "the Scottish Isles and man,",
          "offset": 4826,
          "duration": 9,
          "formattedTime": "80:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "and together they headed to Britain.",
          "offset": 4829,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "80:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "There they linked up [music] with not",
          "offset": 4836,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "80:36"
        },
        {
          "text": "only Constantine and Owen's armies, but",
          "offset": 4838,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "80:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "also men from Wales, Cumbria, and",
          "offset": 4841,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "80:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "possibly even Cornwall. [music]",
          "offset": 4845,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "80:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "The last vestigages of pre- Anglo-Saxon",
          "offset": 4850,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "80:49"
        },
        {
          "text": "Britain.",
          "offset": 4852,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "80:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "Debate still rages as to the exact route",
          "offset": 4856,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "80:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "which Olaf took or even the exact",
          "offset": 4859,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "80:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "location of the battle.",
          "offset": 4862,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "81:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "Some historians think he rounded the",
          "offset": 4866,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "81:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "Scottish mainland to make landfall near",
          "offset": 4868,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "81:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] York",
          "offset": 4870,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "81:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "where he could count on support from",
          "offset": 4874,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "81:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "many of the local fains of North Umbrea.",
          "offset": 4875,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "81:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "Others think he took the shortest route",
          "offset": 4880,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "81:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "and landed on the Murzy estie where he",
          "offset": 4883,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "81:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "met up with the Allied army.",
          "offset": 4885,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "81:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 4889,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "81:28"
        },
        {
          "text": "All that is known for certain is that",
          "offset": 4890,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "81:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "the combined army assembled somewhere",
          "offset": 4892,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "81:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] in North Umbrea",
          "offset": 4894,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "81:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "where they linked up with significant",
          "offset": 4897,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "81:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "elements from the Dan law and together",
          "offset": 4899,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "81:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "began to ravage the countryside.",
          "offset": 4902,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "81:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "When news reached Athlan in the early",
          "offset": 4910,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "81:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "autumn of the implosion of his empire so",
          "offset": 4913,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "81:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "late in [music] the usual campaigning",
          "offset": 4917,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "81:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "season,",
          "offset": 4918,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "81:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "he is said to have entered a state of",
          "offset": 4922,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "deep contemplation.",
          "offset": 4924,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "82:04"
        },
        {
          "text": "An extremely pious king, according to",
          "offset": 4927,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "tradition, he prayed for his soul at a",
          "offset": 4930,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "local church, knowing the terrible",
          "offset": 4932,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "82:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "bloodbath that would inevitably follow.",
          "offset": 4935,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "before calling his banners and heading",
          "offset": 4940,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "north.",
          "offset": 4943,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "82:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 4945,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "82:25"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 4950,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "82:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "The most important yet little known",
          "offset": 4952,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "battle in English history was about to",
          "offset": 4954,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "82:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "be fought.",
          "offset": 4957,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "82:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "According to the historian Ethelweird,",
          "offset": 4961,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "writing a generation after the battle,",
          "offset": 4964,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:43"
        },
        {
          "text": "it was still known by the common people",
          "offset": 4966,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "82:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "simply as the Great War.",
          "offset": 4969,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "Unfortunately, possibly as a result of",
          "offset": 4975,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "82:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "Athlan's apparent unpopity amongst the",
          "offset": 4978,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "82:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "political elite [music] of Wessix during",
          "offset": 4981,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "83:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "his reign, very little evidence remains",
          "offset": 4982,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "83:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the battle itself.",
          "offset": 4985,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "83:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "What we do know derives mostly [music]",
          "offset": 4990,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "83:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "from a single heroic poem from the",
          "offset": 4992,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "83:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Anglo-Saxon chronicle.",
          "offset": 4994,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "83:13"
        },
        {
          "text": "It seems that Athlan took his time to",
          "offset": 5000,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "83:20"
        },
        {
          "text": "prepare,",
          "offset": 5003,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "83:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "gathering together as many men as he",
          "offset": 5004,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "83:24"
        },
        {
          "text": "could from all of his territories,",
          "offset": 5006,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "83:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "most notably from his heartlands of",
          "offset": 5010,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "83:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "Mercia and Wessix,",
          "offset": 5012,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "83:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "but also from Kent, Essex, and large",
          "offset": 5014,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "83:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "contingents of Anglo Danes from the",
          "offset": 5018,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "83:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music] east of the country.",
          "offset": 5020,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "83:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "Together they headed north to a fortress",
          "offset": 5026,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "83:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "named Brunanand Burr where the English",
          "offset": 5030,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "83:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "army is said to have attacked the Allied",
          "offset": 5033,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "83:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "forces in a head-long frontal assault.",
          "offset": 5035,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "83:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "Both armies would have been made up",
          "offset": 5041,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "almost entirely of foot soldiers",
          "offset": 5042,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "standing side by side in a tight",
          "offset": 5045,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "84:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "formation [music] of interlocking",
          "offset": 5047,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "shields known as a shield wall.",
          "offset": 5049,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:08"
        },
        {
          "text": "A half-remembered battle [music] tactic",
          "offset": 5052,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "once used by Roman legionaries",
          "offset": 5054,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "84:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "and at this time a mainstay of combat",
          "offset": 5057,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "until the advent of Norman cavalry over",
          "offset": 5063,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "84:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "a century later.",
          "offset": 5066,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "84:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "Due to the sheer lack of sources on this",
          "offset": 5073,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "84:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "battle, the numbers involved are",
          "offset": 5075,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "difficult to estimate.",
          "offset": 5077,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "84:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though due to the perceived importance",
          "offset": 5080,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "84:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "of Brunenberg and the sheer variety of",
          "offset": 5082,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:41"
        },
        {
          "text": "different groups involved, it seems",
          "offset": 5084,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "84:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "probable that many thousands took part",
          "offset": 5086,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "84:46"
        },
        {
          "text": "on either side.",
          "offset": 5089,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "84:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "At daybreak, both armies advanced.",
          "offset": 5096,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "84:56"
        },
        {
          "text": "Seasoned career soldiers in the front",
          "offset": 5101,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:01"
        },
        {
          "text": "ranks hurling insults, spears, and",
          "offset": 5103,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "85:02"
        },
        {
          "text": "challenges",
          "offset": 5106,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "85:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "as the slow advance gradually churned",
          "offset": 5107,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "forwards.",
          "offset": 5110,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "85:09"
        },
        {
          "text": "Finally, the shield walls sickeningly",
          "offset": 5114,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "crunched into one another. For hours on",
          "offset": 5117,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:16"
        },
        {
          "text": "end, each side pushing on the other in a",
          "offset": 5120,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "85:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "tireless bloodbath.",
          "offset": 5122,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "85:22"
        },
        {
          "text": "Both armies seemed matched at first, and",
          "offset": 5129,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "85:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "more and more casualties mounted up on",
          "offset": 5133,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "85:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "either side,",
          "offset": 5135,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "85:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "including two of Athlan's cousins and",
          "offset": 5139,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:39"
        },
        {
          "text": "countless Thains [music] and Yles on the",
          "offset": 5142,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "other side.",
          "offset": 5144,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "85:44"
        },
        {
          "text": "Finally, by the late afternoon, the",
          "offset": 5148,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:48"
        },
        {
          "text": "better coordinated English army, already",
          "offset": 5151,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "85:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "well-versed in fighting together and not",
          "offset": 5154,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "85:53"
        },
        {
          "text": "made up [music] for many different areas",
          "offset": 5156,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "85:55"
        },
        {
          "text": "like the opposing army, succeeded in",
          "offset": 5158,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "85:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "making a dent in the Allied line.",
          "offset": 5160,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "86:00"
        },
        {
          "text": "A break in the shield wall was all that",
          "offset": 5165,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "86:05"
        },
        {
          "text": "was needed.",
          "offset": 5167,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "86:07"
        },
        {
          "text": "And after several more hours of long",
          "offset": 5171,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "86:10"
        },
        {
          "text": "grueling attrition, the English, ever",
          "offset": 5173,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "86:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "spurred on by Athlan and his younger",
          "offset": 5175,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "86:15"
        },
        {
          "text": "brother and heir, Edmund,",
          "offset": 5177,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "86:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "succeeded in severing the less",
          "offset": 5180,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "86:19"
        },
        {
          "text": "coordinated allies into several groups,",
          "offset": 5182,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "86:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "forcing Olaf's men to fall back to their",
          "offset": 5188,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "86:27"
        },
        {
          "text": "ships in uncoordinated retreat.",
          "offset": 5191,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "86:30"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 5195,
          "duration": 2,
          "formattedTime": "86:34"
        },
        {
          "text": "Constantine abandoned the field, too.",
          "offset": 5197,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "86:37"
        },
        {
          "text": "fleeing back north to the relative",
          "offset": 5200,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "86:40"
        },
        {
          "text": "safety of [music] Cumbria.",
          "offset": 5202,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "86:42"
        },
        {
          "text": "Both were swiftly followed by vengeful",
          "offset": 5208,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "86:47"
        },
        {
          "text": "Englishmen who cut [music] down swavthes",
          "offset": 5210,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "86:50"
        },
        {
          "text": "of fleeing Norsemen and Scots.",
          "offset": 5213,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "86:52"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 5217,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "86:57"
        },
        {
          "text": "Though ultimately both kings escaped,",
          "offset": 5219,
          "duration": 8,
          "formattedTime": "86:58"
        },
        {
          "text": "Owen's fate [music] remains unknown. He",
          "offset": 5224,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "87:03"
        },
        {
          "text": "may have died in the fighting.",
          "offset": 5226,
          "duration": 4,
          "formattedTime": "87:06"
        },
        {
          "text": "[music]",
          "offset": 5232,
          "duration": 3,
          "formattedTime": "87:11"
        },
        {
          "text": "Having secured the survival of his",
          "offset": 5233,
          "duration": 5,
          "formattedTime": "87:12"
        },
        {
          "text": "kingdom, but at great cost to his",
          "offset": 5235,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:14"
        },
        {
          "text": "Christian soul, Athlan ruled for another",
          "offset": 5238,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:17"
        },
        {
          "text": "year and a half after Brunenber",
          "offset": 5241,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:21"
        },
        {
          "text": "before he died exhausted after a",
          "offset": 5244,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:23"
        },
        {
          "text": "lifetime of war.",
          "offset": 5247,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:26"
        },
        {
          "text": "True to his word, he never married and",
          "offset": 5250,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:29"
        },
        {
          "text": "had no heirs and was succeeded [music]",
          "offset": 5253,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:32"
        },
        {
          "text": "by his younger brother Edmund.",
          "offset": 5256,
          "duration": 7,
          "formattedTime": "87:35"
        },
        {
          "text": "still a teenager at the time,",
          "offset": 5259,
          "duration": 6,
          "formattedTime": "87:38"
        },
        {
          "text": "though one who had stood in the shield",
