      "url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EIIFRXXFjVs",
      "description": "The Amazon is one of the most fascinating regions in the world for archaeology. Over the last few decades a series of groundbreaking discoveries here have finally proved to the world the region had been home to many advanced societies. Dare we say it, civilisations. Join me for this two hour deep dive into these fascinating societies.\n\nCome on an epic Anatolian adventure this September !\nhttps://www.thecommunitygarden.org/tours/p/ancientanatolia\n\nLost Cities In The Amazon \n22:32: Part 1 - New World  \n49:23: Part 2 - Green Desert Myth \n1:09:49: Part 3 - Beyond The Great River  \n1:45:03: Part 4 - Finding Z\n\nPete Kelly here. Narrator / writer / researcher / editor behind the channel. This episode was a labour of love. I started writing it back in 2020. I'm glad I held off on releasing it as vast amounts of new data has been released just in the years since. Notably with the incredible discoveries of the Upano Valley just released in 2024. I was lucky enough to visit the Amazon in 2023 where I researched, wrote and filmed much of the footage for the episode. I've been chipping away at it since finishing the script last year and have just spent a solid month finally editing it. Glad to have it finally released! \n\nReferences :\n\nJournal Articles - \nAmazonian Dark Earths in Western Amazonia? - Manuel Arroyo-Kalin (2014) \nThe Andes-Amazonia divide: Myth & Reality - Pearce, Beresford-Jones & Heggarty  \nRewriting the late Pre-European History of Amazonia - William M. Denevan (2012)\nGeolocation of unpublished archaeological sites in the Peruvian Amazon  - Coomes et al (2021)\nChanging Perspective on the archeology of the Upper Amazon - Clasby & Nesbitt  \nTropical Garden Cities: archaeology and memory In the southern Amazon - Michael Heckenberger  \nPre-Colombian Urbanism, Anthropogenic Landscapes and the future of the amazon - Michael Heckenberger et al \nKuhikugu : Largest Pre-Columbian Tree Settlement -- Xingu region of the Amazon Rainforest\n\nBooks - \nThe Ecology of Power: Culture, Place & Personhood in the Southern Amazon, AD 1000-2000 (2003) \nRiver of Darkness - Buddy Levy (2011)  The River of Doubt - Candice Millard (2005)\nMoundbuilders of the Amazon: Geophysical archaeology on Marajo Island, Brazil - Anna Roosevelt \nAmazonian Indians: From Prehistory to the Present - Anna Roosevelt \nExplorers of the Amazon - Anthony Smith \nThe Lost city of Z- David Grann \nLand Without Evil - Utopian Adventures Across The South American Watershed \nEbenezer Howard - Garden Cities of Tomorrow \n1491- the Americas before Columbus - Charles C Mann \nRed Gold , the conquest of the Brazilian Indians - Hemming \nExploration Fawcett- Col PH Fawcett \nConquistador - Buddy Levy \nPeople of the Rainforest - John Hemming  \nSpirit of the Amazon - Sue & Patrick Cunningham \nPre-Colombian Art - Esther Pasztory\nTree Of Rivers: The Story of the Amazon - John Hemming\n\nJoin Pete in Peru next April/May \n- Details very soon\n\nOriginal music composed by Joss Edwards & Brodie Marshall \nOriginal art by Ettore Mazza \nWritten, filmed, narrated, edited by Pete Kelly\n\nCheck out my new podcast History Time: Unearthed - \nhttps://youtube.com/playlist?list=PLWUs3Loz3TsnpJPvqVZ28re3t1dQ_ypbS&si=h3_z_LT6Au2il8-M",
